hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16076","(16070) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Shādhakhī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from al-Awzāʿī, who said: Ḥiṣn narrated to me: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me: ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Those who have killed should restrain one after another"
"16077","(16071) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, from Abī ʿUbayd, who said regarding the hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ): \Let the people of the slain restrain the nearest after the nearest"
"16078","(16072) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: \A man found another man with his wife and killed her. The matter was raised to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). Some of her brothers were present"
"16079","(16073) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to me, from Sulaymān al-Aʿmash, from Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhanī: \A man killed her (his wife). Three of her brothers sought retaliation against him before ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). One of them pardoned"
"16080","(16074) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muḥammad, i.e. ibn al-Ḥasan, informed us: Abū Ḥanīfah narrated to us, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī: \ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a man who had committed deliberate murder"
"16081","(16075) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Jahm ibn Hārūn al-Simmariyy narrated to us: Hawdha ibn Khalīfa al-Bakrāwiyy narrated to us: ʿAwf narrated from Ḥamza Abī ʿUmar al-ʿĀidhiyy.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us — and the wording is his — Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābiyy narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us: ʿAwf al-Aʿrābiyy narrated — I think from Ḥamza al-ʿĀidhiyy — from ʿAlqama ibn Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr al-Ḥaḍramiyy, from his father, who said: The killer was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the guardian of the slain accompanied him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Will you pardon?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Will you accept the blood-money?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Will you kill?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then take him.\"" When he had gone"
"16082","(16076) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād: Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adami narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Jamīl narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever kills intentionally shall be handed over to the guardian of the slain; if he wishes"
"16083","(16077) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿba narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtiyy narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Shuʿba narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from Abū Qilāba, from Abī al-Ashʿath, from Shaddād ibn Aws, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Two qualities I heard from the Prophet ﷺ: Verily"
"16084","(16078) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabāriyy narrated to us: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhiyy narrated to us, saying: I heard Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb say: I asked Yaḥyya ibn Ḥammād about the ḥadīth of Hunayy ibn Nuwayra, and he said: Abū ʿAwāna narrated to us from Mughīra, from Ibrāhīm, from Hunayy ibn Nuwayra, from ʿAlqama, from ʿAbd Allāh, from the Prophet ﷺ: \The most forgiving of people in killing are the people of faith.\""\n\nAnd Hushaym narrated it from Mughīra"
"16085","(16079) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us: Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, who said regarding a man who apprehends the killer of his brother: \Is there any sin upon him before Allah"
"16086","(16080) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnaziyy narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥa, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding His statement {And whoever transgresses against you, then transgress against him in the like of that which he transgressed against you} and His statement {And whoever defends himself after his being wronged — against them there is no cause of blame} and His statement {And if you punish, then punish with the like of that wherewith you were punished} and His statement {And the recompense of an evil deed is an evil deed the like thereof}.\n\nAnd the like of this was revealed in Makka, when the Muslims were few and had no authority to overpower the polytheists. The polytheists used to assail them with abuse and harm. So Allah commanded the Muslims, if any of them were to be requited, that they should requite with the like of what had been done to them, or they should be patient and pardon, and that is better. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated to Madīna and Allah strengthened his authority, He commanded the Muslims to refer their grievances to their authority and not to transgress against one another as the people of Jāhiliyya did. So He said {And whoever is killed wrongfully, We have given his heir authority, but let him not exceed bounds in the killing; verily, he shall be supported}. He says: The authority (sulṭān) shall support him until he obtains justice from his oppressor. And whoever takes vengeance for himself without the authority is a transgressor who has exceeded bounds, having acted with the zeal of Jāhiliyya and not being content with the judgment of Allah. [Weak]"
"16087","(16081) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiya narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān, from Jābir, from al-Ḥakam, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote: \Let no one lead the prayer sitting after the Prophet ﷺ. The deliberate act of a child and his error are the same; in both there is expiation (kaffāra). And any woman who commits adultery with her slave"
"16088","(16082) And it is narrated from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, through a chain containing weakness. Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sābūr al-Daqīqiyy narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū Nuʿaym al-Ḥalabiyy ʿUbayd ibn Hishām narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Madaniyy narrated from Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḍumayra, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The deliberate act of the insane person and the child is considered error (khaṭaʾ).\"" [Very Weak]"""
"16089","(16083) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣriyy narrated to us: Mālik ibn Yaḥyā Abū Ghassān narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated from Ḥumayd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, who said: When ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, was stabbed, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar attacked al-Hurmuzān and killed him. It was said to ʿUmar: \ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar has killed al-Hurmuzān.\"" He said: \""Why did he kill him?\"" He said: \""He killed my father.\"" It was said: \""How is that?\"" He said: \""I saw him in private with my father"
"16090","(16084) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahāniyy narrated to us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābiyy narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarāniyy narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us: Qatāda narrated from Anas: That a young girl's head was crushed between two stones. It was said to her: \Who did this to you? Was it so-and-so? Was it so-and-so?\"" — until the Jew was named. She indicated with her head. The Jew was sent for and he confessed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded regarding him"
"16091","(16085) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū Sa'īd ibn al-A'rābī informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Za'farānī informed us — 'Affān informed us — Hammām informed us — Qatādah reported from Anas: that a group from the tribe of 'Uraynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \We have found Madīnah unbearable; our stomachs have swollen and our limbs have withered.\"" The Prophet ﷺ commanded them to join the camel-herdsman and to drink from the camels' urine and milk. So they joined the camel-herdsman and drank from the camels' urine and milk until their stomachs and complexions recovered. Then they killed the herdsman and drove off the camels. This reached the Prophet ﷺ"
"16092","(16086) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us — Abū 'Abdillāh ibn Abī al-Thalj informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Ghaylān informed us — Yazīd ibn Zuray' reported from Sulaymān al-Taymī from Anas: The Prophet ﷺ only branded their eyes with heated iron because they had branded the eyes of the herdsman.\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Faḍl ibn Sahl, from Yaḥyā ibn Ghaylān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq 'alayh)]"
"16093","(16087) Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us — Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — Abū 'Abdillāh Baḥr ibn Nāṣr ibn Sābiq al-Khawlānī informed us — 'Abdullāh ibn Wahb informed us — Mālik reported from 'Umar ibn Ḥusayn: that 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwān carried out a legal execution (qiṣāṣ) upon a man who had killed another with a staff, so he was killed with a staff. And it has been related from al-Sha'bī that he said: \If he mutilated him and then killed him"
"16094","(16088) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — 'Abdullāh ibn Ja'far informed us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Qays reported from Jābir al-Ju'fī from Abū 'Āzib from al-Nu'mān ibn Bashīr from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \There is no retaliatory punishment (qiṣāṣ) except with iron (i.e."
"16095","(16089) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — 'Alī ibn 'Umar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Nu'mānī informed us — al-Ḥusayn ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Jarjarā'ī informed us — Mūsā ibn Dāwūd reported from Mubārak from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no retaliatory punishment (qiṣāṣ) except with the sword.\""\n\nYūnus said: I asked al-Ḥasan"
"16096","(16090) And it was related from Mubārak ibn Faḍālah from al-Ḥasan from Abī Bakrah, raised (mawfūqan): Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us — Isḥāq ibn Ḥakīm informed us — Abū Umayyah al-Ṭarsūsī informed us — al-Walīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us — Mubārak ibn Faḍālah mentioned it.\n\n[Ḍa'īf]"
"16097","(16091) Abū Sa'd al-Mālinī informed us — Abū Aḥmad ibn 'Adī informed us — 'Umar ibn Sinān informed us — Ibn Muṣaffá informed us — Baqiyyah informed me — Sulaymān from al-Zuhrī from Abī Salamah from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no retaliatory punishment (qiṣāṣ) except with the sword.\""\n\nThus he said it from Abī Salamah.\n\n[Ḍa'īf]"""
"16098","(16092) And others related it from Baqiyyah, saying from Sa'īd ibn al-Musayyib: Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us — 'Abd al-Ghaffār al-Ḥimṣī informed us — al-Musayyib ibn Wāḍiḥ informed us — Baqiyyah from Abī Mu'ādh mentioned it.\n\nAnd thus 'Āmir ibn Sayyār related it from Abī Mu'ādh Sulaymān ibn Arqam. And it was related from Sulaymān from 'Abd al-Karīm ibn Abī al-Mukhāriq from Ibrāhīm from 'Alqamah from 'Abdullāh, raised (mawfūqan). And that was related from Mu'allā ibn Hilāl from Abī Isḥāq from 'Āṣim from 'Alī (may Allah be pleased with him), raised (mawfūqan). And this ḥadīth does not have a sound chain of transmission.\n\nMu'allā ibn Hilāl al-Ṭaḥḥān is abandoned (matrūk); Sulaymān ibn Arqam is weak (ḍa'īf); Mubārak ibn Faḍālah cannot be used as a proof; and Jābir ibn Yazīd al-Ju'fī is impugned (maṭ'ūn fīh).\n\n[Ḍa'īf]"
"16099","(16093) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr said — Abū al-'Abbāṣ al-Aṣamm informed us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us — 'Abdullāh ibn Wahb informed me — 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar reported from al-Naḍr: that a man stood before 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was upon the minbar and said, \O Commander of the Faithful"
"16100","(16094) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-'Anazī informed us — 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī informed us — 'Abdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ reported from Mu'āwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn 'Abbās (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the words of the Almighty: {"
"16101","(16095) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us from the original of his book; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us; Thābit narrated from Anas: that the sister of al-Rubayyiʿ, Umm Ḥārithah, wounded a person. They brought the dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Retribution"
"16102","(16096) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ʿAbdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr informed us; Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us; al-Anṣārī narrated to us; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: Al-Rubayyiʿ bint al-Naḍr struck a slave-girl and broke her incisor tooth. They sought pardon from them, but they refused. They offered them the blood-money, but they refused. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered retribution. Anas ibn al-Naḍr said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16103","(16097) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; Ḥajjāj narrated from ʿAṭāʾ that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāy — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \I do not enforce retribution for bones.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16104","(16098) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Hushaym narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh narrated to us; ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ narrated: A man broke another man's thigh. He brought the dispute to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him. He said: \O Commander of the Faithful"
"16105","(16099) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffāʾ al-Baghdādī informed us; Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ both said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madīnah. Ismāʿīl said in his hadith: They used to say: \Retribution is applicable among people for every fracture or wound"
"16106","(16100) Among them is what Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ṭalḥah; from Yaḥyā and ʿĪsā, the two sons of Ṭalḥah, or one of them, from Ṭalḥah: that the Prophet ﷺ said: \There is no retribution for a severe head wound (maʾmūmah).\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"16107","(16101) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Abū Yaʿlā informed us; Abū Kurayb narrated to us; Rishdīn ibn Saʿd narrated from Muʿādh ibn Muḥammad al-Anṣārī; from Ibn Ṣuhbān; from al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no retribution for a severe head wound (maʾmūmah)"
"16108","(16102) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Maḥmūd ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Faraj informed us; Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Dahtham ibn Qurʾān al-ʿIjlī; Nimrān ibn Jāriyah narrated to me from his father: that a man struck another man with the sword on his forearm and severed it at a point other than the joint. He sought redress from the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered the blood-money for him. He said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16109","(16103) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Makkī narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir; from Ṭāwūs, who mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ said: \There is no divorce before possession"
"16110","(16104) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us; Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī informed us; Sufyān narrated from Mukhāriq; from Ṭāriq: that Khālid enforced retribution for a slap. [Ḥasan]"
"16111","(16105) He said: And Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār that Ibn al-Zubayr carried out qiṣāṣ (retaliatory punishment) for a slap. Aḥmad said: \Thus it is in my book.\"""""
"16112","(16106) Al-Ḥumaydī narrated it from Sufyān from the nephew of ʿAmr, from ʿAmr — Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ibn Durustawayh informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nSufyān said in the narration of Yaḥyā: \Ibn Shubrumah and Ibn Abī Laylā differed concerning it. Ibn Shubrumah said: 'I would carry out qiṣāṣ.' And Ibn Abī Laylā said: 'I do not know; perhaps you are strict in this matter — a slap may be given that is less severe than the original"
"16113","(16107) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān and al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān — Abū al-Shaykh — informed us, ʿAbdān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ayyūb, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir: \That a man stabbed another man in his knee with a horn. He came to the Prophet (ﷺ) seeking qiṣāṣ. He said to him: 'Until it heals.' In the narration of Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ"
"16114","(16108) And ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it from Ismāʿīl. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Idrīs al-Anṣārī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, and he mentioned it, saying: \It was said to him: 'Until it heals.'\"""""
"16115","(16109) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \The two sons of Abī Shaybah erred in it"
"16116","(16110) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Abū Bakr informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from Ayyūb, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), similarly. And from Maʿmar, from Ayyūb, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \May Allah keep you far away — you have been hasty.\"""""
"16117","(16111) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn Shaybān al-Ramlī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, ʿAmr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah, who said: \A man stabbed another in his leg with a horn. He came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'Carry out qiṣāṣ for me.' He said: 'Wait.' Then he came again and said: 'Carry out qiṣāṣ for me.' He said: 'Wait.' Then he came a third time — or as many times as Allah willed — and said: 'Carry out qiṣāṣ for me.' So he carried out qiṣāṣ for him. The first man's leg healed"
"16118","(16112) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Ḥumayd ibn Kāsib narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Umawī narrated from Ibn Jurayj, ʿUthmān ibn al-Aswad, and Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir: \That a man was wounded and wished to seek qiṣāṣ. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade that retaliation be carried out against the assailant until the wounded person had healed.\""\n\nThis Umawī was alone in narrating it from them"
"16119","(16113) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us, Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khālid narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Ibn Lahīʿah, Abū al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Wounds shall be assessed"
"16120","(16114) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Mīkāl informed us, ʿAbdān al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, Abū Aḥmad narrated to us, Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Yaḥyā, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \A man's thigh was injured"
"16121","(16115) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Qāḍī Abū Ṭāhir narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us; al-Qawārīrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥumrān narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that a man stabbed another man in the knee with a horn, and he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, \O Messenger of Allah"
"16122","(16116) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʾAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh narrated from Abū Yaḥyā, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Whoever dies while a prescribed punishment (ḥadd) is being carried out upon him"
"16123","(16117) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Isfarāyīnī narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated from Khālid, from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah, from ʿUqbah ibn Aws, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon on the Day of the Conquest of Makkah and said the takbīr three times, then said: \There is no god but Allah alone. He fulfilled His promise"
"16124","(16118) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated from ʿAlī ibn Zayd, from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ) with the same meaning. He said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon on the Day of the Conquest or the Conquest of Makkah upon the steps of the House or the Kaʿbah.\""\n\n(T) Abū Dāwūd said: And Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it from ʿAlī ibn Zayd"
"16125","(16119) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Yazīd al-Baḥrānī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ and Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal both said: Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ narrated to us from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah, from Yaʿqūb ibn Aws — and Bishr said: he is the one whom Muḥammad used to call ʿUqbah ibn Aws — from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ): that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Makkah on the Day of the Conquest, he said: \There is no god but Allah alone…\"" And he mentioned the meaning of the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Zayd."""
"16126","(16120) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: \Yaʿqūb ibn Aws and ʿUqbah ibn Aws are one and the same person.\"" He said: And Yaḥyā was asked about this ḥadīth of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr. The man said"
"16127","(16121) And it was narrated in another place from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah al-Qurashī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The aggravated blood-money (al-diyyah al-mughallaẓah) consists of thirty ḥiqqah (full-grown she-camels)"
"16128","(16122) And Abū Ḥāzim informed us; Abū al-Faḍl informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khāld narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from Zayd ibn Thābit, that he used to say: \In the aggravated blood-money are thirty ḥiqqah"
"16129","(16123) He said: And Hushaym narrated to us; Mughīrah narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah and Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, that both of them said regarding the aggravated blood-money the same as Zayd ibn Thābit said. And it has been narrated from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān and Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with them both) something that partially contradicts it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16130","(16124) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us; Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from ʿAbd Rabbih, from Abū ʿIyāḍ, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān and Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with them both): \In the aggravated blood-money are forty jadʿah khalifah (pregnant four-year-old she-camels)"
"16131","(16125) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It has been narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, the same as we have stated regarding shibh al-ʿamd (quasi-intentional killing): thirty hiqqah (four-year-old she-camels), thirty jadhʿah (five-year-old she-camels), and forty khalifah (pregnant she-camels). And from another hadith: thirty-three hiqqah, thirty-three jadhʿah, and thirty-four thaniyyah (two-year-old she-camels) up to bāzil ʿāmihā (a camel in its ninth year), all of them being khalifah (pregnant).\n\n[Sound. Narrated from al-Shāfiʿī]"
"16132","(16126) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us with this latter narration that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Hannād informed us that Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Abū Isḥāq from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said regarding shibh al-ʿamd: In groups of three — thirty-three hiqqah, thirty-three jadhʿah, and thirty-four thaniyyah up to bāzil ʿāmihā, all of them being khalifah (pregnant).\n\n[Hasan through other chains]"
"16133","(16127) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Hannād informed us that Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Abū Isḥāq from ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad that ʿAbdullāh — that is, ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him — said regarding shibh al-ʿamd: twenty-five hiqqah, twenty-five jadhʿah, twenty-five banāt labūn (two-year-old she-camels), and twenty-five banāt makhāḍ (one-year-old she-camels).\n\n[Hasan through other chains]"
"16134","(16128) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik informed us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Sulaymān al-Taymī informed us from Abī Mijlaz from Abī ʿUbaydah from ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding shibh al-ʿamd: in four parts — a quarter banāt labūn, a quarter ḥiqqāq (plural of hiqqah), a quarter jidhāʿ (plural of jadhʿah), and a quarter thaniyyah up to bāzil ʿāmihā.\n\nThey have differed in this manner, and the statement of the one whose opinion accords with the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ mentioned in the preceding section is more deserving of being followed. And success is through Allah. [Hasan through other chains]"
"16135","(16129) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us that Abū al-Naḍr informed us that Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever kills intentionally is handed over to the guardians of the deceased; if they wish, they may execute him, and if they wish, they may accept the diyah (blood money), which is thirty hiqqah, thirty jadhʿah, and forty khalifah. That is the ʿaql (blood money) for intentional killing. And whatever they agree upon in settlement belongs to them. That is the intensification of the ʿaql. And indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The ʿaql for shibh al-ʿamd (quasi-intentional killing) is mughallaẓah (intensified) like the ʿaql for intentional killing, and its perpetrator is not executed. That is when Satan causes discord among people, resulting in a reckless act in a state of confusion, without enmity or bearing of arms.\n\n[Hasan through other chains]"
"16136","(16130) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Abī Salamah from Abī Hurayrah who said: Two women from Hudhayl fought, and one of them threw a stone at the other, striking her abdomen, killing her, and she miscarried a fetus. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed that the diyah (blood money) for her be paid by the ʿāqilah (tribal group) of the other woman, and for the fetus, a ghurrah (a slave, male or female). A speaker said: How do we pay ʿaql for one who neither ate nor drank, nor spoke nor cried out at birth? Such a matter is void. The Prophet ﷺ said, as Abī Hurayrah understood: \This is from the brothers of the soothsayers.\"" Muslim narrated this in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"
"16137","(16131) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd that it is from the Sunnah that the diyah (blood money) be paid in installments over three years.\n\n[Weak]"
"16138","(16132) Abū Saʿīd informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: What is the taʿlīgh (intensification) of the camels? He said: One hundred from all categories, and at the end of each year there shall be taken thirteen and one-third khalifah (pregnant she-camels), ten jidhāʿ (five-year-old she-camels), and ten ḥiqqāq (four-year-old she-camels). Al-Shāfiʿī said: The taʿlīgh (intensification) is as ʿAṭāʾ stated — at the end of each year thirteen and one-third khalifah, ten ḥiqqāq, and ten jidhāʿ.\n\n[Weak]"
"16139","(16133) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī informed us that Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd informed us that al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us that Shuʿbah informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Najīḥ informed us. He said: I heard my father say: A man had intercourse with a woman who was a mawlāh (freed slave) of the ʿAbalāt, and he killed her while she was in the Ḥaram (Sacred Sanctuary). ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, assigned for her a diyah (blood money) and an additional third.\n\n[Weak]"
"16140","(16134) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us that Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from his father that a man had intercourse with a woman in Makkah during Dhī al-Qaʿdah and killed her. ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, decreed for her a diyah (blood money) and an additional third.\n\n[Weak]"
"16141","(16135) And Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkari — informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Layth, from Mujāhid, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled regarding one who kills within the Ḥaram, or during the Sacred Month, or while in the state of iḥrām: the full diyah plus one-third of the diyah.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: \The diyah of one killed during the Sacred Months is increased by four thousand"
"16142","(16136) Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Isfarāʾinī informed us there: Abū Saʿīd al-Rāzī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Hishām informed us: Qatādah narrated from Saʿīd — that is, ibn al-Musayyab — regarding one who kills within the Ḥaram, he said: \His diyah is a full diyah plus one-third of a diyah.\"" [Weak]"""
"16143","(16137) And Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Umayyah informed us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us: Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʬāʾ, regarding the slain in the Ḥaram and the Sacred Month: \A diyah and one-third of a diyah.\"" [Good]"""
"16144","(16138) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Ṣāliḥ and Ibn Bukayr both said: Al-Layth informed us: Yūnus narrated to me from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Muslim ibn Yazīd, one of Banī Saʿd ibn Bakr ibn Qays, narrated to me that Abū Shuraīḥ ibn ʿAmr al-Khuzāʿī — who was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — informed him: \The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) killed a man from Hudhayl whom they were pursuing for a blood-feud of the Jāhiliyyah"
"16145","(16139) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adamī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham informed us: al-Haytham ibn Jamīl informed us: Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever kills intentionally is handed over to the guardian of the slain; if he wishes"
"16146","(16140) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed me: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ṣaqr informed me: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd informed me: ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from al-Ḥajjāj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather: \That Qatādah ibn ʿAbdullāh had a slave-girl who tended his sheep. He sent her out one day to graze them"
"16147","(16141) And Abū Aḥmad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī al-ʿAdl — informed us: Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb: \That a man from Banī Mudlij"
"16148","(16142) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us: Bishr ibn ʿUmar al-Zahrānī narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father: \That al-Ḥārith ibn Zayd had been severe against the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"16149","(16143) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ — informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū al-Rabīʿ informed us: Hushaym informed us: Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah ibn Jawshan, from ʿUqbah ibn Aws, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ): \That the Prophet (ﷺ) delivered a sermon on the Day of the Conquest and said: 'There is no deity but Allah alone. He fulfilled His promise"
"16150","(16144) And Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqrīʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū al-Rabīʿ informed us: Hushaym narrated from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), with something similar to the statement of Khālid, except that he said: \One hundred camels"
"16151","(16145) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr — informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas informed me that 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr informed him that his father informed him regarding the document written by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for 'Amr ibn Hazm: \And for the soul (i.e."
"16152","(16146) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us: Abu al-'Abbas informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, regarding the blood-money (diyat) in the document of the Prophet ﷺ to 'Amr ibn Hazm: \And for the soul"
"16153","(16147) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Muhammad al-'Anbari narrated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated from Sulayman ibn Dawud, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ: \He wrote a letter to the people of Yemen containing the obligatory duties"
"16154","(16148) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd narrated from Bushayr ibn Yasar al-Ansari, who claimed that a man from the Ansar called Suhayl ibn Abi Hathmah was informed that a group of his people set out to Khaybar and dispersed among it, and they found one of them killed. He mentioned the hadith of the qasamah (oath-taking). In it: the Prophet of Allah ﷺ disliked that his blood be rendered null and void, and so he paid his blood-money with one hundred camels from the sadaqah (charitable) camels.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Nu'aym, and Muslim recorded it from another route from Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd. [Sahih — agreed upon (muttafaq 'alayh)]"
"16155","(16149) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to me: Malik — (h) — and Abu Sa'id informed us: Abu al-'Abbas informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Malik narrated from Ibn Shihab and Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, and it reached him from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that they used to say: \The blood-money for accidental killing (al-khata') is twenty bint makhad (a one-year-old she-camel)"
"16156","(16150) And Abu Sa'id informed us: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Bahr narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to me: Mukhriqah ibn Bukayr narrated from his father, who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar saying: \The ages of the camels in the blood-money are five categories: five bint labun"
"16157","(16151) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Rafafa' al-Baghdadi informed us: Abu 'Amr 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Bashir narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways and 'Isa ibn Myna narrated to us, they said: 'Abd Abi al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us that his father said: \Those of our jurists whom I met and whose word was considered authoritative — among them Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib"
"16158","(16152) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hannad narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated from Sufyan, from Abi Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn Damrah, who said: 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \For accidental killing"
"16159","(16153) And Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us, they said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Isma'il narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn Yazid narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Abi Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn Damrah, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: \The blood-money for accidental killing is divided into four parts"
"16160","(16154) And Abu 'Abd al-Rahman and Abu Bakr informed us, they said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar narrated to us: 'Umar ibn Ahmad al-Marwazi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: al-Nadr narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Aribah, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, and from 'Abd Rabbihi, from Abi Iyyad, that 'Uthman ibn 'Affan and Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: \The blood-money for accidental killing is thirty hiqqah"
"16161","(16155) And there has been narrated regarding this from the Prophet ﷺ a disconnected hadith, and another which cannot be used as a proof. It was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ, who informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: \Among the rulings of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"
"16162","(16156) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith both informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever is killed by mistake"
"16163","(16157) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Shādhān in Baghdād informed us: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, that he said regarding accidental killing: \It is in fifths — twenty ḥiqqah"
"16164","(16158) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated from Abū Mijlaz, from Abū ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbd Allāh, regarding the blood-money of accidental killing: \It is in fifths — five banī makhāḍ"
"16165","(16159) The hadith of Ibn Masʿūd has been narrated from another route as marfūʿ, but its being raised (to the Prophet) is not authentic. Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us.\n\n(And) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān both informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, all saying: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah Muḥammad ibn Khāzim narrated from al-Ḥajjāj, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khishf ibn Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the blood-money of accidental killing in fifths. He did not add anything beyond this. [Weak]"
"16166","(16160) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj narrated from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khishf ibn Mālik al-Ṭāʾī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The blood-money of accidental killing is twenty ḥiqqah"
"16167","(16161) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh both said: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said regarding the criticism of this hadith: \We do not know anyone who narrated it except Khishf ibn Mālik"
"16168","(16162) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to me: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — and he is Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: \I asked Abū ʿUbaydah: 'Do you transmit anything from ʿAbd Allāh?' He said: 'I do not transmit anything from him.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16169","(16163) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿUrubah and Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāʿid both narrated to us: Bundār narrated to us: Umayyah ibn Khālid narrated to us: Shuʿbah said: \I was with Abū Isḥāq when a man said to Abū Isḥāq: 'Shuʿbah claims that you did not hear anything from ʿAlqamah.' He said: 'He has spoken the truth.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — for Shuʿbah and Abū Isḥāq]"""
"16170","(16164) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: \Abū Isḥāq saw ʿAlqamah but did not hear from him.\""\n\nThe other matter is the hadith of Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah regarding the one whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ compensated. In it"
"16171","(16165) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated — and others with him — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muslim narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from Ibn Shihāb, and from Makḥūl and ʬṭāʾ, who said: We found the people upon the position that the diyah (blood-money) of a free Muslim during the time of the Prophet ﷺ was one hundred camels. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, appraised that diyah in terms of currency at one thousand dinars or twelve thousand dirhams. Abū Saʿīd added in his narration: He said: If the one liable is a Bedouin, then his diyah is one hundred camils, and the Bedouin is not required to pay gold or silver. [Weak]"
"16172","(16166) Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muslim ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to appraise camels for the people of the towns at four hundred dinars or their equivalent in silver, and he would divide it according to the price categories of camels. When camels became expensive, he raised their valuation, and when they became cheap, he reduced their price. The price for the people of the towns remained as it was. [Weak]"
"16173","(16167) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, who said: Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, ruled for the people of the towns when wealth became abundant and camels became scarce, and he set the value of one hundred camels at six hundred dinars up to eight hundred dinars. [Weak]"
"16174","(16168) Abū Saʿīd narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, who used to say: Upon all people collectively — the people of the towns and the people of the desert — is one hundred camels, whether the liable party is a Bedouin or a townsman. [Sound]"
"16175","(16169) Abū Saʿīd narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: Is the diyah in livestock or gold? He said: It was in camels, until ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, came and appraised each camel at one hundred and twenty. So if a townsman wishes, he may give one hundred she-camels and need not give gold — that is according to the original ruling. [Weak]"
"16176","(16170) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī, the jurist, informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān — Abū al-Shaykh — narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, Shaybān ibn Farūkh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Mūsā narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to appraise the diyah for accidental killing for the people of the towns at four hundred dinars or their equivalent in silver, and he would appraise it according to the price categories of camels. When camels became expensive, he raised their valuation, and when they became cheap, he reduced their valuation. During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, it reached between four hundred and eight hundred dinars, or their equivalent in silver — eight thousand dirhams. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for the people of cattle at two hundred cows, and for those whose diyah was in sheep, at two thousand sheep. [Fair]"
"16177","(16171) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us, Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The value of the diyah during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was eight hundred dinars, or eight thousand dirhams, and the diyah of the People of the Book at that time was half the diyah of the Muslims. He said: It remained so until ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, was appointed as Caliph. He stood up as an orator and said: Indeed, camels have become expensive. So ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, fixed it for the people of gold at one thousand dinars, and for the people of silver at twelve thousand dirhams, and for the people of cattle at two hundred cows, and for the people of sheep at two thousand sheep, and for the people of garments at two hundred suits of clothing. He said: And he left the diyah of the People of the Covenant unchanged; he did not raise it when he raised the other diyahs. [Fair]"
"16178","(16172) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated — Isḥāq ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated to me — from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: Among the rulings of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he ruled regarding the major diyah — and he mentioned it — and he mentioned the minor diyah. Then he said: After the passing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, camels became scarce and dirhams became cheap, so ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, appraised the camels of the diyah at six thousand dirhams, calculated at one and a half ūqiyyahs per camel. Then camels became expensive and dirhams became cheap, so ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, added two thousand, calculated at two ūqiyyahs per camel. Then camels became expensive and dirhams became cheap, so ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, set it at twelve thousand dirhams, calculated at three ūqiyyahs per camel. And a third of the diyah is added in the sacred month, and another third for the sacred land. He said: Thus the diyah of the two sacred places reached twenty thousand. He said: And it was said that from the Bedouin, their livestock is taken — they are not required to pay silver or gold — and from each people, the fair value is taken from their wealth, according to the fair valuation of their assets. [Weak]"
"16179","(16173) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: The diyah during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one hundred camels, each camel valued at one ūqiyyah — that being four thousand dirhams. When ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, came to power, camels became expensive and silver became cheap, so ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, made it two ūqiyyahs per camel — that being eight thousand dirhams. Then camels continued to become expensive and silver continued to become cheap, until ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, set it at twelve thousand dirhams in silver, or one thousand dinars in gold, and from cattle two hundred cows, and from sheep two thousand sheep. [Sound as narrated by al-Zuhrī]"
"16180","(16174) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us — Yūnus informed me — from Ibn Shihāb, who said: The value of that during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was four thousand dirhams, one ūqiyyah per camel. Then ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, appraised it during his caliphate when camels became expensive at six thousand dirhams — one and a half ūqiyyahs per camel. Then camels became expensive, so ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, appraised it at two ūqiyyahs per camel — eight thousand dirhams. Then camels became expensive, so ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, appraised it at three ūqiyyahs per camel — twelve thousand dirhams. Ibn Shihāb said: And ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, appraised the diyah in gold at one thousand dinars, and the imams after ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, affirmed it upon that — gold and silver for the people of the towns, and one hundred camels for the people of camels. Al-Shāfiʿī said: The diyah is not appraised except in dinars and dirhams, just as nothing else is appraised except by them. The Sheikh said: What is narrated from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, may also mean that he appraised it without dirhams or dinars by the consent of the perpetrator and the guardian of the victim. And Allah knows best."
"16181","(16175) And similarly is what is reported in the hadith that Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us — Ḥammād informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed the blood-money for the people of camels to be one hundred camels, and for the people of cattle to be two hundred cows, and for the people of sheep to be two thousand sheep, and for the people of garments to be two hundred garments, and for the people of wheat something — which Muḥammad did not retain accurately. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16182","(16176) And Abū ʿAlī informed us — Abū Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd said: I read to Saʿīd ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ṭālaqānī — he informed us — Abū Tumaylah informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq said: ʬāʾ mentioned from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed… and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Mūsā, and said: and for the people of food something — I do not retain it accurately.\n\nThus did Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār narrate it, and the narration of the one who narrated from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) is more abundant and more well-known. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16183","(16177) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī, Abū Bakr, informed us — Muʾādh ibn Hānī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Muslim informed us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A man was killed during the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ set his blood-money at twelve thousand, and that is the meaning of His statement {"
"16184","(16178) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — they both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid informed us — Muḥammad ibn Maymūn al-Khayyāṭ al-Makkī informed us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Prophet ﷺ decreed twelve thousand for the blood-money.\n\nMuḥammad ibn Maymūn said: He only said to us regarding it, on one occasion, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, and more frequently than that he would narrate it from ʿIkrimah from the Prophet ﷺ. [Munkar]"
"16185","(16179) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us — al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah informed us from Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd from al-Zuhrī from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm from his father from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, in the document that he wrote concerning blood-moneys: And upon the people of gold, one thousand dinārs. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"
"16186","(16180) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī informed us — Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān informed us — Mūsā ibn Khalaf informed us from Qatādah from Anas and Yazīd al-Raqāshī from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Verily, my sitting with a people who remember Allah from the morning prayer until the sun rises is dearer to me than what the sun rises upon; and my sitting with a people who remember Allah from the ʿAṣr prayer until the Maghrib prayer is dearer to me than freeing eight descendants of Ismāʿīl — the blood-money of each one of them being twelve thousand. [Ḥasan]"
"16187","(16181) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī related on the authority of Yazīd ibn Hārūn from Hishām from al-Ḥasan: that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) decreed the blood-money at twelve thousand. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16188","(16182) Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us — Ibn Wahb informed us — Muḥammad ibn Muslim al-Ṭāʾifī informed me from Ibrāhīm ibn Maysarah: that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) was one day praying when a serpent appeared near her, so she commanded that it be killed, and it was killed. Then it was shown to her in her dream: \Have you killed a Muslim man who came to hear the Qurʾān? His blood-money is such.\"" So she paid his blood-money: twelve thousand. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16189","(16183) And we have been narrated from Abū Hurayrah that which indicates that the blood-money is twelve thousand, as Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us by way of ijāzah — Abū al-Walīd informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us — ʿImrān ibn Mūsā al-Qazzāz informed us — ʿAbd al-Wārith informed us — Khālid informed us from ʿIkrimah that Abū Hurayrah said: Indeed, I glorify Allah every day to the extent of my blood-money: twelve thousand. [Ḥasan]"
"16190","(16184) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed me that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed them from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Verily, I fear that after me there may come someone who destroys the blood-music of the Muslim person, so I shall say regarding it: upon the people of camels, one hundred camels; upon the people of gold, one thousand dinārs; and upon the people of silver, twelve thousand dirhams. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16191","(16185) And Abū Saʿīd informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me — ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn ʿUmar, informed me, from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from Ibn Shihāb and Ibn Abī Rabāḥ: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, valued the diyah (blood-money) at one thousand dinārs or twelve thousand dirhams. [Weak]"
"16192","(16186) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī said: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan said: \It has reached us from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"
"16193","(16187) Abū Ḥanīfah narrated to us regarding that — from al-Haytham — from al-Shaʿbī — from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him. And he said: The people of Madinah said that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, imposed the diyah upon the people of silver at twelve thousand dirhams. Muḥammad said: \The people of Madinah have spoken the truth that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"
"16194","(16188) Muḥammad said: \Al-Thawrī informed us — from Mughīrah al-Ḍabbī — from Ibrāhīm"
"16195","(16189) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Yūnus informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \I read the letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ which he wrote to ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm when he sent him to Najrān"
"16196","(16190) And Abū Bakr, Abū Zakariyyā, and Abū Saʿīd informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Mālik ibn Anas narrated to me — that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr informed him, that his father informed him, regarding the letter which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm concerning blood-money (al-ʿuqūl), similar to the ḥadīth of Ibn Shihāb, except that he did not mention the ears or the munqilah. [Authentic (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"
"16197","(16191) Abū ʿAbd Allāl-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us — al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated to me — from Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd — from al-Zuhrī — from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm — from his father — from his grandfather — from the Prophet ﷺ: that he wrote a letter to the people of Yemen containing the obligatory duties, the sunnahs, and the blood-money (al-diyāt), and he sent it with ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm. It was read to the people of Yemen, and this is its copy. He then mentioned the ḥadīth in its entirety, and in it: \And in the soul is the diyah of one hundred camels; and in the nose"
"16198","(16192) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik informed us — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr — from his father, that in the letter which the Prophet ﷺ wrote to ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm it stated: \And in the muḍiḥah are five camels.\"" [Authentic (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"16199","(16193) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us — Ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us — Mūsā narrated to us — Hishām ibn Yūsuf narrated to me — from Maʿmar — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr — from his father — from his grandfather, that the Prophet ￺ judged in the muḍiḥah with five camels. And ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar and added therein: \And in the māʾmūmah is one-third of the diyah"
"16200","(16194) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Abū Kāmil Fuḍayl ibn Ḥusayn narrated to us — Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to them — Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated to us — from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb — that his father informed him — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \In the mawāḍiḥ (wounds that expose the bone) are five camels.\"" [Good (Ḥasan)]"""
"16201","(16195) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated from Matar, from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \For the exposed bone wounds (al-mawadiha)"
"16202","(16196) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamirawayh informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated from Abu Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn Damrah, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: \For the exposed bone wound (al-mudihah)"
"16203","(16197) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated from Makhul, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said: \For the exposed bone wound (al-mudihah)"
"16204","(16198) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me by way of ijazah: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us: 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib, from his father, from his grandfather, that Abu Bakr and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \The exposed bone wound (al-mudihah) on the face and the head are equal.\"" [Sahih]"""
"16205","(16199) He said: And Abu Bakr — that is, Ibn Abi Shaybah — narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from Hajjaj, from Makhul, from Zayd: \The exposed bone wound (al-mudihah) on the face"
"16206","(16200) He said: And Abu Bakr informed us: Abu Usamah narrated from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Shuraih and al-Hasan, who said: \The exposed bone wound (al-mudihah) on the face is the same as the exposed bone wound (al-mudihah) on the head.\"" [Sahih]"""
"16207","(16201) And Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: al-Layth — meaning Anas ibn Iyyad — narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that he used to say: \The exposed bone wound (al-mudihah) on the face is the same as the exposed bone wound (al-mudihah) on the head"
"16208","(16202) Abu al-Hasan al-Baghdadi al-Raffa' informed us: 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Isma'il al-Qadi narrated to us: Ibn Abi Uways and 'Isa ibn Mina' narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madinah: \They used to consider the exposed bone wound (al-mudihah) on the face and the head as equal"
"16209","(16203) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us, saying: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Farisi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Makhul, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said: \For the exposed bone wound (al-mudihah)"
"16210","(16204) And Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzaki informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us: Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from Makhul, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) decreed regarding wounds: for the exposed bone wound (al-mudihah) and above"
"16211","(16205) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Abū Isḥāq from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), who said: In the case of the *munqilah* [a wound that displaces a bone], [the diyah is] fifteen [camels].\n\nAnd it has also been reported from Zayd ibn Thābit (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16212","(16206) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik ibn Anas informed us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr from his father: That in the document which the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) wrote for ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, [it stated]: And in the case of the *maʾmūmah* [a wound reaching the brain membrane], [the diyah is] one-third of the diyah for murder, and in the case of the *jāʾifah* [a wound reaching the abdominal cavity], the same as that. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"
"16213","(16207) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh, narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us — Shaybān narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Mūsā narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) decreed regarding the *maʾmūmah* [a wound reaching the brain membrane] one-third of the ʿaql [blood-money]: thirty-three camels and one-third, or their equivalent value in gold, silver, cattle, or sheep; and the *jāʾifah* [a wound reaching the abdominal cavity] is the same as that.\n\nAnd it has also been reported from ʿAlī and Zayd ibn Thābit (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā). [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi]"
"16214","(16208) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me — ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn ʿUmar informed me — from Ibn Shihāb, and Rabīʿah, and Abū al-Zinād, and Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh: That the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) did not enforce the ʿaql [blood-money] for injuries less than the *muḍiḥah* [a wound exposing the bone], and he made what is less than the *muḍiḥah* a matter of pardon [ʿafw] among the Muslims. [Ḍaʿīf jiddan]"
"16215","(16209) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik ibn Anas said: The matter upon which there is consensus [ijmāʿ] among us is that there is no ʿaql [blood-money] for wounds [shijāj] less than the *muḍiḥah* [a wound exposing the bone] until it reaches the *muḍiḥah*. The ʿaql is only in the *muḍiḥah* and what is above it. That is because the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) ended at the *muḍiḥah* in his document to ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm and assigned therein five camels. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Mālik]"
"16216","(16210) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārīzī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us — Abū ʿUbayd narrated to us — Hushaym narrated from Ḥuṣayn, who said: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said: What is less than the *muḍiḥah* [a wound exposing the bone] are merely scratches [khudūsh], in which there is reconciliation [ṣulḥ].\n\nAnd Ibn ʿUlāthah narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Abī ʿAblah: That Muʿādh and ʿUmar (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) assigned, for what is less than the *muḍiḥah*, only the fee of the physician [ajr al-ṭabīb].\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of Ibn Ghanm from Muʿādh ibn Jabal (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), it is raised [marfūʿ]: \And in the *muḍiḥah* [a wound exposing the bone] there are five camels"
"16217","(16211) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — al-Thiqah [a trustworthy narrator] informed us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith — \If I did not hear it from ʿAbd Allāh\"" — from Mālik ibn Anas from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qusayṭ from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib: That ʿUmar and ʿUthmān (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) decreed regarding the *milṭāh* [a wound reaching the periosteum] half of the diyah of the *muḍiḥah* [a wound exposing the bone]. [Ḥasan]"""
"16218","(16212) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Bakr, and Abū Zakariyyā informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj from al-Thawrī from Mālik from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qusayṭ from Ibn al-Musayyib from ʿUmar and ʿUthmān (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) the like of that, or the like of its meaning.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And someone who heard Ibn Nāfiʿ informed me that he mentioned from Mālik, with this chain of narration, the like of it.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And we read upon Mālik: \We do not know of any of the imāms"
"16219","(16213) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī in Baghdad informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Ibn Jurayj narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Mālik from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qusayṭ from Ibn al-Musayyib: That ʿUmar and ʿUthmān (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) decreed regarding the *milṭāh*, which is the *simḥāq* [a wound reaching the periosteum], half of what is in the *muḍiḥah* [a wound exposing the bone].\n\nʿAbd al-Razzāq said: Then Sufyān came to us, and we asked him about it, and he narrated it to us from Mālik. Then I met Mālik and said: \Sufyān narrated to us from you"
"16220","(16214) Abū Muḥammad al-Sukkārī informed him — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated from Makhūl from Qabīṣah ibn Dhūʾayb from Zayd ibn Thābit (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), who said: In the *dāmiyah* [a wound that bleeds] [the diyah is] one camel; in the *bāḍiʿah* [a wound that does not bleed] two camels; in the *mutalāḥimah* [a wound in which the flesh becomes exposed] three; in the *simḥāq* [a wound reaching the periosteum] four; and in the *muḍiḥah* [a wound exposing the bone] five.\n\nThe shaykh [i.e., the author] said: Muḥammad ibn Rāshid — even though we narrate his ḥadīth for the narration of the great narrators from him — is not among those whose solitary reports constitute a proof [ḥujjah].\n\nAnd it has been reported from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) that he said: In the *simḥāq* [a wound reaching the periosteum] [the diyah is] four camels.\n\nAnd from Jābir al-Juʿfī from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) the like of that. The first [chain] is severed [munqaṭiʿ], and the second is severed. Then, if this narration is authentic, it is interpreted as their having decreed regarding what is less than the *muḍiḥah* a ruling that reached this amount [by way of discretionary assessment], and Allah knows best. [Ḥasan]"
"16221","(16215) It was narrated that Abū ‘Abdillāh al-Hāfiẓ said: Al-Husayn b. Muḥammad al-Māsarjisī said: “What I have heard him narrate from his hearing, Abū Bakr said: “Ahmad b. Mas‘ūd al-Tujībī narrated to us: “Yaḥyā b. Muḥammad b. ‘Akhī Harmlaḥ narrated to us: “My uncle Harmlaḥ b. Yaḥyā narrated to us: ‘Al-Shāfi‘ī – may Allah have mercy on him – said: The first type of wound is al-shijāj al-ḥārisa, which is the one that tears the skin slightly until it splits; and some say that al-qassār – the tailor – is so named because he tears the cloth when it splits, then al-bāḍi‘a, which is the one that tears the flesh and exposes it after the skin; then al-mutallāḥima, which is the one that cuts into the flesh but does not reach the simḥāq. The simḥāq is a thin layer of skin between the flesh and the bone, and any thin layer of skin is called simḥāq. When the wound reaches this thin layer of skin until nothing remains between the flesh and the bone except it, that is the simḥāq, which is also called al-milṭā’a. Then al-mūḍiḥa, which is the one that removes that thin layer and splits it until the bone becomes visible; that is al-mūḍiḥa. And al-hāshima, which crushes the bone, and al-munaqqala, which removes the bone dust from it, and al-‘āmā’a, which is al-mā’mūma, the one that reaches the uppermost part of the skull, and al-jā’ifa, which is the one that penetrates deeply until it reaches the sides, and anything less than al-mūḍiḥa is a scratch in which there is no bleeding, and al-dāmīya is the one that causes a wound or injury without any blood flowing from it.”"
"16222","(16216) It was narrated that Abū al-Ḥusayn b. Bashrān al-‘Adl said: Abū Ja‘far – Muḥammad b. ‘Amr al-Razzāẓ narrated to us: Yaḥyā b. Ja‘far narrated to us: Wahb b. Jarīr narrated to us: Hishām narrated to us: “Yaḥyā b. Abī Kaṡīr said: ‘Yaḥyā b. Sa‘īd sent me a copy of the book that was with Abū Bakr b. Muḥammad b. ‘Amr b. Ḥazm, which the Messenger of Allah – ﷺ – had written for ‘Amr b. Ḥazm, and in it is: If the udhūb (the udhūb is the udhūb of the udhūb) is cut off completely, then the udhūb is complete; and in the eye, half of the udhūb; and in the udhūma, one-third of the udhūb; and in the jā’ifa, one-third of the udhūb; and in the mūḍiḥa, five udhūb; and in the sin, five udhūb; and in each finger, ten udhūb.’”\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from other chains, both mursala and muqaddama. [Hasan li-ghayrih]"
"16223","(16217) It was narrated that Abū Naṣr b. Qatāda said: Abū al-Faḍl b. Khumayr narrated to us: Ahmad b. Najda narrated to us: Sa‘īd b. Manṣūr narrated to us: Abū ‘Awn narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq, from ‘Asim b. Dhamra, from ‘Alī – may Allah be pleased with him – who said: “In the jā’ifa, one-third; and in the ‘āmā’a, one-third.” [Da‘īf]"
"16224","(16218) It was narrated that Abū Bakr al-Ardastānī said: Abū Naṣr al-‘Irāqī narrated to us: Sufyān b. Muḥammad al-Jawḥarī narrated to us: ‘Alī b. al-Ḥasan al-Darābadjirdī narrated to us: ‘Abdillāh b. al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us from Muḥammad b. ‘Ubaidillāh, from ‘Amr b. Shu‘ayb, from Sa‘īd b. al-Muṣayyab, that a man shot another man, and a jā’ifa wound struck him, and it came out from the other side; Abū Bakr – may Allah be pleased with him – judged that it was one-third of the udhūb. [Da‘īf]"
"16225","(16219) It was narrated that Abū Naṣr b. Qatāda said: Abū al-Faḍl b. Khumayr narrated to us: Ahmad b. Najda narrated to us: Sa‘īd b. Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Hajjāj narrated to us: ‘Amr b. Shu‘ayb narrated to us from Sa‘īd b. al-Muṣayyab, that Abū Bakr – may Allah be pleased with him – judged that in the jā’ifa, it was one-third of the udhūb. [Da‘īf]"
"16226","(16220) It was narrated that Abū Bakr b. al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and others said: Abū al-‘Abbās al-Asamm narrated to us: Bahr b. Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Yunus b. Yazīd narrated to me from Ibn Shihāb, who said: “I read the letter of the Messenger of Allah – ﷺ – which he wrote for ‘Amr b. Ḥazm when he sent him to Najrān, and in it he wrote: In the udhūb, fifty udhūb.” [Sahīh li-Zuhayrī, jadīd]"
"16227","(16221) It was narrated that Abū Bakr b. al-Ḥasan and others said: Abū al-‘Abbās narrated to us: Bahr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: ‘Iyāḍ b. ‘Abdillāh al-Fihrī narrated to me that he heard Zayd b. Aslam say: “The sunna of the human body has passed, and he mentioned the hadith, saying: ‘In it, and in the two ears, the udhūb.’” [Da‘īf]"
"16228","(16222) It was narrated that Abū Muḥammad as-Sukkarī said: Ismā‘īl as-Saffār narrated to us: Ahmad b. Manṣūr narrated to us: ‘Abdur-Razzāq narrated to us: Ma‘mar narrated to us from ‘Amr b. Muslim, from Tawus and ‘Ikrima, that ‘Umar – may Allah be pleased with him – judged that in the udhūb, it was half of the udhūb. Ma‘mar said: “And the people say that Abū Bakr – may Allah be pleased with him – judged it to be fifteen udhūb.” [Da‘īf]"
"16229","(16223) It was narrated that Abū Naṣr b. Qatāda said: Abū al-Faḍl b. Khumayr narrated to us: Ahmad b. Najda narrated to us: Sa‘īd b. Manṣūr narrated to us: Abū ‘Awn narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq, from ‘Asim b. Dhamra, from ‘Alī – may Allah be pleased with him – who said: “In the udhūb, half.” The Sha‘bī narrated from Ibn Mas‘ūd – may Allah be pleased with him – that he said: “In the udhūb, if it is cut off, half of the udhūb is one-fifth, and whatever is less than that is calculated.” [Da‘īf]"
"16230","(16224) It was narrated to me by Abū ‘Abdillāh al-Hāfiẓ with ijāza: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: al-Ḥasan b. Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Rishdīn b. Sa‘d narrated to us from ‘Abdur-Raḥmān b. Ziyād b. An‘am, from ‘Utba b. Ḥumayd, from ‘Ubāda b. Nuṣayy, from Ibn Ghannam, from Mu‘ādh b. Jabal – may Allah be pleased with him – that the Prophet – ﷺ – said: “In the udhūb, one hundred udhūb.” [Da‘īf]"
"16231","(16225) And with this chain, it is narrated: In the case of loss of hearing, the blood-money is one hundred camels. It has been narrated to us from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, peace be upon him, that he made a definitive ruling regarding compensation for loss of hearing through blood-money. \nThis is related by Hajjaj ibn 'Arta' from Makhul from Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him. [Weak]"
"16232","(16226) It was reported to us by Abu Zakariya ibn Ibrahim and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Sa'id ibn 'Amr, who said: Abu al-'Abbas, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb reported to us, Yunus reported to us from Ibn Shihab, who said: In the case of loss of hearing, if the blood-money is fully paid, it is complete. [Sahih]"
"16233","(16227) It was reported to us by Abu Sa'id, who said: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us, Bahr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb reported to us, Yunus reported to us from Rab'iyya, who said: In the case of loss of hearing, if all of it is lost, the blood-money is complete. Rab'iyya said: And if it is lost from one ear, then half of the mind is in it. Yunus said: Abu al-Zinad said this. Ibn Wahb said: I heard Mu'awiya ibn Salih say: Al-'Ala' ibn al-Harith reported to me that he heard Makhul say: That is in the case of total loss of hearing, the blood-money is complete. Mu'awiya said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id say this. \nThis is also narrated by ash-Sha'bi, Ibrahim, and others. [Sahih]"
"16234","(16228) It was reported to me by Abu 'Abd Allah, in the form of a concession, that Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Hasan ibn Sufyan reported to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us from 'Awf, who said: I heard an old man before the Fitna of ibn al-Ash'ath, and he was called Abu al-Muhallab, uncle of Abu Qilabah, who said: A man was stoned on the head, and his hearing, speech, mind, and memory were lost; he did not approach women, and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, ruled for him four blood-moneys. [Weak]"
"16235","(16229) He said, and narrated to us: Abu Bakr, who is ibn Abi Shaybah, from 'Abd al-A'la from Yunus from al-Hasan: In a man who is struck such that his hearing, sight, and speech are lost, there are three blood-moneys. [Sahih, by al-Hasan]"
"16236","(16230) It was reported to us by Abu 'Abd al-Rahman as-Sulamiyy and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih, who said: Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Farisi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Rashid from Makhul from Qabisah ibn Dhaw'ib from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: In a man who is struck until his mind is lost, the blood-money is complete. \nThis is also narrated by Hajjaj ibn 'Arta' from Makhul from Zayd, who said: In the case of loss of mind, the blood-money is complete. [Hasan]"
"16237","(16231) It was reported to us by Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariya ibn Ibrahim and Abu Sa'id ibn 'Amr, who said: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Jawab narrated to us, 'Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ubaid Allah ibn 'Umar from 'Umar from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: In the nose, if the bone is dislocated, the blood-money is one hundred camels; in the hand, fifty; in the foot, fifty; in the eye, fifty; in the brain, one-third of the soul; in the spine, one-third of the soul; in the spinal cord, fifteen; in the exposed bone, five; in the teeth, five; and in each finger of that category, ten. \nThis is also narrated by Waki' from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from a man from the family of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made a ruling, and he mentioned additions and deductions. [Weak]"
"16238","(16232) It was reported to us by Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishrān, who said: Isma'il as-Saffar narrated to us, Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us, Mu'adh narrated to us from Ash'ath from al-Hasan: A question was asked about a man who was struck so that his mind was lost. He said: If 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, had reached him, he would have included it in the blood-money. [Sahih]"
"16239","(16233) It was reported to us by Abu Bakr: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Sa'id ibn 'Amr and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman as-Sulamiyy, who said: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Jawab narrated to us, 'Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ubaid Allah ibn 'Umar from 'Umar from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: In the nose, if the bone is dislocated, the blood-money is one hundred camels; in the hand, fifty; in the foot, fifty; in the eye, fifty; in the brain, one-third of the soul; in the spine, one-third of the soul; in the spinal cord, fifteen; in the exposed bone, five; in the teeth, five; and in each finger of that category, ten. \nThis is also narrated by Waki' from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from a man from the family of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made a ruling, and he mentioned additions and deductions. [Weak]"
"16240","(16234) It was reported to us by Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah, who said: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamirwayh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from 'Asim ibn Dhamra from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: In the eye, it is half. [Weak]"
"16241","(16235) It was narrated that Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hafiz, with ijazah, said: ‘Abu ‘Abdillah narrated to us: ‘Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: ‘Abbad ibn al-‘Awwam narrated to us from ‘Umar ibn ‘Amir, from Qatadah, from Sa‘id ibn al-Mu’ayyib, that a man struck another man in the eye, so he took part of his sight and some remained. He took that to ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who ordered that the sound eye be bound with a bandage. A man was sent with a piece of white cloth, and he went with it while looking until his sight was restored. Then he marked it with a flag, and they examined it and found it to be equal. He gave him as much as he had lost from his sight, as much as was taken from the other."
"16242","(16236) Sulaymi and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us: Ali ibn ‘Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma‘il al-Farisi narrated to us: Ishmaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: ‘Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Makhul, from Qabisah ibn Dhul-‘Ayb, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that in the case of the eye, a quarter of the diyah is required. It was narrated by Muhammad ibn Ishmaq from Makhul, who said: They would place in the eye when something was taken from the eye, the diyah. It was narrated to us in this regard by al-Sha‘bi (may Allah have mercy on him)."
"16243","(16237) Zakariyya ibn Ishmaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Abu al-‘Abbas narrated to us: Rab‘i narrated to us: al-Shafi‘i narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us from ‘Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, that in the document that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote for ‘Amr ibn Hazm: “In the case of the nose, if it is gouged out, there are one hundred camels.”"
"16244","(16238) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us: Ali ibn ‘Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Hatim ibn Isma‘il narrated to us from Muhammad ibn ‘Umarah, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Amr ibn Hazm, who said: In the document of ‘Amr ibn Hazm, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent him to Najran: “In the case of the nose, if the bleeding camel is fully bled, the diyah is complete.” It was narrated to us in the connected hadith from ‘Amr ibn Hazm from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “In the case of the nose, if his gouging is fully gouged, the diyah.”"
"16245","(16239) Abu Bakr: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Harith al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan, Abu al-Shaykh, narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Shibab narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us: Sulaiman ibn Musa narrated to us from ‘Amr ibn Shu‘ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled in the case of the nose: if it is gouged out, the diyah is complete; and if the gouging of his nose is gouged, then half of the diyah is fifty camels, or its equivalent in gold or silver."
"16246","(16240) Abu Sa‘id ibn Abi ‘Amr narrated to us: Abu al-‘Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya‘qub narrated to us: Rab‘i ibn Sulaiman narrated to us: al-Shafi‘i said: Ibn Tawus narrated to us from his father, who said: There is a book from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in which it is written: “In the case of the nose, if the bleeding camel is cut off, one hundred camels.”"
"16247","(16241) The Sheikh said: In the narration of Waki‘ from ibn Abi Layla, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from a man from the family of ‘Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled in the case of the nose: if his bleeding camel is fully bled, the diyah. And this is what Abu ‘Abdillah narrated to me with ijazah: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Ibn Zuhayr narrated to us: ‘Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us: Waki‘ narrated to us. He mentioned it and narrated what we narrated before this in the case of the eye."
"16248","(16242) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah narrated to us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamir narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa‘id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abu ‘Awanah narrated to us from Abu Ishmaq, from ‘Asim ibn Dhamrah, from ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: “In the case of the nose, the diyah.”"
"16249","(16243) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran narrated to us: Isma‘il al-Saffar narrated to us: Sa‘dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Mu‘adh ibn Mu‘adh narrated to us: al-Ash‘ath narrated to us from al-Hasan, who said: “In the case of the bleeding camel, the diyah.”"
"16250","(16244) The Imam, Abu ‘Uthman, narrated to us: Zahir narrated to us: al-Baghawi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: ‘Abbad ibn al-‘Awwam narrated to us: ‘Umar, who is ibn ‘Amir, narrated to us from Makhul, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: “In the three perforations of the nose, the diyah, and in each one, a third of the diyah.”"
"16251","(16245) And he narrated: Hajjaj narrated from Makhuul from Zaid ibn Thabit, as before. [Weak]"
"16252","(16246) He informed us, Abu ‘Abdur-Rahman as-Sulami and Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah, said: He informed us, Abu ‘Amr ibn Matar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn ‘Abdul-Jabbar narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Sulaiman ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Amr ibn Hazm from his father from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wrote to the people of Yemen in a letter: “And in the two cheeks, there is a diya.” [Good, for others]"
"16253","(16247) He informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, and Abu Zakariya ibn Ibrahim, and Abu Sa’id ibn Abu ‘Amr, said: He narrated to us, Abu al-‘Abbas, Muhammad ibn Ya’qub narrated to us, Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, ibn Wahb informed me, ‘Iyad ibn ‘Abdillah al-Fihri informed me, that he heard Zaid ibn Aslam say: “The Sunnah has been established concerning matters of the human body, and he mentioned the hadith, saying in it: ‘And in the two cheeks, there is a diya.’ And ‘Amr ibn Shu’aib narrated, saying: “Abu Bakr (radiyallahu ‘anhu) judged in the two cheeks with a diya of one hundred camels.”\n\nAnd it was narrated to us from ash-Sha’bi that he said: “In the two cheeks, there is a diya, and in each of them, there is half.” [Weak]"
"16254","(16248) He informed us, Abu ‘Abdur-Rahman as-Sulami and Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah, said: He informed us, Abu ‘Amr ibn Matar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn ‘Abdul-Jabbar narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Sulaiman ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Amr ibn Hazm from his father from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wrote to the people of Yemen in a letter: “And in the tongue, there is a diya.”\n\nAnd it is in the hadith of Mu’adh ibn Jabal, raised, and in the hadith of a man from the family of ‘Umar (radiyallahu ‘anhu) from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAnd it was narrated to us from ‘Umar (radiyallahu ‘anhu) that it does not indicate that he judged it with a diya. [Good, for others]"
"16255","(16249) And he informed us, Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah, he informed us, Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamirwayh, he informed us, Ahmad ibn Najdah, narrated to us, Sa’id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu ‘Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from ‘Asim ibn Dhamrah, from ‘Ali (radiyallahu ‘anhu), that he said: “In the tongue, there is a diya.” [Weak]"
"16256","(16250) And he informed us, Abu Zakariya ibn Ibrahim, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, and Abu Sa’id ibn Abu ‘Amr, said: He narrated to us, Abu al-‘Abbas, Muhammad ibn Ya’qub narrated to us, Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, ibn Wahb informed me, Yunus from ibn Shihab informed me, that Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab informed him, that the Sunnah has been established in the mind that in the tongue, there is a diya. [Authentic, for ibn al-Musayyab]"
"16257","(16251) He said, and ibn Wahb narrated to me, Yunus informed me from ibn Shihab, that ‘Iyad ibn ‘Abdillah al-Fihri informed me, that he heard Zaid ibn Aslam say: “The Sunnah has been established concerning matters of the human body, he said: ‘And in the tongue, there is a diya, and in the voice, when the diya is cut off.’” [Weak]"
"16258","(16252) He informed us, Abu Sa’d al-Malini, narrated to us, Abu Ahmad ibn ‘Adi al-Hafiz, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Barqiy, narrated to us, Yunus ibn ‘Abdul-‘Aziiz informed us, ibn Wahb informed me, al-Harith ibn Nabhan informed me, from Muhammad ibn ‘Ubaidillah, from ‘Amr ibn Shu’aib, from his father, from ‘Abdillah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), he said: “In the tongue, there is a diya, when speech is prevented, and in the male organ, there is a diya, when the foreskin is cut off, and in the two cheeks, there is a diya.”\n\nThis isnad is weak. Muhammad ibn ‘Ubaidillah al-‘Arzamiy and al-Harith ibn Nabhan are weak. [Weak]"
"16259","(16253) He informed me, Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hafiz, by way of ijazah, he informed us, Abu al-Walid, narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abu Shiba’a, I think he is from Muhammad ibn Bakr, from ibn Juraij, informed me, ‘Abdul-‘Aziz ibn ‘Umar informed me, that in a letter of ‘Umar ibn ‘Abdul-‘Aziz, from ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab (radiyallahu ‘anhu): “And in the tongue, when the diya is taken completely, and nothing is lost from the tongue, it is said that speech is prevented, and in it, there is a diya, and what is less than that, it is accounted for.” [Weak]"
"16260","(16254) He said, and Abu Bakr narrated from ibn Fudayl, from Ash’ath, from ash-Sha’bi, from ‘Abdillah, he said: “In the tongue, there is a diya, when it is cut off, and if there is any deficiency, it is accounted for.” [Weak]"
"16261","(16255) Abu Bakr narrated: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, who said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, ruled regarding the tongue: if it is severed at its root, the entire compensation is due; and if it is cut but speech is not prevented, then half of the compensation is due."
"16262","(16256) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran from Bagdad informed us: Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr informed us: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, who said: In the case of speech being cut off, the entire compensation is due."
"16263","(16257) Abu al-Husayn informed us: Ismail informed us: Sa'dan informed us: Abu Muhammad, 'Abd Allah ibn Yufin informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabiyy informed us: Sa'dan informed us: Sufyan narrated from Ma'mar, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: There are twenty-eight letters. Whatever is cut from the tongue is due according to the number of letters it lacks. It is also related from Masruq that he said: In the language of the Ahras, there is governance."
"16264","(16258) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated from al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan, who narrated from Muhammad ibn Bashir, from Sa'id, who is Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Matar, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) ruled concerning the teeth: five for five camels, and concerning the teeth: five for five, and concerning the fingers: ten for ten."
"16265","(16259) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamiruwaih informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdat narrated from Sa'id ibn Mansur, who narrated from Abu 'Awannah, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn Dhamrah, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: In the teeth, there are five."
"16266","(16260) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abu Ishaq, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated from Bahr ibn Nasr, who narrated from ibn Wahb, who narrated to me, 'Iyad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Fihri, that he heard Zayd ibn Aslam say: The sunna has decreed matters concerning the human body, and he mentioned the hadith, saying: In the teeth, there is compensation. It is also related in the hadith of Mu'adh ibn Jabal, reported in the elevated form: In all the teeth, there are one hundred camels. In its chain, there is weakness. The hadith of Zayd ibn Aslam is interrupted. The report of one who narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him): In every tooth, there are five camels, is more numerous and more famous. We have been informed by Sharih that he said: When a tooth is broken, he is given a year's respite. We have also been informed by al-Sha'bi from al-Harith, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: It is expected to last for about a year. And from Makhul, from Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, in the same manner."
"16267","(16261) This entire matter is what Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu al-Walid narrated: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shibah narrated: Abu Khalid narrated from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Sharih, who mentioned it."
"16268","(16262) He said, and Abu Bakr narrated: 'Abbad narrated from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who mentioned it. And from 'Abbad, from Hajjaj, from Makhul, from Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, in the same manner."
"16269","(16263) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sadiq, Muhammad ibn Abi Falasis, and Abu al-Hasan, 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tirazi, said: Abu al-'Abbas, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated from al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri, who narrated from 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq, who informed us, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The teeth and the fingers are equal."
"16270","(16264) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us: Abu Tahir al-Muhammad Abadiyy narrated: Abu Qilabah, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad narrated: 'Abd al-Samad, and Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbariyy informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated: Abu Dawud narrated: 'Abbas al-Anbari narrated: 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to me, Shucbah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The fingers are equal, and the teeth are equal, the second and the third are equal, this and this are equal. In the report of Abu Qilabah, he said: This and this are equal, meaning the incisors and the canines, the third and the second. Abu Dawud reported it, al-Nadhr ibn Shumail narrated from Shucbah in the meaning of the hadith of 'Abd al-Samad, the Dari narrated from al-Nadhr."
"16271","(16265) It was narrated that Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Rab'i ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from Abu Ghathafan ibn Tharif al-Murri, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to 'Abdullah ibn Abbas to ask him about the dhiras. Ibn Abbas said concerning it: Five units of camels. Marwan then sent him back and said: Do you equate the front teeth with the molar teeth? Ibn Abbas said: Even the fingers are all equal; their intellect is complete. Al-Shafi'i said: This is as Ibn Abbas said. If Allah wills, the blood-money is fixed according to number, not according to benefit."
"16272","(16266) It was narrated that Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas al-Ash'am narrated to us, Rab'i ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id, who said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, judged in the case of the molar teeth by one camel, while Mu'awiya, may Allah be pleased with him, judged in the case of the molar teeth by five camels. The blood-money decreases in the judgment of 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and increases in the judgment of Mu'awiya, may Allah be pleased with him. If I had been the judge, I would have judged in the case of the molar teeth by two camels; that blood-money would be complete. Al-Shafi'i said: Then you have contradicted the hadith of 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and you say concerning the molar teeth: five, five—and we say that as it has come from the Prophet (peace be upon him): in the teeth, five. And the molar tooth is a tooth.\n\nThe Sheikh said: It has also been narrated by Jabir al-Ju'fi from 'Amr from Shurahbil and Masruq from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: the teeth are all equal. And it is also mentioned from al-Hasan from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The teeth are all equal—whether molar or premolar."
"16273","(16267) It was narrated that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab said: When a tooth turns black, its intellect is complete.\n\nMalik said to me: Our position on this is as such."
"16274","(16268) It was narrated that Muhammad ibn Ya'qub said: Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to me from his father, who said: I heard my father say: In the case of a tooth, if it is struck and then turns black, all of its intellect is complete."
"16275","(16269) It was narrated that Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Salim said: It was mentioned to us that he was with the sword of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning the matter of intellect, and in the case of a tooth, if it turns black, its intellect is complete; but if it is struck again after that, then there is a second intellect in it. This narration is incomplete."
"16276","(16270) It was narrated that 'Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated from Yahya ibn Ya'mar from Ibn Abbas from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: In the case of the standing eye, the blackened tooth, and the withered hand, one-third of its blood-money is due.\n\nIt is said: This is what he intended, and Allah knows best—that he made a ruling in it that reaches one-third of its blood-money."
"16277","(16271) It was narrated from al-Sha'bi from al-Harith from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that in the case of a tooth, if part of it is broken, the owner is given compensation according to what is lost from it, and it is left to heal for a year. If it turns black, its intellect is complete; otherwise, nothing is added to that.\n\nAnd it is also narrated from Hajjaj from Makhul from Zayd in the same way."
"16278","(16272) It was narrated that 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated from his father that in the document that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) wrote for 'Amr ibn Hazm: In the hand, fifty, and in the foot, fifty, and in each of the fingers that are in that, ten camels."
"16279","(16273) It was narrated that 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) judged in the case of the hand when it is severed: half of the intellect, and in the case of the foot: half of the intellect."
"16280","(16274) It was narrated that 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace be upon him), while standing with his back to the Ka'bah, said in his sermon: In the fingers, ten, ten."
"16281","(16275) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī in al-Baṣrah narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us — Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \This and this are equal"
"16282","(16276) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh al-Isfarāyinī therein informed us — Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Madīnī narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm, that is Ibn ʿUlayyah, narrated to us — Ghālib al-Tammār narrated from Masrūq ibn Aws al-Tamīmī, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \In the fingers"
"16283","(16277) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Bishr al-ʿAbdī narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah — Ghālib al-Tammār narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from Masrūq ibn Aws, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he decreed regarding the fingers ten [camels] ten from the camels.\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated by Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar and ʿAbadah ibn Sulaymān from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah.\n\nAnd Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated from Ghālib, mentioning in it Ghālib's hearing from Masrūq, except that he did not establish his name clearly in most of the narrations from him. [Ḥasan]"
"16284","(16278) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed him — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from Ghālib al-Tammār — Aws ibn Masrūq or Masrūq ibn Aws narrated from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The fingers are equal.\"" I said: \""In each finger"
"16285","(16279) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us — al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Maṭar, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \For [wounds exposing] bone"
"16286","(16280) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmr ibn Abān narrated to us — Abū Tumaylah narrated from Yāsar al-Muʿallim, from Yazīd al-Naḥwī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the fingers of the hands and the feet equal. [Ḥasan]"
"16287","(16281) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khayrūyah informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him — I think he said: \In the hand"
"16288","(16282) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us — Saʿīd narrated from Maṭar, from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from Saʿd ibn Hishām, that Zayd ibn Thābit said: \In the fingers"
"16289","(16283) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me — Ibn Luhīʿah informed me — Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from Abī al-Zinād — Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit narrated from his father, that wounds are compensated according to their measure from the full diyah: finger is like finger among the five fingers, with nothing having precedence over anything else. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16290","(16284) He said, and Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Makhramah informed me from his father, who said: I heard Sulaymān ibn Yasār being asked, \How much is the diyah for a toe?\"" He said: \""Ten obligatory camels.\""\n\nBukayr said"
"16291","(16285) As for the hadith which Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān and ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled regarding the thumb: fifteen camels; regarding the one next to it: ten; regarding the middle finger: ten; regarding the one next to the little finger: nine; and regarding the little finger: six. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16292","(16286) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled regarding the fingers: for the thumb, thirteen; for the one next to it, twelve; for the middle finger, ten; for the one next to it, nine; and for the little finger, six — until a document was found in the possession of the family of ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, in which they mentioned that it was from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \And for the fingers therein"
"16293","(16287) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Munqidh al-Khawlānī al-Miṣrī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ informed us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb informed us, Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb informed us that Mūsā ibn Saʿd ibn Zayd ibn Thābit informed him from Abī Ghaṭafān that Ibn ʿAbbās used to say: \For the fingers"
"16294","(16288) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us from Jābir, from al-Shaʿbī, from Sharīḥ, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote: \Indeed"
"16295","(16289) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me, al-Layth narrated to me from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā al-Qurashī, from Makḥūl, that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz wrote to the military districts: \For each phalanx severed from the phalanges of the fingers"
"16296","(16290) Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh narrated from Makḥūl, from Zayd, who said: \For the fingers"
"16297","(16291) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā informed us, Abū Kurayb informed us, Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿUmārah, from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, who said: In the document of ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent him to Najrān, it was written: \For every tooth"
"16298","(16292) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us, Sufyān narrated from Firās, from al-Shaʿbī, from Masrūq, regarding a one-eyed person whose sound eye is struck out: He said, \I did not put out his eye; I am the killer of Allah's slain one therein — half the blood-money.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16299","(16293) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Hushaym informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us from Abī al-Ḍuḥā, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mughaffal — thus he said — regarding a one-eyed person who puts out the eye of a sound-eyed person: He said, \An eye for an eye.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16300","(16294) As for the athar which Abū Ḥāzim informed us of, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Hushaym informed us, Yūnus narrated from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to say regarding a one-eyed person whose eye is put out: \If he wishes"
"16301","(16295) It has also been narrated in this regard from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), and it is a mursal narration. Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to me, ʿUmar ibn Qays informed me from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) gave a ruling concerning a one-eyed man whose eye was gouged out, that he was entitled to the full blood-money (diyah). [Weak]"
"16302","(16296) He said: And Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Ibn Lahīʿah informed me from Jaʿfar from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, a similar narration. [Weak]"
"16303","(16297) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yūnus narrated to us from Ibn Shihāb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib that he said regarding the eye of a one-eyed man, if his remaining eye is gouged out deliberately: the prescribed retaliation (qiṣāṣ) applies; he shall not be subjected to more than having a similar eye taken from him. However, if he accepts the blood-money (ʿaql) for it, then the full blood-money (diyah) is due for it, because it is the remainder of his sight. [Authentic]"
"16304","(16298) He said: And Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me from his father, who said: I heard Sulaymān ibn Yasār being asked about a man who is one-eyed and then his other eye is struck. He said: The blood-money (diyah) is due for it. [Good]"
"16305","(16299) He said: And Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb that he said regarding a one-eyed man who gouges out the eye of a sound man: Ibn Shihāb said: Allah has decreed in His Book that \an eye for an eye\"" [al-Māʾidah 5:45]"
"16306","(16300) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us, Abū Saʿīd al-Rāzī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Hishām narrated to us, Qatādah narrated to us from ʿAbd Rabbih from Abū ʿIyāḍ that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) had a case brought before him concerning a one-eyed man who had gouged out the eye of a sound man, and he did not order retaliation against him; rather, he ruled in the matter that the full blood-money (diyah) be paid.\n\nHe (the author), may Allah have mercy on him, said: The apparent meaning of the Book indicates \an eye for an eye"
"16307","(16301) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Saʿīd — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us, Abū al-Muwajjah narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, Shuʿbah narrated to us from Qatādah, who said: I heard Abā Mijlaz say: I asked ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar about a one-eyed man whose eye is gouged out. ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣafwān said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled in the matter with the blood-money (diyah). I said: I am only asking Ibn ʿUmar. He said: Is he not narrating to you from ʿUmar?\n\nThe apparent meaning of this is that he (ʿUmar) ruled in the matter for the entirety of the blood-money. It may also be possible that he ruled for the blood-money of that eye specifically. And the apparent meaning from Ibn ʿUmar is that he did not hold the view that the full blood-money was obligatory in this case. And Allah knows best. [Authentic]"
"16308","(16302) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd narrated to me, al-Zuhrī narrated to me from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wrote to the people of Yemen a letter in which was: \And for the backbone (ṣulb)"
"16309","(16303) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib informed him: The established Sunnah regarding the blood-money (diyah) has been that for the backbone (ṣulb), the blood-money is due. [Authentic]"
"16310","(16304) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī narrated to us, al-Muḥāribī narrated to us from Ashʿath from al-Zuhrī, who said: It has reached us from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \For the backbone (ṣulb)"
"16311","(16305) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us — Abu al-Tayyib Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Sha'iri narrated to us — Mahmud ibn 'Asam narrated to us — Hafs ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to me — Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated from Bakr ibn Khunays from 'Ubaydah ibn Nusayy from Ibn Ghanim from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The diyah (blood-money) of a woman is half the diyah of a man.\n\nAnd this was also reported through another chain from 'Ubaydah ibn Nusayy, but it contains weakness. [Da'if]"
"16312","(16306) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Muslim ibn Khalid narrated from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar from Ayyub ibn Musa from Ibn Shihab and from Makhul and 'Ata', who said: We found the people upon the view that the diyah of a free Muslim during the era of the Prophet ﷺ was one hundred camels. Then 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, valued that diyah for the people of the cities at one thousand dinars or twelve thousand dirhams. And the diyah of a free Muslim woman, if she was from the people of the cities, was five hundred dinars or six thousand dirhams. And if the one who inflicted the injury was from the Bedouins, then her diyah was fifty camels. And the diyah of a Bedouin woman, if a Bedouin inflicted it upon her, was fifty camels — the Bedouin is not required to pay in gold or silver. [Da'if]"
"16313","(16307) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Ibn Abi Najih from his father: That a man had intercourse with a woman in Makkah and then killed her, so 'Umar ibn 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, decreed eight thousand dirhams and one-third as diyah.\n\nAl-Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, went toward a severe (increased) diyah because he killed her in the Haram. [Da'if]"
"16314","(16308) Abu Hazim, the hafiz, informed us — Abu al-Fadl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us — Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us — Hushaym narrated from al-Shaybani and Ibn Abi Layla and Zakariyya from al-Sha'bi: That 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: The wounds (injuries) of women carry half the diyah of a man, whether the wound is minor or major. [Da'if]"
"16315","(16309) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan — Abu Hanifah narrated from Hammad from Ibrahim from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The 'aqilah (blood-money liability) of a woman is half that of a man, in the case of life (i.e., murder) and what is less than that.\n\nAnd from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, who said: Muhammad ibn Aban informed us — from Hammad — from Ibrahim — from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that they both said: The 'aqilah of a woman is half the diyah of a man, in the case of life and what is less than that.\n\nThe hadith of Ibrahim is munqati' (disconnected), except that it corroborates the narration of al-Sha'bi. [Da'if]"
"16316","(16310) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, narrated to us — Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us — 'Amr narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated — (and in another chain:) the Sharif Abu al-Fath al-'Umar informed us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh informed us — Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi narrated to us — 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd informed us — Shu'bah narrated — from al-Hakam — from al-Sha'bi — from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said: The wounds of men and women are equal up to one-third (of the diyah); whatever exceeds that, the woman's share is half. And Ibn Mas'ud said: Except for the tooth and the mudihah (a wound exposing the bone), for they are equal, and whatever exceeds that is half. And 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: It is half in all matters. And al-Sha'bi said: The statement of 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was the most pleasing to me.\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of al-'Umar. Ibrahim al-Nakha'i also narrated it from Zayd ibn Thabit and Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with both, but both chains are munqati' (disconnected). And Shaqiq narrated it from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, and it is mawsul (connected).\n\n[Sahih from 'Ali and Zayd; munqati' from Ibn Mas'ud]"
"16317","(16311) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to me — Malik, Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi, and Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Rabi'ah: That he asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, \How much is the diyah for a woman's finger?\"" He said: \""Ten (camels).\"" He asked: \""For two?\"" He said: \""Twenty.\"" He asked: \""For three?\"" He said: \""Thirty.\"" He asked: \""For four?\"" He said: \""Twenty.\""\n\nRabi'ah said: When her wound became severe and her affliction intensified"
"16318","(16312) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us — al-Rabi' said: Al-Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: When Ibn al-Musayyib said, \It is the Sunnah"
"16319","(16313) Abu Bakr al-Ardastani, the hafiz, informed us — Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi in Bukhara narrated to us — Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us — 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Darabadjirdi narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from Jabir from al-Sha'bi from Shurayh, who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to me regarding five matters from the reserved properties of the commanders: That the teeth are equal (between men and women), and the fingers are equal; and in the eye of an animal, one-quarter of its price; and that a man is asked about his children at the time of his death — so I shall confirm what is the case at the time of his death; and the wounds of men and women are equal up to one-third of the diyah of a man.\n\nJabir al-Ju'fi is not used as a proof (in hadith), and his wording and ruling have been contradicted. [Da'if]"
"16320","(16314) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us — Hushaym informed us — Mughirah narrated from Ibrahim, who said: Among what 'Urwah al-Bariqi brought to Shurayh from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was: That the fingers are equal — the little finger and the thumb alike; and the wounds of men and women are equal in the case of the tooth and the mudihah (a wound exposing the bone), and other than that is half; and in the eye of an animal, one-quarter of its price; and that the most deserving of a man's conditions to be believed at the time of his death is regarding his child, if he acknowledges him.\n\nMughirah said: And I forgot the fifth until 'Ubaydah reminded me: That if a man divorces his woman with a triple talaq, she inherits from him as long as she is in the 'iddah (waiting period).\n\nAnd in this there is a disconnection (inqita'). And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"
"16321","(16315) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: \In one breast of a woman is half the diyah"
"16322","(16316) He said: And Yūnus informed me from Rabīʿah that he said: \The breast of a woman is a covering for her chest and a nourishment for her child. It holds the status of wealth in terms of richness"
"16323","(16317) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, they said: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us from Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd, al-Zuhrī narrated to me from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen a letter in which was: \And in the two testicles is the diyah"
"16324","(16318) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: \And in the penis is the diyah"
"16325","(16319) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — he is al-Aṣamm — narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab informed him: \The established sunnah regarding blood-money is that in the penis is the diyah"
"16326","(16320) He said: And Ibn Wahb narrated to me, ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Fihrī narrated to me that he heard Zayd ibn Aslam say: \The established sunnah is that in the penis is the diyah"
"16327","(16321) ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah al-Anṣārī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl informed us, Abū Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us from al-Ḥajjāj, from Makhūl, from Zayd ibn Thābit, that he said: \In the two testicles"
"16328","(16322) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl informed us, Abū Shuʿayb narrated to us, ʿAlī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated to us from Qatādah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: \In the left testicle is two-thirds of the diyah"
"16329","(16323) He said: And ʿAbd al-Razzāq ibn Hammām narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, Ibn Abī Najīḥ informed me from Mujāhid, who said: \In the two testicles is the diyah"
"16330","(16324) He said: And Ibn Jurayj informed me. He said: \I said to ʿAṭāʾ: 'The two testicles?' He said: 'In them are fifty in each testicle.'\"" And it has been narrated to us from Masrūq"
"16331","(16325) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashr informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us; Ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ both said: Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: In the case of the nose, if it is entirely severed or its tip (al-arnabah) is cut off, the full blood-money (diyah) is due. The male organ is similar: if it is entirely cut off or its glans (ḥashafah) is severed, the full blood-money is due. And they assigned blood-money for the two testicles, and whichever of the two is afflicted, half the blood-money is due. [Weak]"
"16332","(16326) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd informed us; Sufyān informed us; ʿAwf al-Aʿrābī said: I met a shaykh during the time of the civil wars (al-jamājim) and I asked about him, and it was said: \That is Abū al-Muhallab"
"16333","(16327) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Qatādah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah, from Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: In the case of the eye that remains in its socket but is sightless, the tooth that turns black, and the hand that becomes paralyzed, one-third of their respective blood-money is due."
"16334","(16328) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bukayr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that Zayd ibn Thābit decreed, regarding the eye that remains in its socket but has been extinguished—or he said, has been destroyed—one hundred dinars of blood-money.\n\nMālik said: There is no fixed precedent regarding this matter; rather, it is a matter of ijtihād, and nothing is predetermined. It is possible that the statement of Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him, means that he exercised ijtihād and determined the compensation to be one-fifth of the blood-money.\n\nThe Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: The statement of ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, may carry the same possibility as the statement of Zayd. (Tirmidhī) And it has been narrated from Masrūq that he said: In the case of the eye that is destroyed, the paralyzed hand, and the tongue of the mute person, there is a ruling (ḥukm). And it has been narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī that he said: In the case of the eye that remains in its socket but is sightless, the paralyzed hand, and the tongue of the mute person, there is a ruling of equitable judgment (ḥukūmah ʿadl). [Authentic]"
"16335","(16329) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me; Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, that Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, decreed regarding the eyebrow, if it is injured such that its hair is destroyed, two muḍiḥah (specific wound compensations) — ten camels.\n\nIbn Wahb said: Mālik said to me: In both of them there is ijtihād.\n\nThe Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It is possible that he decreed regarding both eyebrows, if they are injured by a wound that exposes the bone, the compensation of two muḍiḥah, or an equitable judgment (ḥukūmah) amounting to that measure. However, this hadith is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous), and there is no proof in it. [Weak]"
"16336","(16330) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us; Ḥajjāj narrated from Makḥūl, from Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: Regarding hair, if it does not grow back, the blood-money is due. This is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous). And Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh is not used as a proof.\n\nIbn al-Mundhir said: And it has been narrated from Zayd ibn Thābit that he said: In the case of the eyebrow, one-third of the blood-money is due. Ibn al-Mundhir said: Regarding hair that is cut and does not grow back, it has been narrated from ʿAlī and Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that they both said: In it is the full blood-money.\n\nHe said: And what has been narrated from ʿAlī and Zayd is not established. [Weak]"
"16337","(16331) Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked ʿAṭāʾ about the eyebrow being disfigured. He said: I have not heard anything regarding it.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: In it there is an equitable judgment (ḥukūmah) proportionate to the disfigurement and the pain. [Weak]"
"16338","(16332) Through this same chain of narration, al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Muslim ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: Shaving the head — is there a vow (naẓr) associated with it? He said: I do not know. Al-Rabīʿ said: The vow and the amount are one and the same. Al-Shāfiʿī said: In it there is an equitable judgment (ḥukūmah). [Weak]"
"16339","(16333) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me; Mālik and Hishām ibn Saʿd informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyāʾ ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Aslam, the freedman of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, decreed regarding the molar one camel, regarding the collarbone (al-tarqūwah) one camel, and regarding the rib one camel. This is the wording of al-Shāfiʿī's hadith.\n\nAbū Saʿīd added in his narration: Al-Shāfiʿī said: In the case of the molars, five each, because of what has come from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the tooth — five camels — and the molar is a tooth. And I hold the opinion of ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding the collarbone and the rib, because no one among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ opposed him in what I know of, and I do not see any reason to depart from his opinion and oppose him with another view.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib held this same opinion.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said in the book of Injuries (al-Jirāḥ), and Allah knows best: It is possible that what has been narrated from ʿUmar regarding what I have described is an equitable judgment (ḥukūmah) and not a fixed amount determined by precedent. Thus, in every bone of a human being that is broken, other than a tooth, there is an equitable judgment, and in none of these is there a specified compensation (arsh maʿlūm). [Weak]"
"16340","(16334) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb said: And I heard Sufyān al-Thawrī narrate from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah al-Qurashī, from Bishr ibn ʿĀṣim, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, said: In the case of the forearm, if it is broken, two hundred dirhams. And it has been narrated from a man, from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: If the shin or the forearm is broken, then in it are twenty dinars or two ḥiqqah (young she-camels), meaning when it heals without malunion (ʿathm). [Weak]"
"16341","(16335) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisī informed us — Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Ashhabani narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Faris narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us — Abu Nu'aym narrated to us — Ibn Abi Ghanīyah narrated from Ishaq ibn al-Muhtafiz al-A'rabi, from al-Kasir, that he broke a man's shin, and Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) adjudged it at eight camels.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The variance in these narrations indicates that he (Umar) ruled in it by means of a discretionary judgment (hukmah) that reached this amount. [Da'if]"
"16342","(16336) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us — Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to me — 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated from Ibn Shihab, Rabi'ah, and Ibn Abi Farwah, from the writings of Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not establish any diyah for the breaking of a hand in error except the compensatory payment (jābr) — and if it heals straight and there is no defect or anything for which a valuation is set, then the one who broke it must pay that amount. [Da'if]"
"16343","(16337) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Raffa' informed us — Abu 'Amr 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Bashir narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Abi Uways and 'Isa ibn Myna narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated that his father said: Those of our fuqahā' whom I reached and whose opinions are authoritative used to say: Every bone that is broken accidentally and then heals straight, without deficiency or defect — there is in that nothing except the payment to the one who treats it (al-mudāwī) and the like thereof. But if something of it heals with a defect or a deficiency, then it is according to the extent of that blemish and its defect; those of sound judgment and discernment shall assess it, and compensation shall be affixed according to what they determine. And they said the same regarding the mulṭā'i wound and every wound in the body if it heals without defect — they saw in that nothing except the payment to the one who treats it and the like thereof. [Da'if]"
"16344","(16338) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Fudayl ibn Iyyad narrated from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir — from Thabit al-Haddad — from Ibn al-Musayyib: that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled that the diyah of the Jew and the Christian was four thousand (dirhams), and the diyah of the Magian was eight hundred dirhams. [Sahih]"
"16345","(16339) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, who said: We sent to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib asking him about the diyah of the mu'āhid (non-Muslim under treaty). He said: 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled it at four thousand. We said: And who ruled before him? He pelted us (with stones).\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: They were those who asked him last.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) to the contrary, through two chains of narration — one of which is not preserved (mahfūz) and the other is munqati' (disconnected) — both of which we have mentioned in the chapter \A believer shall not be killed for a disbeliever.\"" [Sahih]"""
"16346","(16340) Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Musa ibn al-Fadl narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Abi al-Miqdam — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled that the diyah of the Magian was eight hundred dirhams. [Sahih]"
"16347","(16341) He said: And Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Jarir ibn Hazim narrated — from Qays ibn Sa'd — from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, who said: The diyah of the Magian is eight hundred dirhams. [Sahih]"
"16348","(16342) He said: And Ibn Wahb narrated to me — 'Umar ibn Qays narrated — from 'Ata' — from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr — from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding that. He said: And the Magian woman — four hundred dirhams — from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: And Malik told me the same. [Sahih]"
"16349","(16343) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Ibn Lahi'ah narrated — from Yazid ibn Abi Habib — from Ibn Shihab: that 'Ali and Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: The diyah of the Magian is eight hundred dirhams.\n\nAnd that has been narrated from Ibn Lahi'ah through another chain of his, raised (mawdu'an). [Da'if]"
"16350","(16344) Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us — 'Isa ibn Ahmad al-Sadafi narrated to us — 'Allan ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us — Abu Salih narrated — Ibn Lahi'ah narrated — from Yazid ibn Abi Habib — from Abi al-Khayr — from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The diyah of the Magian is eight hundred dirhams.\n\nAbu Salih, the scribe of Layth, was alone in narrating it. And the first (narration) is more likely to be the preserved one, and Allah knows best. [Da'if]"
"16351","(16345) As for the hadith which Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan — and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us, Usāmah ibn Zayd informed us from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The blood-money (ʿaql) of a disbeliever is half the blood-money of a believer.\"" [Ḥasan for other than this chain]"""
"16352","(16346) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated us from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"
"16353","(16347) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us, Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: \The value of the blood-money (diyah) at the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was eight hundred dinars"
"16354","(16348) And that which confirms this is what Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me — ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb informed me — that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) imposed upon every Muslim who killed a man from among the People of the Scripture the payment of four thousand (dirhams). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16355","(16349) And as for what Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-ʿAnbarī narrated to me, Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Abū Saʿd al-Baqqāl, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made the blood-money of the two ʿĀmirī men equal to the blood-money of a free Muslim"
"16356","(16350) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-Asfāṭī — meaning al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl — narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Abū Bakr narrated it with his chain, except that he said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made the blood-money of those under covenant (al-muʿāhadayn) equal to the blood-money of a Muslim.\"" Now"
"16357","(16351) And al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah narrated it from al-Ḥakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) compensated two polytheists from among the People of the Covenant with the blood-money of two free Muslims"
"16358","(16352) And as for what ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us, Abū Kurz informed us from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The blood-money of a dhimmī is the blood-money of a Muslim.\"" And other than him narrated from ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd: \""He compensated a dhimmī with the blood-money of a Muslim.\"" [Mawḍūʿ]"""
"16359","(16353) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, they both said: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \This Abū Kurz is abandoned in hadith (matrūl al-ḥadīth)"
"16360","(16354) And as for what Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Shaybānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Ibn Jurayj narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: \The blood-money of the Jew and the Christian in the time of the Prophet (ﷺ) was the same as the blood-money of a Muslim"
"16361","(16355) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us — Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah — from al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whoever has a covenant (of protection) or is a Dhimmi (non-Muslim under protection), his blood-money is the blood-money of a Muslim. This hadith is munqati' (disconnected) and mawquf (stopping at the Companion)."
"16362","(16356) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from al-Zuhri — from Ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The blood-money (diyah) of a slave is in accordance with his price. [Sahih]"
"16363","(16357) And Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us — Abu al-'Abbas informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Yahya ibn Hassān narrated from al-Layth ibn Sa'd —\n\n(And in another chain:) And Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us — Yunus and al-Layth informed me from Ibn Shihab — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who used to say: The blood-money of a slave is in accordance with his price, just as the blood-money of a free person is in accordance with his blood-money.\n\nIbn Shihab said: And there were some men who said otherwise — he is merely a commodity that is appraised. This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Wahb."
"16364","(16358) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb said — and Makhrah ibn Bukayr informed me from his father, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Jabir saying — I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: When a slave receives a wound that exposes the bone (mudihah), he is entitled to one-twentieth of his price therein. And Sulayman ibn Yasar said the same. And this is the meaning of the statement of Shurayh, al-Sha'bi, and al-Nakha'i. [Da'if]"
"16365","(16359) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us — they said: Abu 'Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us — Waki' narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn, Abu Malik al-Nakha'i — from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar — from 'Amir — from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: (Cases of) deliberate killing, a slave, a settlement, and a confession — the 'aqilah (paternal relatives liable for blood-money) do not bear responsibility for them. Thus he narrated from 'Amir from 'Umar, and it is munqati' (disconnected) from 'Umar. What is preserved (al-mahfuz) is from 'Amir al-Sha'bi as his own statement. [Da'if]"
"16366","(16360) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us — Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Karzi narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated from Mutarrif — from al-Sha'bi, who said: The 'aqilah does not bear responsibility for deliberate killing, nor for a slave, nor for a settlement, nor for a confession.\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: They differed regarding the interpretation of his statement \nor for a slave.\"" Muhammad ibn al-Hasan said to me: Its meaning is that if a slave kills a free person"
"16367","(16361) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asam narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated from his father, who said: A trustworthy narrator narrated to me from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas that he said: The 'aqilah does not bear responsibility for deliberate killing, nor for a settlement, nor for a confession, nor for what a slave has committed. He said: And al-Layth said the same, except if they so wish. [Da'if]"
"16368","(16362) And Abu Sa'id informed us — Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us — Bahr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Malik ibn Anas narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah — from his father, who said: The 'aqilah is not liable for the blood-money of one who kills deliberately, except if they so wish. Rather, what is upon them is (the blood-money for) accidental killing. [Sahih]"
"16369","(16363) He said: And Malik ibn Anas informed me from Ibn Shihab, who said: The established sunnah has been that the 'aqilah does not bear anything of the blood-money for deliberate killing, unless the 'aqilah willingly assist out of their own volition.\n\nMalik said: And Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated the same to me.\n\nYahya said: And I did not find the people except upon that. [Sahih]"
"16370","(16364) Abu al-Hasan al-Raffa' informed us — 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Bashir narrated to us — Isma'il al-Qadi narrated to us — Ibn Abi Uways and 'Isa ibn Myna narrated to us — they said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated from his father — from the jurists among the people of Madinah, who used to say: The 'aqilah does not bear responsibility for that which is deliberate, nor for a settlement, nor for a confession, nor for what a slave has committed, unless they do so willingly and of their own accord. [Da'if]"
"16371","(16365) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us — Yazid ibn Iyad informed me — from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Ubayd — from Mujahid ibn Jabrb — from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to say: The master is not liable for anything on behalf of his slave beyond the slave's own self, even if the wound sustained is greater than the price of the slave, no increase shall be added to it.\n\nAnd it has been reported to us from the jurists of the Tabi'in, 'Urwa ibn al-Zubayr and others. [Da'if]"
"16372","(16366) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us — Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us — my father narrated to me — from Qatada — from Abu Nadra — from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that a slave belonging to some poor people cut off the ear of a slave belonging to some wealthy people. His family came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16373","(16367) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzaki and Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr — said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us — Yunus informed me — from Ibn Shihab — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salama ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — that Abu Hurayra said: Two women of Hudhayl quarrelled, and one of them struck the other with a stone, killing her and what was in her womb. They brought the dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the diya for her unborn child was a ghurra — a male or female slave — and he ruled that the diya for the woman was upon her 'aqila, and he bequeathed her inheritance to her children and her husband and those with them. Hammal ibn al-Nabigha al-Hudhali said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16374","(16368) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu 'Uthman — Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdan and Abu Sadiq Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fawaris al-'Attar — said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Abu al-Bakhtari — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated to us — Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us — Mufaddl ibn Muhalhal narrated to us — from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir — from Ibrahim — from 'Ubayd ibn Nudayla — from al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, that a woman killed her co-wife with a tent pole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought regarding the matter, and he ruled upon her 'aqila for the diya. She was pregnant, so he ruled for the unborn child a ghurra. Some of her 'asaba said: \Shall we compensate one who did not eat"
"16375","(16369) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us — Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us — from Ibn Ishaq — 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn al-Akhnas ibn Shurayq narrated to me: I took this book from the family of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, which was bound with the book of sadaqah that 'Umar wrote for the tax collectors: \In the name of Allah"
"16376","(16370) Kathir ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf narrated from his father from his grandfather that he said: \In the book of the Prophet ﷺ it was: 'Every group shall ransom its captives with justice and equity among the believers"
"16377","(16371) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us — al-Layth informed me — that Ibn Shihab narrated to him — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab — from Abu Hurayra, that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding the unborn child of a woman of Banu Lihyan, who was stillborn, a ghurra — a male or female slave. Then the woman upon whom the ghurra was imposed died, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that her inheritance was for her children and her husband, and that the 'aqila (blood-money liability) was upon her 'asaba. Al-Bukhari and Muslim both narrated it in the Sahih from the hadith of al-Layth."
"16378","(16372) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Faddl al-Qattan in Baghdad narrated to us — Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us — (and) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us — they both said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us — Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us — from al-Zuhri — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab — from Abu Hurayra, who said: Two women of Hudhayl disputed, and one of them cast out the unborn child of her companion. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled upon her a ghurra — a male or female slave. The one upon whom the ruling was imposed said: \How shall I bear the liability of one who did not drink"
"16379","(16373) Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad al-'Attar in Baghdad narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Saliman al-Faqih narrated to us — 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad narrated to us — Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us — 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us — Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to me — al-Sha'bi narrated to me — from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, that two women of Hudhayl killed one another, and each of them had a husband and children. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the diya of the slain woman the responsibility of the 'aqila of the killer woman, and he acquitted her husband and children. The 'aqila of the slain woman said: \Her inheritance is for us.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Her inheritance is for her husband and children.\"" And she was pregnant"
"16380","(16374) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, and he mentioned it with a similar meaning. [Da'if]"
"16381","(16375) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Ansari informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us — Shayban narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us — Sulayman ibn Musa narrated from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) decreed that the blood-money (diyah) of a woman is the responsibility of her 'asabah (paternal relatives) — those who do not inherit from her anything except what exceeds the share of her other heirs. And if she kills someone, her blood-money is upon her heirs, and they are the ones who may execute her killer. [Hasan]"
"16382","(16376) And Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Ansari informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us — al-'Abbas ibn Yazid narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar informed us from a man who heard 'Ikrimah narrate from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace be upon him). 'Abd al-Razzaq said: The name of this man is 'Amr Barq. He said: The 'asabah (paternal relatives) of a woman bear the responsibility for her blood-money, and they do not inherit except what exceeds the share of her other heirs.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: And 'Umar ibn al-Khattab decreed against 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the blood-money for the mawali of Safiyyah bint 'Abd al-Muttalib be borne by him, and he awarded the inheritance to al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him), because he was her son. [Da'if]"
"16383","(16377) Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Ansari informed us — Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us — Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us — 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from Hammad, from Ibrahim: that al-Zubayr and 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) disputed regarding the mawali of Safiyyah before 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), so he awarded the inheritance to al-Zubayr and placed the obligation of the blood-money upon 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both). And it is narrated from al-Hasan that 'Umar said to 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding a crime committed by 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): \I adjure you by Allah to divide the blood-money among the sons of your father.\"" So he divided it among Quraysh. [Da'if]"""
"16384","(16378) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Raffa' informed us — Abu 'Amr — 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Bashir narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us — Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated from his father, from the jurists (fuqaha') among the Tabi'un of the people of Madinah — Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and others — who used to say: When a woman gives birth among a people other than her own, her children inherit from her, and her people ('asabah) bear the responsibility for her blood-money. Her mawlā (freed slave) has that same status — her inheritance goes to her children, and the blood-money for any injury she commits falls upon her people. [Sahih]"
"16385","(16379) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan informed us — Ishaq ibn Ahmad narrated to us — al-Bukhari narrated to us — (h) — and Ibn Hayyan informed us — Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us — 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us — both saying: Abu 'Asim narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj narrated to us — Ibn al-Zubayr narrated from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Upon every womb (i.e."
"16386","(16380) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Rafi' narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ibn Jurayj informed me — Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah saying: The Prophet (peace be upon him) wrote: \Upon every womb is its blood-money.\"" Then he wrote: \""It is not permissible for a mawlā of a Muslim man to be taken as a patron (wali) without his permission.\"" Then I was informed that he cursed in a written document the one who did that.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi'.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) decreed the obligation of blood-money upon the 'asabah"
"16387","(16381) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Saydalani narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us — Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated to us — Sa'id ibn Yazid narrated to us — Abu Nadrah narrated to us — from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who said: The first one to establish the military registers (dīwān) and to organize the 'urafā' (heads of tribal groups) was 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). [Sahih]"
"16388","(16382) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us — 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us — Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us — 'Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us — Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali narrated from his father, who said: Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah married two women — one from Banu Mu'awiyah and the other from Banu Lahyan. The one from Banu Lahyan was struck and she died, and she miscarried a fetus. So Hamal ibn Malik came to her father and said: \The blood-money of my wife and my son.\"" Her father said: \""Only her sons bear the responsibility for her blood-money"
"16389","(16383) And Abu Bakr al-Ansari al-Faqih informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us — Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Umran ibn Hayyaj narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us — al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us — Salamah ibn Tamam, who was Abu 'Abd Allah al-Shaqari, narrated to us — from Abu al-Malih, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was brought to two women who were with a man from Hudhayl. He mentioned the hadith and in it said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16390","(16384) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us — Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us — Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me — from al-Zuhri — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: that Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The 'asabah do not bear the blood-money, nor does the blood-money encompass them, except in one-third of the diyah and above.\n\nThus did Ayyub narrate it, and the well-preserved (mahfūz) version is that it is the statement of Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Sulayman ibn Yasar. [Da'if]"
"16391","(16385) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, and he said: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed me from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Sulaymān ibn Yasār that they both said: \The ʿāqilah (blood-money collective) does not bear more than one-third of the diyah (blood-money)"
"16392","(16386) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us, Manṣūr informed me, he said: Ibrāhīm narrated to me from ʿUbayd ibn Nuḍaylah from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah that a man from Hudhayl had two wives, and one of them struck the other with a tent pole, causing her to miscarry. It was said: \What about one who neither ate"
"16393","(16387) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that the ghurrah (compensation for a fetus) is valued at fifty dīnārs or six hundred dirhams. [Sound]"
"16394","(16388) Abū Saʿīd al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, he said: Al-Shāfiʿī said: \Some of them said that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said: 'It is the ancient practice (al-amr al-qadīm) that the ʿāqilah bears one-third and above.'\"" We said: \""The 'ancient' may refer to one whose practice is followed and whose statement is binding"
"16395","(16389) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, he said: \We found it generally held among the people of knowledge that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of the accidental killing of a free Muslim by a free man one hundred camels upon the ʿāqilah of the killer"
"16396","(16390) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to me from al-Ashʿath ibn Sawwār from ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī, who said: \ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"
"16397","(16391) Abū Saʿīd narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Baḥr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to me from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, ruled that the ʿaql (blood-money) in the case of accidental killing is payable over three years. And from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd: \It is the established practice (al-sunnah) that the diyah be paid in installments over three years.\"" [Weak]"""
"16398","(16392) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and ʿAbdullāh ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik informed me. Abū Dāwūd said: Aḥmad said — thus said Ibn Wahb, and ʿAnbasah, meaning Ibn Khālid. Aḥmad said: \The correct version is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdullāh\"" — that Salamah ibn al-Akwāʿ said: \""On the day of Khaybar"
"16399","(16393) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Hishām ibn Khālid narrated to us, al-Walīd narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Salām from his father from his grandfather Abī Salām from a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \We raided a clan of Juhaynah"
"16400","(16394) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq — informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, al-Layth narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Abī Salamah and Ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \The injury caused by the beast is without liability (jubār)"
"16401","(16395) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammādābādhī narrated to us; Abū Qilābah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad and Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar both said: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The injury caused by a beast is without liability (jubār)"
"16402","(16396) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Mughīrah, from Ibrāhīm, that a mule fell into a well and broke. The people disputed before Shurayḥ. ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith said: \O Abū Umayyah"
"16403","(16397) As for the ḥadīth: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah, Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ, and Abū ʿAwānah—all of them—narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Ḥanash ibn al-Muʿtamir al-Kinānī, who narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to Yemen"
"16404","(16398) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhb al-Wāsiṭī narrated in Wāsiṭ; Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Muṣʿab ibn al-Miqdām narrated to us; Isrāʾīl narrated from Simāk, from Ḥanash ibn al-Muʿtamir al-Kinānī, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to Yemen.\"" Then he mentioned this story. Then ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Gather from the tribes who were present: a quarter of the diyah"
"16405","(16399) Al-Bukhārī said: \Ḥanash ibn al-Muʿtamir—some of them said Ibn Rabīʿah—they speak critically of his ḥadīth.\"" Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī said: \""I heard Ibn Ḥammād mention it from al-Bukhārī.\"" Our companions say: The qiyās (analogical reasoning) is that for the first"
"16406","(16400) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal informed us; Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from Khilāṣ ibn ʿAmr, that a man hired four people to dig a well. A portion of it collapsed upon a man and he died. This was raised to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) assigned three-quarters of the diyah upon the three and waived the quarter—the share of the deceased. The aḥādīth of Khilāṣ from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) are not used as proof due to their being munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And this is upon their ʿāqilah, if the collapse of the portion was caused by their action. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16407","(16401) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Abī ʿUbayd; Ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from Mujālid ibn Saʿīd, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he judged in the case of the qāriṣah (the one who pinched), the qāmiṣah (the one who caused to startle), and the wāqiṣah (the one who broke her neck) with the diyah divided into thirds. Ibn Abī Zāʾidah said: Its explanation is that three young girls were playing. One of them mounted upon her companion, and the third pinched the one being mounted, so she startled, and the rider fell and her neck was broken. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) assigned one-third of the diyah upon the qāriṣah, one-third upon the qāmiṣah, and waived the third, saying: \Because it is the share of the rider"
"16408","(16402) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Ismāʿīl al-Maḥāmilī narrated to us; Zayd ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us; Mūsā ibn ʿUlayy ibn Rabāḥ al-Lakhmī said: I heard my father saying: \Indeed a blind man used to recite poetry during the season (of Hajj) in the caliphate of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"
"16409","(16403) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me; Mālik ibn Anas (ḥ). And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik (ḥ). And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that two women from Hudhayl threw stones at one another, and one of them struck the other, causing her to miscarry her child. The Prophet (ﷺ) judged regarding it a ghurrah—a male or female slave. In the ḥadīth of al-Shāfiʿī: a ghurrah—a male slave or a young female slave. And similarly in the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb. Ibn Wahb added in his narration: \Two women from Hudhayl during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf and others from Mālik. And Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16410","(16404) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid (ḥ). And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿUfayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Khālid ibn Musāfir narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged in the case of two women from Hudhayl who fought with each other. One of them threw a stone at the other, striking her abdomen while she was pregnant, and she killed the child in her womb. They disputed before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that the diyah for what was in her womb was a ghurrah—a male or female slave. The guardian of the woman who was fined said: \How can I be fined"
"16411","(16405) 'Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar reported on the authority of al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nTwo women from Hudhayl fought, and one of them struck the other with a stone, hitting her belly, killing her, and causing her to deliver a stillborn child. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed that the blood-money (diyah) for the woman be paid by the 'aqilah (paternal relatives liable for blood-money) of the other woman, and for the foetus a ghurrah — a male or female slave. A person said: \How do we pay blood-money for one who neither ate"
"16412","(16406) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Birti narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: al-Layth narrated.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Adhan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: 'Ubayd ibn Sharik and Ibn Milhan both said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us: al-Layth narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed regarding the foetus of a woman from Banu Lihyan a ghurrah — a male or female slave. Then the woman upon whom the ghurrah was decreed passed away, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed that her inheritance go to her children and her husband, and that the blood-money ('aql) be upon her 'asabah (paternal relatives).\n\nThe wording is that of Qutaybah's hadith. In the narration of Ibn Bukayr: \regarding the foetus of a woman from Banu Kinanah that was delivered dead.\"" And in the narration of al-Tayalisi: \""A woman from Banu Lihyan struck another who was pregnant"
"16413","(16407) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Malik ibn Anas reported, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed regarding a foetus killed in its mother's womb a ghurrah — a male or female slave. The one against whom the judgment was made said: \How can I pay a fine for one who neither drank"
"16414","(16408) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad: Abu Ahmad Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Rawh narrated to us: 'Utham ibn 'Umar narrated to us: Yunus reported, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said:\n\nTwo women from Hudhayl fought, and one of them struck the other, killing her and what was in her womb. They disputed regarding the blood-money and brought the matter before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He decreed that the blood-money for her foetus was a ghurrah — a male or female slave — and he decreed her blood-money upon her 'aqilah, and he assigned her inheritance to her children and those with them. Hamal ibn Nabighah al-Hudhali said: \How do I pay a fine for one who neither drank"
"16415","(16409) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan, and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq all said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Sufyan reported, from 'Amr ibn Dinar and Ibn Tawus, from Tawus, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said:\n\n\I remind Allah of any man who heard something from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the foetus.\"" Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah stood up and said: \""I was between two of my wives — that is"
"16416","(16410) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mas'ud al-Masisi informed us: Abu 'Asim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj: 'Amr ibn Dinar informed me — he heard Tawus narrating from Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), that he asked about the Prophet's (peace and blessings be upon him) ruling in that matter. Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah stood up and said: \I was between two women"
"16417","(16411) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Waki' narrated.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Waki' narrated to us: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said:\n\n'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) sought counsel regarding a woman's miscarriage. Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decree regarding it a ghurrah — a male or female slave.\"" He said: \""Bring me someone who can testify with you.\"" So Muhammad ibn Salamah testified.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih]"""
"16418","(16412) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Wuhaib narrated, from Hisham, from his father, from al-Mughirah, from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), with the same meaning.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il."
"16419","(16413) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us by dictation: al-Hasan ibn 'Imran al-Qadi in Harat informed us: Abu Hatim 'Abd al-Jalil ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated, from his father, that 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the people: \Who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decree anything regarding the miscarried foetus?\"" Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decree regarding it a ghurrah — a male or female slave.\"" He said: \""Bring someone who can testify with you regarding this.\"" Muhammad ibn Salamah said: \""I testify regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to the same effect.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa"
"16420","(16414) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Jarir narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from 'Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, who said:\n\nA woman struck her co-wife with a tent pole, killing her and what was in her womb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made the blood-money for the slain woman the responsibility of the 'asabah of the female killer, and a ghurrah for what was in her womb. A man from the 'asabah of the killer said: \Shall we pay blood-money for one who neither ate"
"16421","(16415) Abu al-Qasim Zayd ibn Abi Hashim al-'Alawi in Kufah and Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Najjar al-Muqri' therein both narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Ghurzah narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Hammad narrated to us, from Asbat, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said:\n\nThere were two co-wives between whom there was enmity. One of them struck the other with a stone, and she miscarried a boy whose hair had already grown, and he was dead. The woman also died. The Prophet ﷺ decreed the payment of blood-money (diyah) from the 'aqilah (the responsible kin) of the perpetrator. The uncle of the slain woman said: \She has miscarried"
"16422","(16416) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Razi narrated to us: 'Isa, i.e. ibn Yunus, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed for the unborn child (janin) a ghurrah: a slave or a maidservant, or a horse or a mule.\n\nAbu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah and Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, but they did not mention \a horse\"" or \""a mule.\""\n\nThe Shaykh al-Faqih"
"16423","(16417) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Farisi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Abbad narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father:\n\nThat 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, sought counsel, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed the diyah for the woman, and for the unborn child (janin) a ghurrah: a slave or a maidservant, or a horse. This is how he narrated it as a mursal (disconnected) hadith. [Da'if]"
"16424","(16418) 'Amr ibn Dinari narrated it from Tawus, making it a statement of Tawus. It was narrated to us by Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri': al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinari, from Tawus:\n\nThat 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, asked the people about the unborn child (janin), and he mentioned the hadith. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed for the unborn child a ghurrah. Tawus said: \The horse is a ghurrah.\"""""
"16425","(16419) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: 'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-'Azim narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Subayh narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father:\n\nThat a woman threw a stone at another woman and she miscarried. This was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he decreed for her child five hundred sheep, and he prohibited on that day from throwing stones (al-khadf).\n\nAbu Dawud said: In the hadith it is \five hundred"
"16426","(16420) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas informed me, from Ibn Shihab, regarding a man who struck his wife or his concubine and she cast forth what was in her womb. Ibn Shihab said: For her child there is a ghurrah, and upon him (the perpetrator) there is an expiation (kaffarah). [Sahih — from al-Zuhri]"
"16427","(16421) He said: And 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, regarding a woman who was struck and miscarried three (children). Ibn Shihab said: We are of the opinion that for each one of them there is a ghurrah, and we are of the opinion that for every unborn child that is confirmed to be a pregnancy, there is a ghurrah.\n\nYunus said: And Ibn Shihab said regarding a pregnant woman whom a man struck and she died while she was pregnant: For her (the woman) there is the full diyah, and for her unborn child that was with her, when it perishes by her perishing, there is no diyah, and we do not know of any prior ruling (qada') concerning this.\n\nMalik said the same. And Ibn al-Mundhir narrated the expiation (kaffarah) for the unborn child from 'Ata', al-Hasan, and al-Nakha'i. [Sahih — from al-Zuhri]"
"16428","(16422) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Raffa' narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from the fuqaha' (jurists) among the Tabi'un of the people of Madinah, who used to say:\n\nRegarding a man who strikes a woman and she casts forth her unborn child: if it is born dead, then for it there is a ghurrah; and if it is born alive and then dies, then for it there is the full diyah. And they used to say: Whoever kills a pregnant woman, there is no blood-money ('aql) for what is in her womb; the blood-money is for the slain woman, and there is no (separate) unborn child in her womb. [Da'if]"
"16429","(16423) And it has been narrated to us from Hajjaj ibn Artat, from Makhul, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said:\n\nWhen the miscarried child is born alive, its diyah is complete, whether it cried (istahalla) or did not cry. This is from what I was informed of, from Zahir, from al-Baghawi, from Ahmad, from al-'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam, from Hajjaj, and in it there is a break (inqiṭa') in the chain. [Da'if]"
"16430","(16424) And regarding the expiation (kaffarah), what was narrated to us by 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah, Ahmad ibn Muhammad, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-Ayli narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nQays ibn 'Asim al-Tamimi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \I buried alive eight daughters in the Jahiliyyah.\"" He said: \""Free a soul (nasamah) for each one of them.\"" And there is a corroborating witness for this from another source. [Da'if]"""
"16431","(16425) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — recitation — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah al-Shaybānī informed us in Kūfah; al-Haytham ibn Khālid informed us; Abū Nuʿaym informed us; Qays narrated from al-Agharr ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ from Khalīfah ibn Ḥuṣayn from Qays ibn ʿĀṣim: that he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \I buried alive twelve or thirteen of my daughters during the Jāhiliyyah.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"
"16432","(16426) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah; Abū al-Walīd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim informed us; Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān from Layth from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab: that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) shouted at a woman and she miscarried. So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) paid a ghurrah (as blood money). Its chain is disconnected. [Weak]"
"16433","(16427) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us; Mālik and Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from Rabīʿah, that it reached him: that the ghurrah is valued at fifty dinārs or six hundred dirhams; the blood money (diyah) of a woman is five hundred dinārs or six thousand dirhams; and the blood money of her foetus is one-tenth of her blood money. Mālik said: \We are of the opinion that the blood money of the foetus of a slave-woman is one-tenth of the value of her mother.\"" [Sound]"""
"16434","(16428) It is narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) through a disconnected chain that he valued the ghurrah at fifty dinārs. Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah; Abū al-Walīd informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) valued the ghurrah at fifty dinārs. [Weak]"
"16435","(16429) Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī, and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed a ghurrah for the foetus of a free woman"
"16436","(16430) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik ibn Anas informed us.\n\n(And) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī al-ʿAdl informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik informed us; Abū Laylā ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl narrated from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah that he was informed by men from the elders of his people — and in the narration of al-Shāfiʿī: \that he and men from the elders of his people informed him\"" — that ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl and Muḥayyiṣah set out for Khaybar when a hardship had befallen them. They separated to attend to their needs. Muḥayyiṣah came and reported that ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl had been killed and thrown into a well or a spring. He went to the Jews and said"
"16437","(16431) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Bishr ibn Yassār from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah: that ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl and Muḥayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd set out for Khaybar. They separated to attend to their needs, and ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl was killed. He (Muḥayyiṣah), along with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān the brother of the deceased, and Ḥuwayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned to him the killing of ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \Will you swear fifty oaths and thereby establish the right to your companion's killer or your companion?\"" They said"
"16438","(16432) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān and Aḥmad ibn Salamah said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us; al-Layth narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Bishr ibn Yassār from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah — Yaḥyā said, and I think he said — and from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, that both of them said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl ibn Zayd and Muḥayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd ibn Zayd set out until they reached Khaybar. They separated there for some of their affairs. Then Muḥayyiṣah found ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl killed. He buried him and then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, along with Ḥuwayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl, who was the youngest of the group. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān went to speak before his two companions. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \Kabbar\"" — meaning seniority in age. So he fell silent"
"16439","(16433) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Muthannā informed us; Musaddad informed us.\n\n(And) Abū al-Walīd informed me; Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Ṣūfī informed us; ʿUbaydullāh al-Qawārīrī informed us. Both said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī narrated from Bishr ibn Yassār from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl and Muḥayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd ibn Zayd set out for Khaybar, which at that time was under a treaty. They separated to attend to their needs. Muḥayyiṣah came upon ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl while he was weltering in his blood, killed. He buried him and then came to Madīnah. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl, Muḥayyiṣah, and Ḥuwayyiṣah, the two sons of Masʿūd, set out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān went to speak. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \Kabbar al-kubr\"" — and he was the youngest of the group. So he fell silent"
"16440","(16434) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us.\n\n(And) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Maysarah and Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd — both with the same meaning — said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Bishr ibn Yassār from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah and Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj: that Muḥayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd and ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl set out towards Khaybar. They separated among the palm trees, and ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl was killed. They accused the Jews. His brother ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl and his cousins Ḥuwayyiṣah and Muḥayyiṣah came to the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān spoke regarding the matter of his brother, though he was the youngest of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \Al-kubr"
"16441","(16435) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us — Ibn Abī Uways informed me — my father informed me — from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, that Bashīr ibn Yasār, the mawlā of the Banū Ḥārithah, the Anṣārīs, informed him. He was an elderly, venerable man who had met people from the household of his own people, the Banū Ḥārithah, who were Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, among them Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathamah, and Suwayd ibn al-Nuʿmān. They informed him that the practice of qasāmah (the collective oath) existed among them in the case of the Banū Ḥārithah ibn al-Ḥārith, regarding a man from the Anṣār called ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl, who was killed at Khaybar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \Will you swear fifty oaths so that you may claim your killer?\"" — or he said: \""your companion?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"
"16442","(16436) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us — al-Ḥumaydī informed us — Sufyān informed me — Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd heard Bashīr ibn Yasār from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathamah, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl was found slain in one of the wells of Khaybar. His brother, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl, and his paternal unḥuwayṣah and Muḥayyiṣah, came to him. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān went to speak before the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \The eldest"
"16443","(16437) It is mentioned regarding Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah that which indicates he did not narrate this narration with the precision of those narrators. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated from Ibn ʿUyaynah following the ḥadīth of al-Thaqafī, then said: \Except that Ibn ʿUyaynah did not establish whether the Prophet ﷺ gave precedence to the Anṣārīs in the oaths or to the Jews. In the ḥadīth it is stated that he gave precedence to the Anṣārīs"
"16444","(16438) As for the ḥadīth which Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī informed us — Abū Nuʿaym informed us — (ḥ) and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us — Abū Nuʿaym informed us — Saʿīd informed us — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAmr, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Adīb al-Bisṭāmī, informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us — Ibn Abī Shaybah informed us — Abū Nuʿaym informed us — from Saʿīd ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭāʾī, from Bashīr ibn Yasār, who claimed that a man from the Anṣār called Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathamah informed him: \A group of his people set out for Khaybar and became separated there"
"16445","(16439) And as for the ḥadīth which Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us — Yūnus ibn Bukayr informed us — from Ibn Isḥāq — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī informed me — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bujayd ibn Qayẓī, the brother of the Banū Ḥārithah. Ibn Ibrāhīm said: \By Allah"
"16446","(16440) For Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī said: \And from the book of ʿUmar ibn Ḥabīb"
"16447","(16441) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed him — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī informed us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar informed us — from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from men among the Anṣār, that the Prophet ﷺ said to the Jews and began with them: \Let fifty men among you swear an oath.\"" They refused. So he said to the Anṣār: \""Establish your claim (by oath).\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"
"16448","(16442) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him — Abū ʿAmr al-Ḥīrī informed me — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us — Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ informed us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed me — Ibn Jurayj informed me — Ibn Shihāb informed me — Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Sulaymān ibn Yasār informed me — from a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ affirmed the qasāmah (collective oath) as it was in the Jāhiliyyah (pre-Islamic period), and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged by it between people of the Anṣār regarding a slain man whom they claimed was killed by the Jews. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ, and he also extracted it from the ḥadīth of Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān and Yūnus ibn Yazīd from Ibn Shihāb, except that the ḥadīth of Yūnus is abridged. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16449","(16443) And ʿUqayl narrated it, as Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us — Ibn Milḥān informed us — Yaḥyā, that is, ibn Bukayr, informed us — al-Layth informed us — from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from people among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that the qasāmah in the Jāhiliyyah was for the blood (i.e., for murder). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ affirmed it as it was in the Jāhiliyyah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged by it between people of the Anṣār from the Banū Ḥārithah, who claimed that the Jews had killed him."
"16450","(16444) And Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated it from ʿUqayl and others, as Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Razzāz informed us in Baghdad — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Shāfiʿī informed us — ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us — Ibn Abī Maryam informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed me — ʿUqayl, and Qurratah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and Ibn Jurayj informed me — from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: \The established sunnah (practice) regarding the qasāmah is that fifty men shall swear fifty oaths. If even one of them refuses (nakala)"
"16451","(16445) And our companions cited what Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdad — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us — ʿAbadah ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us — al-Zanjī narrated from Ibn Jurayj — from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb — from his father — from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The proof (al-bayyinah) lies upon the claimant"
"16452","(16446) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us — Muslim ibn Khālid, who is al-Zanjī, narrated it with the same. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16453","(16447) As for the ḥadīth which ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — ʿĀṣim ibn Yūsuf al-Yarbūʿī narrated to us in Banī Ḥarām — Salām ibn Sulaym, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ, narrated — from al-Kalbī — from Abī Ṣāliḥ — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \A man from the Anṣār was found slain in a territory of a people from the Jews. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to them and took from them fifty of their leading men. He made them swear by Allah: 'We did not kill him"
"16454","(16448) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us — Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us — Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿAlī — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Bakr al-Ḥafīd narrated to us — Hārūn ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrating from Sufyān, who said: \Al-Kalbī said to me"
"16455","(16449) As for the athar which Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Abū ʿAwanah narrated — from Mughīrah — from ʿĀmir, meaning al-Shaʿbī: \A slain man was found in a ruined area of the ruins of Wādiʿat Hamdān"
"16456","(16450) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated — from Manṣūr — from al-Shaʿbī: \That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"
"16457","(16451) As for the ḥadīth which Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to me — both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us — Hishām ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿlā narrated — from ʿUmar ibn Ṣubḥ — from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān — from Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym — from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: \When ʿUmar"
"16458","(16452) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us — Mālik narrated — from Ibn Shihāb — from Sulaymān ibn Yasār and ʿIrāk ibn Mālik: \That a man from Banī Saʿd ibn Layth had a horse which he raced"
"16459","(16453) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrāk narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated — Abū Isrāʾīl narrated — from Aṭiyyah — from Abī Saʿīd: \That a slain man was found between two tribes. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that the distance be measured to whichever was nearer"
"16460","(16454) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us — Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us — al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us — Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated — from Abū Isrāʾīl al-Mulāʾī with something similar to it. Abū Isrāʾīl is the sole narrator of it from Aṭiyyah al-ʿAwfī, and neither of their two narrations is used as evidence. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16461","(16455) Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Adib informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us — al-Haytham ibn Khalaf informed us — Ishaq informed us — Ma'n informed us — Malik informed us from Abu Layla ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, who informed him — he and some of the elders of his tribe — that 'Abdillah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisah set out toward Khaybar. Then he mentioned the hadith concerning the killing of 'Abdillah ibn Sahl, and that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Will you swear an oath and thereby claim the blood of your companion?\"" [Sahih]"""
"16462","(16456) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — they both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-'Ataridi narrated to us — Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq — al-Zuhri and Bashir ibn Abi Kayyan, mawla of Banu Harithah, narrated to us from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, who said: 'Abdillah ibn Sahl was struck down at Khaybar. He had gone out to it with a group of companions to purchase dates. He was found in a spring, his neck having been broken, and then he was buried. They took him and concealed him, then they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned his affair to him. His brother 'Abd al-Rahman came forward, and with him were his two cousins, Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah, the two sons of Mas'ud. 'Abd al-Rahman was the youngest of them in age, and he was the one entitled to the blood, and he was the spokesman of the people. When he spoke before the sons of his paternal uncle, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The eldest"
"16463","(16457) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us — Abu Dawud informed us — Mahmud ibn Kathir and Kathir ibn 'Ubayd both informed us — al-Walid informed us… (H) Abu Dawud also said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabah ibn Sufyan informed us — al-Walid informed us from Abu 'Amr, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he executed a man through qasamah (compurgation) from among Banu Nasr ibn Malik at Bahrat al-Ri'a, on the shore of Layyah. The killer and the killed were both from among them. Abu Dawud said: And this is the wording of Mahmud — \at Bahrat al-Ri'a\"" — Mahmud alone added this. This is munqati' (disconnected)"
"16464","(16458) Abu Dawud also narrated in al-Marasil from Musa ibn Isma'il from Hammad from Qatadah and 'Amir al-Ahwal from Abu al-Mughirah, that the Prophet ﷺ executed a man through qasamah in Ta'if. This is also munqati'. Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed us — al-Fasawi informed us — al-Lu'lu'i informed us — Abu Dawud informed us and mentioned it. [Da'if]"
"16465","(16459) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Raffa' al-Baghdadi in Khusrujird informed us — Abu 'Amr 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Bashir informed us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq informed us — Isma'il ibn Abi Uways and 'Isa ibn Myna both informed us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us that his father said: Those of the jurists whom I met — whose opinions are followed, meaning the people of Madinah — used to say: The oaths in qasamah are begun with those who come forward with the testimony of latah (staining) and subtle suspicion, where their adversaries do not come forward with the same, and wherever that is the case, the qasamah is for them.\n\nAbu al-Zinad said: And Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit informed me that a man from the Ansar killed a man while he was intoxicated, having struck him with a shawbaq (a whip or stick), and there was no definitive proof except latah or something similar to that. And among the people at that time were Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and jurists beyond enumeration, and no two of them differed that the heirs of the slain should swear oaths and execute the killer, or grant him pardon. So they swore fifty oaths and executed him. And they used to report that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had judged by qasamah, and they considered it to be for the one who brings latah and suspicion, stronger than what the opponent brings, and they held this view regarding the killing of the man by the Hatibis and otherwise.\n\nAnd Ibn Wahb narrated from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, adding therein that Mu'awiyah wrote to Sa'id ibn al-'As: \If what we have mentioned to you is true"
"16466","(16460) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-A' informed us — Bahr ibn Nasr informed us — 'Abdillah ibn Wahb informed me — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed me that Hisham ibn 'Urwah informed him: A man from the family of Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah had a dispute with a man from the family of Suhayb. Then he mentioned the hadith concerning his killing. He said: Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib rode to 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan regarding this matter, and he judged by qasamah against six men from the family of Hatib. He doubled the oaths for them, so the family of Hatib requested to swear against two of them and execute them both, but 'Abd al-Malik refused unless they swore against one of them and executed him. So they swore against the Suhaybi man and executed him. Hisham said: 'Urwah did not deny this and considered that the right had been achieved therein.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us regarding al-Zuhri and Rabi'ah, and it is mentioned from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from 'Abd al-'Aziz and Ibn al-Zubayr, that both of them executed by qasamah. And it is mentioned from 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz that he retracted from that and said: \If his companions find proof"
"16467","(16461) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us — Isma'il al-Qadi informed us — Sulayman ibn Harb informed us — Hammad informed us from Ayyub from Abu Raja', mawla of Abu Qilabah, who said: Abu Qilabah was in the presence of 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, and he asked them about qasamah. They said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ executed by it"
"16468","(16462) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Yusuf al-Hafiz informed me — my father informed me — Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us — Isma'il ibn Ju'ayy informed us — Hajjaj ibn Abi 'Uthman al-Sawwaf informed me — Abu Raja', mawla of Abu Qilabah, informed me — Abu Qilabah informed me: 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz one day brought out his couch for the people, gave them permission, and they entered upon him. He said: \What do you say about qasamah?\"" The people became agitated and said: \""We say that execution by it is a right"
"16469","(16463) Abu Bakr al-Ardastani informed us — Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi informed us — Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us — 'Ali ibn al-Hasan informed us — 'Abdillah ibn al-Walid informed us — Sufyan informed us from 'Abd al-Rahman from al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \Qasamah obligates the diyah (blood-money) but does not require the shedding of blood.\"" This is munqati' (disconnected). [Da'if]"""
"16470","(16464) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us — al-Hasan ibn Salam informed us — Abu Nu'aym informed us — 'Abd al-Salam informed us from Yunus from al-Hasan, who said: \Killing by qasamah is a practice of the Jahiliyyah (pre-Islamic ignorance).\"" [Sahih — from al-Hasan]"""
"16471","(16465) And in what Abū Dāwūd narrated in *al-Marāsīl*, from Hārūn ibn Zayd ibn Abī al-Zarqāʾ, from his father, from Muḥammad ibn Rāshid, from Makḥūl: that the Messenger of Allah — peace and blessings be upon him — did not rule regarding *qasāmah* (compurgation oaths) with *qiṣāṣ* (retaliatory punishment). It was narrated to us by Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad; it was narrated to us by al-Fasawī; it was narrated to us by al-Luʾluʾī; it was narrated to us by Abū Dāwūd, and he mentioned it. And ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Mālik ibn Anas also said the same. It was said to Mālik: \Why do you (your school) execute based upon it?\"" He said: \""We do not place the statement of the Messenger of Allah — peace and blessings be upon him — in the category of deception (i.e."
"16472","(16466) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, from the original of his book; it was narrated to us by Abū Jaʿfar — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Asadī al-Ḥāfiẓ in Hamadhān, in the year 342 AH; it was narrated to us by Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn; it was narrated to us by Abū Maʿmar — ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Abī al-Ḥajjāj al-Minqarī; it was narrated to us by ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn Saʿīd; it was narrated to us by Quṭan, Abū al-Haytham; it was narrated to us by Abū Yazīd, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Indeed"
"16473","(16467) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ; it was narrated to us by Abū ʿAlī — al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ; it was narrated to us by Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah; it was narrated to us by Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā; it was narrated to us by Ibn Wahb; it was narrated to me Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb; it was narrated to me by Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Sulaymān ibn Yasār, the freed slave of Maymūnah, from a man from the Companions of the Prophet — peace and blessings be upon him — from the Anṣār: that the Messenger of Allah — peace and blessings be upon him — affirmed *qasāmah* (compurgation) as it had been in the Jāhiliyyah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Ḥarmalah. And this wording came as a general statement, but he intended by it the number of oaths. For we have narrated in this hadith that he said: \The Messenger of Allah — peace and blessings be upon him — ruled with it among a group of the Anṣār regarding a slain person whom they claimed against the Jews.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated it through authentic chains from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah and others from the Anṣār"
"16474","(16468) Abū Dāwūd narrated in *al-Marāsīl* from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Hamdānī; it was narrated to us by Mūsā ibn Dāwūd; it was narrated to us by Salām ibn Miskīn, from al-Ḥasan, who said: \A people fought with stones"
"16475","(16469) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ; it was narrated to us by Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb; it was narrated to us by al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān; it was narrated to us by al-Shāfiʿī, who said: \{Min qawmin ʿaduwwin lakum}\"" — meaning"
"16476","(16470) It was narrated to us by Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, who said: \A people sought refuge with the tribe of Khathʿam. When the Muslims surrounded them"
"16477","(16471) It was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥusayn — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad; it was narrated to us by Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz; it was narrated to us by Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār; it was narrated to us by Abū Muʿāwiyah, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, from Jarīr, who said: \The Messenger of Allah — peace and blessings be upon him — sent a detachment to Khathʿam. Some people sought protection by prostrating (in prayer)"
"16478","(16472) And it was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān; it was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī; it was narrated to us by Miqdām ibn Dāwūd; it was narrated to us by Yūsuf ibn ʿAdī; it was narrated to us by Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, from Jarīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh: that the Messenger of Allah — peace and blessings be upon him — sent him to some people of Khathʿam. They sought protection by prostrating (in prayer), but he killed them. The Messenger of Allah — peace and blessings be upon him — paid their blood-money at half the *diyah*, then he said: \I am free of every Muslim who is with a polytheist.\"" His saying \""he paid their blood-money\"" (*fawadāhum*) is more apparent in indicating that he gave it voluntarily."""
"16479","(16473) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī; they both said: it was narrated to us by Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb; it was narrated to us by Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār; it was narrated to us by Yūnus ibn Bukayr, from Ibn Isḥāq; it was narrated to me ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAyyāsh. He said: al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr said to me: \This verse was revealed — {And it is not for a believer to kill a believer"
"16480","(16474) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ; it was narrated to us by Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb; it was narrated to us by Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī; it was narrated to us by Abū al-Jawwāb; it was narrated to us by ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq; it was narrated to us by ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Abū Yaḥyā, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the words of the Almighty: {And if he is from a people who are enemies to you, and he is a believer, then the freeing of a believing slave}. He said: \A man would come to the Messenger of Allah — peace and blessings be upon him — and become Muslim"
"16481","(16475) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us, from Isrāʾīl, from Simāk, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the verse: **\And if he is from a people who are enemies to you"
"16482","(16476) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, saying: al-Fāryābī narrated to us, saying: Minjāb ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The polytheists were defeated on the day of Uḥud with a defeat that was evident among them. Then Iblīs cried out: \O servants of Allah"
"16483","(16477) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdad, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAttāb narrated to us, saying: al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us, from his paternal uncle Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, who said: al-Yamān was the father of Ḥudhayfah, and his name was Ḥusayl ibn Jubayr, an ally of theirs from Banī ʿAbs. The Muslims struck him during the battle — they claimed — but they did not know who had struck him. So Ḥudhayfah waived the blood-money for whoever had killed him.\n\nMūsā ibn ʿUqbah said: Ibn Shihāb said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr said: The Muslims erred concerning him that day, and they struck him with their swords, thinking he was from the enemy, while Ḥudhayfah was calling out: \My father! My father!\"" But they did not understand his words until they were done with him. Ḥudhayfah said: \""May Allah forgive you"
"16484","(16478) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, saying: Muṭarrif narrated to us, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, who said: The father of Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān was an old man. He had been placed among the women atop the fortifications on the day of Uḥud, but he came out seeking martyrdom. He came from the direction of the polytheists, and the Muslims rushed upon him and struck him with their swords, while Ḥudhayfah was saying: \My father! My father!\"" But they could not hear him due to the turmoil of battle until they killed him. Ḥudhayfah said: \""May Allah forgive you"
"16485","(16479) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibn Isḥāq, saying: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah narrated to me, from Maḥmūd ibn Labīd, who said: As for the father of Ḥudhayfah, the swords of the Muslims fell upon him and they killed him without recognizing him. Ḥudhayfah said: \My father! My father!\"" They said: \""By Allah"
"16486","(16480) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿUtbah Aḥmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, saying: Ḍamrah ibn Rabīʿah narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm ibn Abī ʿAblah, from al-Gharīf ibn al-Daylamī, who said: We came to Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ and said: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with no one between you and him. He said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding a companion of ours upon whom the Fire had become obligatory. He said: \Set a free slave on his behalf; Allah will free"
"16487","(16481) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: Ḍamrah ibn Rabīʿah narrated to us, mentioning something similar to it, except that he said: \regarding a companion of ours upon whom the Fire had become obligatory through killing.\""\n\nIbn al-Mubārak narrated it from Ibrāhīm ibn Abī ʿAblah.\n\n---"""
"16488","(16482) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAmr, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever kills a person under covenant (muʿāhad) without right shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise"
"16489","(16483) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it, saying: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn Idrīs al-Anṣārī narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Muslim al-Ṭūsī narrated to us, saying: Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAmr al-Fuqaymī narrated to us, saying: Mujāhid narrated to us, from Junādah ibn Abī Umayyah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever kills a person from among the People of the Covenant (Ahl al-Dhimmah) shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise"
"16490","(16484) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdad, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, from Maʿmar, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Abū Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The fragrance of Paradise is found at a distance of one hundred years' travel"
"16491","(16485) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan — and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, saying: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed you, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The killer shall not inherit from the blood-money (diyah) of the one he killed.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16492","(16486) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us; Yunus informed us, from Ibn Shihab, who said: It reached us that a man from Banu Mudlij killed his son, whose name was 'Arfajah. 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) commanded him, so he brought forth his blood-money and gave it to a brother of the slain man, who shared the same father and mother. [Da'if]"
"16493","(16487) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, that a man from Kinanah, whose name was Qatadah, ordered his son to do something, but the son was slow in complying. So he hurled a sword at him, which severed his leg, and the son died. This reached 'Umar ibn al-Khatrab (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: \I shall surely kill Qatadah!\"" Then Suraqah ibn Malik came to him and said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"
"16494","(16488) Abu Muhammad — 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani — narrated to us by dictation; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: \The blood-money belongs to the 'aqilah (the paternal relatives who bear the liability)"
"16495","(16489) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us; Abu al-'Abbas informed us; al-Rabi' informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, that the Prophet (ﷺ) wrote to al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan to grant the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabiyy a share from his blood-money. Ibn Shihab said: Ashyam had been killed by mistake (khata'an). [Da'if]"
"16496","(16490) Abu al-Hasan — Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi — narrated to us by dictation, and Abu 'Ali — al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Faqih — narrated to us by recitation before him; both said: Abu Tahir — Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muhammadabathi narrated to us; Abu Qilabah al-Basri narrated to us; Qays ibn Hafs al-Darimi narrated to me; al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to me; 'A'idh ibn Rabi'ah ibn Qays narrated to me; Qurrah ibn Du'mus al-Numayri narrated to me, saying: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ), I and my paternal uncle. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16497","(16491) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us; Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan informed us; Abu Ya'la narrated to us; Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us; Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, saying: I read in the book of Mu'awiyah, the paternal uncle of Abu Qilabah, that it was from the books of Abu Qilabah. I found in it: \This is what Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah recalled of the judgment rendered by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): that the blood-money is to be divided among the heirs as an inheritance according to the Book of Allah"
"16498","(16492) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Rashid informed us; Hushaym informed us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, who narrated to us; 'Abayah ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, who said: A man from the Ansar was found killed in Khaybar. His guardians went to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. He said: \Do you have two witnesses to testify to the killing of your companion?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"
"16499","(16493) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us; Abu Shihab informed us, from al-A'mash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Shu'rayh, who said: Two men testified before Shu'rayh, saying: \We testify that this man struck him with his elbow in his throat"
"16500","(16494) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Tahir al-Faqih, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, Abu al-'Abbas — Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shadhyakhi, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr all said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us; Anas ibn Iyyad informed us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (ﷺ) was bewitched to the point that he would imagine he had done something when he had not done it. He then supplicated his Lord and then said: \Are you aware that Allah has given me guidance concerning that in which I sought His guidance?\"" 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""What is that"
"16501","(16495) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī in Marw informed us that ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl al-Balkhī informed us that Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī informed us that Abū Badr Shujāʿ ibn al-Walīd informed us — both saying — that Hāshim ibn Hāshim informed us from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd that Saʿd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever begins his morning with dates of ʿajwah"
"16502","(16496) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us that Aḥmad ibn Mihrān al-Aṣbahānī informed us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us that ʿAwf ibn Abī Jamīlah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qāḍī in Marw informed us that al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah informed us that Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us that ʿAwf informed us from Khilās and Muḥammad from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever comes to a soothsayer (ʿarrāf) or a fortune-teller (kāhin) and confirms what he says has indeed disbelieved in what was revealed upon Muḥammad.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16503","(16497) Abū Muḥammad Jānāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Jānāḥ al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah informed us that al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā, and Thābit ibn Muḥammad al-Kinānī all said: Sufyān informed us from Abū Isḥāq from Hubayrah ibn Yarīm from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \Whoever comes to a sorcerer (sāḥir)"
"16504","(16498) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr al-Makhramī informed us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Sufyān informed us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār that he heard Bajālah say: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote: 'Kill every sorcerer (sāḥir) and sorceress (sāḥirah).' He said: \So we killed three sorceresses.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16505","(16499) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, was bewitched by her slave-girl. She confessed to the sorcery and extracted it, whereupon Ḥafṣah killed her. This reached ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, and he became angry. Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, came to him and said: \Her slave-girl bewitched her; she confessed to the sorcery and extracted it.\"" So ʿUthmān"
"16506","(16500) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿImrān ibn Mūsā informed us that Abū Maʿmar informed us that Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us from Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim from al-Ḥasan from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The prescribed punishment (ḥadd) of the sorcerer is striking him with the sword.\""\n\nIsmāʿīl ibn Muslim is weak (ḍaʿīf). [Ḍaʿīf. And the mawqūf version is ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"16507","(16501) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that al-Qāḍī al-Maḥāmilī informed us that Ziyād ibn Ayyūb informed us that Hushaym informed us that Khālid informed us from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī from Jundub al-Bajalī that he killed a sorcerer who was in the presence of al-Walīd ibn ʿUqbah, and then he recited: \Do you practice sorcery while you can see?\"" [Al-Anbiyāʾ 3]. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16508","(16502) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Ibn Lahīʿah informed us from Abū al-Aswad that al-Walīd ibn ʿUqbah was in Iraq and a sorcerer was performing before him. He would strike a man's head and then call out to him, and the man would stand up outside, and his head would return to him. The people said: \Glory be to Allah! He brings the dead to life!\"" A man from among the righteous Muhājirūn saw him and looked on. When the next day came"
"16509","(16503) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed us from Ibn Shihāb who informed me that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab informed me that Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity but Allah.' Whoever says 'There is no deity but Allah' has protected from me his wealth and his life"
"16510","(16504) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us that Shuʿbah informed us from ʿAmr ibn Murrah who heard Abū ʿUbaydah narrate from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Allah extends His Hand by night so that the one who committed wrong by day may repent"
"16511","(16505) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī — from his original — narrated, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to me; Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated to me, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said:\n\nA woman from the people of Dūmat al-Jandal came seeking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after his death — that was shortly after that event — asking him about something she had entered into regarding magic, though she had not acted upon it. ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to ʿUrwah: \O son of my sister"
"16512","(16506) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated, saying: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd say: Ibn ʿAmrah — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥārithah, who was known as Abū al-Rijāl — narrated to me, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her):\n\nShe fell ill, and some of her nephews mentioned her complaint to a man from the Zuṭṭ who practiced medical treatment. He said to them: \You are mentioning a woman who has been bewitched. A slave-girl of hers bewitched her. In the slave-girl's lap there is now a young boy who has urinated in her lap.\"" They mentioned this to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"
"16513","(16507) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Maʿmar narrated, from a man, from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said:\n\nA woman came to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: \Is there any sin upon me if I restrain my camel (through magic)?\"" She said: \""Restrain your camel.\"" She said: \""Then I will detain my husband (through magic).\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Remove this sorceress from me.\"" So they removed her. [Weak]"""
"16514","(16508) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Maʿmar narrated, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam al-Sulamī, that:\n\nThe Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16515","(16509) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd narrated to us; ʿUqbah ibn ʿAlqamah narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated to me; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to me; Hilāl ibn Abī Maymūnah narrated to me; ʬāṭāʾ ibn Yasār narrated to me; Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam al-Sulamī narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, three hadiths. He said:\n\n\O Messenger of Allah"
"16516","(16510) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālūyah narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ṣafiyyah, from some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n\Whoever comes to a soothsayer (ʿarrāf) and asks him about something"
"16517","(16511) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān narrated in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Maʿmar narrated, from al-Zuhrī, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:\n\nI said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16518","(16512) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us; Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated, from al-Zuhrī; ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn narrated to me — I think he said — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Men among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ from the Anṣār narrated to me, saying:\n\nWhile we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a star was cast and it illuminated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \What used you to say when something like this occurred in the Jāhiliyyah"
"16519","(16513) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Akhnas narrated to me; al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me, from Yūsuf ibn Māhik, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\Whoever acquires knowledge of the stars has acquired a branch of magic. The more he increases"
"16520","(16514) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated from the original of his hearing; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Firyābī narrated, saying: Sufyān mentioned, from Maʿmar, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding a people who write Abjad and look into the stars, that he said:\n\n\I do not know; whoever does that"
"16521","(16515) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from ʿAwf al-ʿAbdī, from Ḥayyān — who is Ibn al-ʿAlāʾ — from Qaṭan ibn Qabīṣah, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Al-ʿiyāfah"
"16522","(16516) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, ʿAwf narrated it with a similar wording. ʿAwf said: \Al-ʿiyāfah is the scaring of birds (zajr al-ṭayr)"
"16523","(16517) ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī al-Mu'adhdhin informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard ʿĪsā ibn ʢāṣim —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard ʿĢsā ibn ʢāṣim from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and in the narration of Shuʿbah from the Prophet ﷺ he said: \Al-ṭīrah (omens from birds) is shirk (associating partners with Allah)"
"16524","(16518) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \There is no ṭīrah (evil omen)"
"16525","(16519) ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Khanb informed us, Abū Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī informed me, Abū Hāshim narrated to me, who said: I heard al-Aṣmaʿī, and he was asked about al-kalimah al-ṣāliḥah (the good word), so he said: \A man loses something of his"
"16526","(16520) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī and Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb both said: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Hishām narrated to us, Qatādah narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \There is no ʿadwā (contagion) and no ṭīrah (evil omen)"
"16527","(16521) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī informed us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from ʿUrwah ibn ʢāmir, who said: Al-ṭīrah (omens) was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: \The best of it is the fāʾl (good omen)"
"16528","(16522) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Hishām narrated from Qatādah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ would never take an evil omen from anything. And when he sent a worker (ʿāmil), he would ask about his name. If its name pleased him, he would be happy with it, and the joy of that would be seen on his face. And if he disliked his name, the displeasure of that would be seen on his face. And when he entered a village, he would ask about its name. If its name pleased him, he would be happy with it, and the joy of that would be seen on his face. And if he disliked its name, the displeasure of that would be seen on his face. [Weak]"
"16529","(16523) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us, my father informed us, al-Awzāʿī narrated to me, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to me, Ḥaḍramī ibn Lāḥiq narrated to me, Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me, who said: I heard Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no hāmah (superstition regarding owls)"
"16530","(16524) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us verbally on more than one occasion, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Qaṭṭān, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us, ʿUtbah ibn Muslim narrated from Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \If al-shuʾm (ill omen) is in anything"
"16531","(16525) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Abū Ḥassān al-Aʿraj, that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: \The people of the Jāhiliyyah used to say that evil omen (al-ṭīrah) is found in the woman"
"16532","(16526) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd said: It was recited to al-Ḥārith ibn Miskīn while I was present — Ibn al-Qāsim informed you, saying: Mālik was asked about evil omen (al-shuʾm) in the horse and the house. He said: \How many a house there is whose inhabitants perished"
"16533","(16527) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, who said: And I heard in the interpretation of this hadith that it was said: \The evil omen of the woman is her being barren; the evil omen of the horse is that it is not used in jihād; and the evil omen of the house is a wicked neighbour.\"" [Sound — from Maʿmar]"""
"16534","(16528) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Tamtām informed us, Abū Ḥudhayfah informed us, ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: A man from the Anṣār came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16535","(16529) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Nawfal, from ʿAbdillāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād, that a woman from the Anṣār said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16536","(16530) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahm narrated, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever practices medicine without being known for knowledge of medicine and thereby causes the loss of a life or less"
"16537","(16531) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī informed us, al-Qaʿnabī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb informed us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us — both said: al-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The people are followers of Quraysh in this matter: their Muslims are followers of their Muslims"
"16538","(16532) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Abū Muslim informed us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The people are followers of Quraysh in good and evil.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Rūḥ"
"16539","(16533) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, al-Asfaṭī informed us — both said: Abū al-Walīd informed us, ʿĀṣim ibn Muḥammad said: I heard my father narrate from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \This matter shall remain among Quraysh as long as there are two people among mankind.\"" In the narration of al-Dārimī: \""As long as two people remain among mankind.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd"
"16540","(16534) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī informed us, Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from his father.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Qāḍī Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarashī informed us, Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū Yaḥyā ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham informed us, Abū al-Yamān informed me, Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: Muḥammad ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim used to narrate that it reached Muʿāwiyah — while he was with him among a delegation of Quraysh — that ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ was narrating that there would be a king from Qaḥṭān. Muʿāwiyah became angry and stood up, praising Allah as He deserves, then said: \To proceed: it has reached me that certain men among you are narrating accounts that are not in the Book of Allah and are not traced back to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Those are your ignorant ones. Beware of vain desires that lead their people astray"
"16541","(16535) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Uwaysī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said:\n\n\It was among the news that reached us when Allah took His Prophet ﷺ that the Anṣār had opposed us and gathered with their families in the Saqīfah of Banī Sāʿidah. ʿAlī and al-Zubayr"
"16542","(16536) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ, Ibn al-Ḥammāmī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us in Baghdad: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād informed us, saying: It was recited to Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham while I was listening: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that:\n\nWhen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was at al-Sunḥ. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and said, 'By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has not died.' ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said, 'By Allah, nothing occurred to my mind except that, and that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will surely send him, and he will cut off the hands and feet of men.' Then Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came and uncovered the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, kissed him, and said, 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; you are good in life and in death. By Him in whose Hand is my soul, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will never cause you to experience the two deaths.' Then he went out and said, 'O you who swore an oath, take your time.' When Abū Bakr spoke, ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, sat down. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, 'Whoever was worshipping Muḥammad, then Muḥammad has indeed died. And whoever was worshipping Allah, then Allah is Ever-Living and does not die.' And he recited: 'You will surely die, and they will surely die' [al-Zumar 30], and he recited: 'Muḥammad is not but a messenger; messengers have passed before him. So if he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels?' [Āl ʿImrān 144]—the entire verse. The people sobbed and wept.\n\nThe Anṣār gathered around Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, may Allah be pleased with him, in the Saqīfah of Banī Sāʿidah, and they said, 'One amīr from us and one amīr from you.' Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ, may Allah be pleased with them, went to them. ʿUmar went to speak, but Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, silenced him. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, would say, 'By Allah, I only intended that I had prepared a speech that pleased me, and I feared that Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, would not convey it, so he spoke and conveyed it eloquently.' He said in his speech: 'We are the amīrs and you are the ministers.'\n\nAl-Ḥabbāb ibn al-Munḏhir said, 'No, by Allah, we will never do that. One amīr from us and one amīr from you.' Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said, 'No, but we are the amīrs and you are the ministers. They are the most central of the Arabs in abode and the most noble of them in lineage. Pledge allegiance to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb or Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.'\n\nʿUmar said, 'Rather, we shall pledge allegiance to you. You are the best of us, our master, and the most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' ʿUmar took his hand and pledged allegiance to him, and the people pledged allegiance to him. A speaker said, 'You have killed Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah.' ʿUmar said, 'Allah has killed him.'\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon.]"
"16543","(16537) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār, regarding the sermon of Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\n\This matter belongs to Quraysh"
"16544","(16538) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us orally, and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ recited to him. They both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir informed us: ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated to us: Abū Naḍrah narrated to us from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nWhen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, the orators of the Anṣār stood up, and each man among them would say, 'O company of the Muhājirūn, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a governor from among you, he would pair with him a man from among us. We see that this matter should be overseen by two men—one from you and one from us.' The orators of the Anṣār continued in this vein. Then Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was from the Muhājirūn, and the imām shall be from the Muhājirūn, and we are his helpers, just as we were the helpers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Then Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and said, 'May Allah reward you well, O company of the Anṣār, and keep your speaker firm.' Then he said, 'If you were to do otherwise, we would not make peace with you.' Then Zayd ibn Thābit took the hand of Abū Bakr and said, 'This is your companion; pledge allegiance to him.' Then they departed.\n\nWhen Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sat upon the minbar, he looked at the faces of the people and did not see ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, so he asked about him. A group from the Anṣār went and brought him. Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said, 'O cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his son-in-law, do you wish to split the staff of the Muslims?' He said, 'There is no blame, O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah.' So he pledged allegiance to him. Then he did not see al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām, may Allah be pleased with him, so he asked about him until they brought him. He said, 'O nephew of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his disciple, do you wish to split the staff of the Muslims?' He said the same as ʿAlī had said: 'There is no blame, O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah.' So both of them pledged allegiance to him.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16545","(16539) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Isfarāʾīnī informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah and Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib both said: Bundār ibn Bashshār informed us: Abū Hishām al-Makhzūmī informed us: Wuhayb narrated to us, and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: I heard Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah say: Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj came to me and asked me about this hadith, so I wrote it down for him on a sheet and read it to him. He said, 'This hadith is worth a sacrificial camel.' I said, 'It is worth a sacrificial camel? Rather, it is worth a purse of gold.'\""
16546"""
"16546","(16540) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī narrated to us; al-Fayḍ ibn al-Faḍl al-Bajalī narrated to us; Misʿar narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Abū Ṣādiq from Rabīʿah ibn Nājidh from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""The Imams (leaders/caliphs) are from Quraysh."" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihī]"
"16547","(16541) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Abū al-Jawwāb informed us: ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Sahl from Bukayr al-Jazarī from Anas ibn Mālik, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were in a house among a group of the Muhājirūn. Each of us began making space for him, hoping that he would sit beside him. He stood at the door of the house and said: 'The imāms are from Quraysh. I have a great right over you, and they have a similar right'—three times. 'When they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; when they judge, they judge with justice; and when they make a covenant, they fulfill it. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all of mankind.'\\n\nLikewise"
"16548","(16542) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk and Aḥmad ibn Salmān both said: Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qāḍī informed us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us from his father from Anas ibn Mālik that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\The imāms are from Quraysh: when they judge"
"16549","(16543) Mūsā al-Juhanī also narrated it from Manṣūr, from one who heard Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with its meaning. Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed him: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Mūsā al-Juhanī narrated it."
"16550","(16544) ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūh al-Shaybānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak al-ʿAyshī informed us: al-Ṣaʿq ibn Ḥazn narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\The amīrs are from Quraysh\""—he said it three times. \""Verily"
"16551","(16545) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, 'Alī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Bayān narrated to us, 'Ārim narrated to us, al-Ṣa'q ibn Ḥazn narrated to us, 'Alī ibn al-Ḥakam narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The commanders are from Quraysh"
"16552","(16546) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us, saying: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfi'ī informed us, Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated from Ibn Abī Dhi'b, from Sharīk ibn 'Abdullāh ibn Abī Namir, from 'Aṭā' ibn Yasār, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Quraysh: \You are the most deserving people of this matter (authority)"
"16553","(16547) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Awn narrated from Khālid — (ḥ) and Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Bakr ibn 'Abdullāh informed me, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khālid ibn 'Abdullāh narrated from al-Jurayrī, from Abū Naḍrah, from Abū Sa'īd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When two caliphs are given the pledge of allegiance"
"16554","(16548) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdūs informed us, 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī informed us, Bundār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated from Furāt, who said: I heard Abū Ḥāzim narrating, who said: I sat with Abū Hurayrah for five years, and I heard him narrate from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The Children of Israel were governed by the prophets; whenever a prophet died"
"16555","(16549) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us, saying: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Salamah ibn Nubayt al-Ashja'ī, from his father, from Sālim ibn 'Ubayd, who was among the Companions of the Ṣuffah, who said: Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when it was said to him: \O Companion of the Messenger of Allah"
"16556","(16550) Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said in his sermon on that day — as Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq regarding the sermon of Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, on that day — he said: \It is not permissible for the Muslims to have two amirs"
"16557","(16551) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdūs informed us, 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī informed us, al-Qa'nabī narrated from what he read to Mālik, from Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd, who said: 'Ubādah ibn al-Walīd informed me from his father, from 'Ubādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: \We gave the pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey"
"16558","(16552) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū 'Abdullāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb and 'Alī ibn 'Īsā ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Qabbānī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd and 'Ubaydullāh ibn 'Umar, from 'Ubādah ibn al-Walīd ibn 'Ubādah, and he narrated something similar, adding: \And upon us being placed at a disadvantage"
"16559","(16553) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Faḍl al-Faḥḥām informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated from 'Amr ibn al-Ḥārith, Bukayr narrated to me from Busr ibn Sa'īd, from Junādah ibn Abī Umayyah, from 'Ubādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called us"
"16560","(16554) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdūs informed us, 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd informed us, al-Qa'nabī narrated from what he read to Mālik, from 'Abdullāh ibn Dīnār, from 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar, who said: \When we used to give the pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey"
"16561","(16555) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Fāriyābī and Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Muqaddamī both said: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; Sayyār informed us.\n\n(al-Ismāʿīlī said) And Ḥāmid informed me; Surayj narrated to us; Hushaym narrated from Sayyār, from al-Shaʿbī, from Jarīr, who said: \I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to hear and obey.\"" He instructed me: \""In whatever you are able"
"16562","(16556) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Faḥḥām informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from Ibn Khuthaym, meaning from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) remained in Makkah for ten years"
"16563","(16557) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām and Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Khālid ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us from Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ, from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aʿraj, from Maʿqil ibn Yasār al-Muzanī, who said: \The people pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of Ḥudaybiyyah while he was beneath the tree"
"16564","(16558) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; al-Asfaṭī informed us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us; Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir, who said: \We were on the day of Ḥudaybiyyah one thousand four hundred"
"16565","(16559) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd narrated from Salamah al-Akwaʿ, who said: \I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of Ḥudaybiyyah"
"16566","(16560) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd informed us; Abū Muslim informed us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, and he mentioned it similarly, except that he said: \Then I stepped aside"
"16567","(16561) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʬUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; al-Asfaṭī informed us; Abū Salamah Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl al-Minqarī informed us; Wuhayb narrated from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī, from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd, who said: \When the time of al-Ḥarrah came"
"16568","(16562) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Burqān, from Thābit ibn al-Ḥajjāj; Ibn al-ʿAfīf narrated to me, who said: \I saw Abū Bakr taking the pledge of allegiance from the people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Groups would gather before him"
"16569","(16563) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us; Juwayriyyah narrated from Mālik, from al-Zuhrī, that Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed him that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him: \The group whom ʿUmar had appointed gathered and consulted among themselves. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf said to them: 'I am not one to compete with you for this matter"
"16570","(16564) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar wrote to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān, who was demanding his pledge of allegiance. He wrote to him: \In the name of Allah"
"16571","(16565) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Muqri', known as Ibn al-Hammamiyy, informed us in Baghdad: Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih informed us: Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar, who said: When the people gathered in allegiance to 'Abd al-Malik, 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar wrote to him: \Peace be upon you. To proceed: I affirm hearing and obedience to 'Abd Allah 'Abd al-Malik"
"16572","(16566) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to me: my father — (h) — and Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamm al-Faqih al-Isfara'iniyy informed us there: Abu Sahl Bishr ibn Ahmad informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Nasr al-Hadda' informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah al-Madiniyy informed us, both saying: 'Abd al-Razaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri from 'Urwah from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to test the women with this verse: {When the believing women come to you to pledge allegiance to you that they will not associate anything with Allah} — and no"
"16573","(16567) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah and Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far informed us: they said: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us: Abu al-Tahir informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yunus said: Ibn Shihab said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), said: \When the believing women emigrated to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"16574","(16568) Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-'Adl informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdiyy informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Malik informed us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Umaymah bint Ruqayqah, who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) among a group of women to pledge allegiance to him"
"16575","(16569) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Fakihiyy informed us: Abu Yahya ibn Abi Masarrat informed us: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed me: Abu 'Aqil narrated to me from his grandfather, 'Abd Allah ibn Hisham, who had met the Prophet (ﷺ). His mother, Zaynab bint Hamid, took him to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16576","(16570) Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmish al-Faqih informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us: Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami informed us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabiyy said: Sufyan mentioned from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \It was said to 'Umar"
"16577","(16571) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan informed us: Abu Usamah informed us from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \I was present with my father when he was struck"
"16578","(16572) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukariyy informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadiyy informed us: 'Abd al-Razaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri from Salim from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \I entered upon Hafsah"
"16579","(16573) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzaz informed us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Marzuq informed us: Shababah ibn Sawwar informed us: Shu'bayb ibn Maymun informed us: Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us from al-Sha'bi from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, who said: \It was said to 'Ali"
"16580","(16574) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us in the final part of the tenth volume of al-Fawa'id al-Kabir li-Abi al-'Abbas: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khulayy al-Himsiyy informed us: Bishr ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us from his father from al-Zuhri from 'Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik al-Ansariyy — and Ka'b ibn Malik was one of the three upon whom repentance was accepted — 'Abd Allah ibn Ka'b informed me that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas informed him that 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, went out from the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during the illness in which he passed away. The people said: \O Abu Hasan"
"16581","(16575) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us; Ṣāliḥ ibn Rustum, Abū ʿĀmir al-Khazzāz, narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her, said: \When my father's condition became severe"
"16582","(16576) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; al-Amīr Abū Aḥmad Khalaf ibn Aḥmad informed us; Abū Muḥammad al-Fākihī narrated to us in Makkah; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrah narrated to us; he said: I heard Yūsuf ibn Muḥammad say: \It has reached me that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq"
"16583","(16577) The Qāḍī Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed me through ijāzah that Abū Muḥammad al-Fākihī had informed them, and he mentioned it in his chain of narration similarly. And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mujabbir narrated it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah, with a connected chain. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16584","(16578) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us from Qatādah from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Maʿdān ibn Abī Ṭalḥah al-Yaʿmarī, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, praised Allah and extolled Him, then he mentioned the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and then said: \O people"
"16585","(16579) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Ḥuṣayn from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn, in the story of the killing of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: \They said: 'Make a bequest"
"16586","(16580) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Khālid al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated to us from his father from al-Zuhrī. Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: \ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"
"16587","(16581) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, and the wording is his. Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hāniʾ informed me, and he wrote it down for me in his own hand. Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus informed us; Zāʾidah narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \I entered upon ʿĀʾishah"
"16588","(16582) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bisṭāmī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed me; Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān al-Juʿfī narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to me; Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb; from Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from his father, who said: \When the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became severe"
"16589","(16583) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ informed us; Zāʾidah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr from Abū Burdah ibn Abī Mūsā from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill and said: 'Command Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' ʿĀʾishah"
"16590","(16584) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Jakkānī narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed me; Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated to me from al-Zuhrī, who said: \Anas ibn Mālik"
"16591","(16585) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Abū Maʿshar narrated from Muḥammad ibn Qays, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was unwell for thirteen days. Whenever he felt relief, he would lead the prayer, and whenever his condition worsened, Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) would lead the prayer. [Weak]"
"16592","(16586) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū al-Bakhtarī ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us, Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī narrated from Zāʾidah, from ʢĀṣim, from Zirr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed away, the Ansār said, \Let there be a leader from among us and a leader from among you.\"" Then ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to them and said"
"16593","(16587) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir al-Ḥizāmī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Fulayḥ narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated to me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf was with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with them both), and that Muḥammad ibn Salamah had broken the sword of al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both). Then Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and addressed the people, apologizing to them, and said, \By Allah"
"16594","(16588) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me on the day his illness began, and I said, \Oh"
"16595","(16589) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh informed me, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, Abū Thābit narrated to us, Ibrāhīm narrated from his father, from Muḥammad ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from his father, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and spoke to him about something, and he told her to return to him. She said, \O Messenger of Allah"
"16596","(16590) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar informed us, al-Ḍaḥḥāk informed us, Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from a freed slave of Ribʿī, from Ribʿī, from Ḥudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Follow the two after me: Abū Bakr and ʿUmar"
"16597","(16591) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from Sufyān, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from Hilāl, the freed slave of Ribʿī, from Ribʿī, from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Follow the two after me\"" — meaning Abū Bakr and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."""
"16598","(16592) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī both said: Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to me, Thābit al-Bunānī narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabbāḥ, from Abū Qatādah, regarding when the Prophet (ﷺ) appointed a deputy over his companions during a journey. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \What do you think the people have done?\"" Then he said"
"16599","(16593) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, al-Qāḍī Abū al-Haytham ʿUtbah ibn Khaythamah, and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, that Saʿīd informed him that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \While I was asleep"
"16600","(16594) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, from his father, regarding the dream of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) concerning Abū Bakr and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both). He said: \I saw the people gathered"
"16601","(16595) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah, the Most High, have mercy upon him, said: \The dreams of the Prophets are revelation.\"" And his statement \""and in his drawing forth there is weakness\"" means the brevity of his tenure"
"16602","(16596) Abū ʿAmr al-Bisṭāmī narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Muṣʿab al-Zubayrī narrated to us: al-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥizāmī narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Zayd ibn Ḥārithah"
"16603","(16597) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, saying: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh al-Qawarīrī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Zayd, Jaʿfar, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rawāḥah, and he handed the banner to Zayd. They were all struck down. Anas said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced their deaths to the people before the news arrived. He said: 'Zayd took the banner and was struck down; then Jaʿfar took it and was struck down; then ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rawāḥah took it and was struck down. Then the banner was taken thereafter by a sword from among the swords of Allah — Khālid ibn al-Walīd.'\"" He said: \""And he was narrating this to the people while his eyes were flowing with tears.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and Aḥmad ibn Wāqid"
"16604","(16598) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ ibn al-Ḥammāmī narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Mihrān al-Dīnawarī narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ṣadaqah al-Dīnawarī narrated to us: Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated to me, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an expedition and appointed Usāmah ibn Zayd"
"16605","(16599) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah, from his father, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him and Muʿādh to Yemen and said to the two of them: \Be cooperative with one another"
"16606","(16600) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥuṣayn al-Aḥmasī narrated to us: my grandmother, whose name was Umm Ḥuṣayn al-Aḥmasiyyah, narrated to me, saying: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'If an Abyssinian slave is appointed over you"
"16607","(16601) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Zuhrī al-Qāḍī in Makkah narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn Khuzaymah ibn Rāshid al-Baṣrī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us, from his father, from Thumāmah ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \Qays ibn Saʿd held a position with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ equivalent to that of the chief of police with the governor — meaning he looked into his affairs.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Anṣārī. [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"16608","(16602) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad al-Aʿwar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said regarding the verse {O you who believe, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you} [al-Nisāʾ 59]: \It was revealed concerning ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥudhāfah ibn Qays ibn ʿAdī al-Sahmī. The Prophet ﷺ sent him in command of a detachment.\"" Yaʿlā ibn Muslim informed me from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"
"16609","(16603) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us in Marw: Abū al-Muwajjah Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Muwajjah narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us: Yūnus narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah"
"16610","(16604) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh al-Fārisī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥubbāb narrated to us: Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me: Ziyād ibn Saʿd informed me that Ibn Shihāb informed him, and he mentioned it in a similar manner. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim, from Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm."
"16611","(16605) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād that ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us that Rūḥ ibn al-Faraj narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Yaʿqūq, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, narrated from Abū Ḥāzim from Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Sammān from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Hold firmly to obedience in what is pleasing to you and what is displeasing to you"
"16612","(16606) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān, Ibn Khuzaymah, and Ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm informed us that Bundār narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to me that Abū al-Tayyāḥ narrated from Anas ibn Mālik who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Listen and obey"
"16613","(16607) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us that Shabbābah narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Abū ʿImrān al-Jawnī from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ṣāmit from Abū Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) enjoined upon me that I should listen and obey, even if it be to a slave whose limbs have been amputated.\\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16614","(16608) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd (ḥ) informed us, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; they said: Musaddad narrated to us that Yaḥyā narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh who narrated to me that Nāfiʿ narrated from ʿAbd Allāh from the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: \Listening and obedience are incumbent upon a Muslim in what he likes and what he dislikes"
"16615","(16609) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Zubayd from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) dispatched a military expedition and appointed a man as its commander over them, and he commanded them to obey him. He kindled a fire for them and commanded them to plunge into it. A group of people resolved to do so, while another group said, \We only fled from the fire (of the world).\"" They refused. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Had they entered it"
"16616","(16610) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb ibn Shābūr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir narrated to us (ḥ). And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Abū ʿAmmār al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth al-Khuzāʿī, Isḥāq ibn Mūsā al-Anṣārī, and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd al-Yashkurī narrated to us; they said: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir narrated to me that Busr ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to me that Abū Idrīs narrated to me that he heard Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān say: \The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about good"
"16617","(16611) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Shaybān ibn Farūkh narrated to us that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated from Ghaylān ibn Jarīr from Abū Qays ibn Rabbāḥ from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \Whoever withdraws from obedience and separates from the jamāʿah and dies"
"16618","(16612) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us that ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Sābiq narrated to us that ʿĀṣim ibn Muḥammad narrated from Zayd ibn Muḥammad from Nāfiʿ and Sālim from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muṭīʿ. When he saw him, he said: \Bring a cushion for Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\"" He said: \""I have not come to sit; I have come to narrate to you a ḥadīth I heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I heard him say: 'Whoever withdraws his hand from obedience will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with no proof (ḥujjah) for him. And whoever dies without having a pledge of allegiance (bayʿah) upon his neck"
"16619","(16613) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us that Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us that Abū Tawbah narrated to us that Muʿāwiyah ibn Salām narrated from Zayd ibn Salām from Abū Salām who narrated to me that al-Ḥārith al-Ashʿarī narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) narrated to them and said: \I command you with five matters which Allah"
"16620","(16614) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn al-Haytham al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh and Zuhayr narrated from Muṭarrif from Abū al-Jahm from Khālid ibn Uhbān from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever separates from the jamāʿah by even a span has removed the noose of Islam from his neck.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16621","(16615) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Zayd ibn Wahb, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There will be selfishness and matters which you will disapprove of.\"" They said: \""What should one do who witnesses that"
"16622","(16616) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl, ʿĀrim, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, and Musaddad said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Jaʿd Abū ʿUthmān — Musaddad said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: al-Jaʿd Abū ʿUthmān narrated to us: Abū Rajāʾ al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās narrate from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever sees something in his amīr that he dislikes"
"16623","(16617) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dārimī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Thaqafī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sahl ibn ʿAskar narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Salām narrated to us: Zayd ibn Salām informed us, from Abū Salām, who said: Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16624","(16618) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd narrated to me: my father narrated to us: al-Awzāʿī narrated to us: al-Zuhrī narrated to me, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There will be khulafāʾ after me who will act upon what they know and do what they are commanded. Then there will be khulafāʾ after them who will act upon what they do not know and do what they are not commanded. Whoever disapproves of them is absolved"
"16625","(16619) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us: Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us: al-Awzāʿī narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said… and he mentioned this ḥadīth."
"16626","(16620) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: al-Muʿallā ibn Ziyād and Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated from al-Ḥasan, from Ḍabbah ibn Miḥṣan, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There will be imāms over you from whom you will recognize [good] and disapprove [of evil].\"" Whoever disapproves — Hishām said: \""with his tongue — is absolved"
"16627","(16621) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed it to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Ḍabbī narrated to us: Ibn Ḥisāb narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it with its chain, similar to it, except that he said: \Whoever disapproves is absolved"
"16628","(16622) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to me: my father narrated to us, from Qatādah: al-Ḥasan narrated to us, from Ḍabbah ibn Miḥṣan al-ʿAnazī, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), with its meaning. He said: \Whoever detests is absolved"
"16629","(16623) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Sahl narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir narrated to us: Ruwayq, the mawlā of Banī Fazārah, informed us that he heard Muslim ibn Quraz̤ah, the paternal cousin of ʿAwf ibn Mālik, say: I heard ʿAwf ibn Mālik al-Ashjaʿī say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \The best of your imāms are those whom you love and who love you"
"16630","(16624) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Simāk, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil — and I do not know it except from his father — who said: Yazīd ibn Salamah al-Juʿfī asked the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16631","(16625) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated it with its chain and its meaning, except that he said: Salamah ibn Yazīd al-Juʿfī, and he said: \Then he asked him a second time"
"16632","(16626) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī informed us in Baghdād; Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl, meaning al-Sulamī, informed us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm, meaning ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, narrated to me; ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sālim narrated to me; Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Fuḍayl ibn Faḍālah informed us that Ḥabīb ibn ʿUbayd informed them that al-Miqdām informed them that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Obey your commanders"
"16633","(16627) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Shuʿbah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us. He said: I heard Qatādah say: I heard Anas ibn Mālik from Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr that a man from the Anṣār said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16634","(16628) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Suwayd ibn Ghaflah, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābb, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: \O Abā Umayyah"
"16635","(16629) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated it to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Sufyān, from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, and he mentioned it with its meaning. He added at the end: \And do not separate from the jamāʿah.\"" He did not mention Manṣūr in its chain"
"16636","(16630) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated from Layth, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sābit, from Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī, from Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ and Muʿādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with both of them, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Allah began this matter as prophethood and mercy"
"16637","(16631) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed us; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us; Ṣakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar gathered his household when the people of Madīnah rallied to ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, and they Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah. He said: \We pledged allegiance to this man upon the pledge of Allah and His Messenger"
"16638","(16632) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, that Muʿāwiyah sent one hundred thousand dirhams to Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them. When Muʿāwiyah called for the pledge of allegiance to Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah, he said: \Do you think that he wanted this? If so"
"16639","(16633) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī, Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd, narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us; Ayyūb narrated from Nāfiʿ, who said: When the people of Madīnah deposed Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah, Ibn ʿUmar gathered his retinue and his freedmen. In the narration of Sulaymān: his retinue and his children. He said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'For every traitor a banner will be raised on the Day of Resurrection.'\"" Al-Zahrānī added in his narration: He said: \""And we have pledged allegiance to this man upon the pledge of Allah and His Messenger"
"16640","(16634) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bisṭāmī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Khalīfah narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbd Allāh, and from Thābit, from Anas, with two chains in two places, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \For every traitor there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection.\"" One of them said: \""It will be raised.\"" The other said: \""It will be seen on the Day of Resurrection"
"16641","(16635) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr al-Ḥīrī informed me; Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us; Abū Khaythamah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyān narrated to us; Abū Naḍrah narrated from Abū Saʿīd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Every traitor shall have a banner raised for him on the Day of Resurrection in proportion to the extent of his treachery. Beware"
"16642","(16636) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated; he said: I heard Abū Ṣāliḥ say: I heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There are three persons whom Allah shall not look at on the Day of Resurrection"
"16643","(16637) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed me; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Beware"
"16644","(16638) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Daqqāq narrated to us in Baghdad; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed me; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to me; from his father, from Qatādah, from Abū al-Malīḥ, that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ziyād came to visit Maʿqil ibn Yāsar while he was ill. He said: \Were it not that I am in the throes of death"
"16645","(16639) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Abū al-Ashhab Jaʿfar ibn Ḥayyān narrated from al-Ḥasan, from Maʿqil ibn Yāsar al-Ashjaʿī, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \There is no man who is given charge of a people and dies while he is deceiving his flock"
"16646","(16640) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb and ʿImrān ibn Mūsā both said: Shaybān ibn Farūkh narrated to us; Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us; al-Ḥasan narrated that ʿĀʾidh ibn ʿAmr, who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, came to ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ziyād and said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The worst of shepherds are the harsh ones"
"16647","(16641) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī informed us in Kūfah, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us in Naysābūr; both said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ḥāzim al-Ashjaʿī, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There are three persons whom Allah shall not speak to on the Day of Resurrection"
"16648","(16642) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ẓabyān and Zayd ibn Wahb, from Jarīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever does not show mercy to people"
"16649","(16643) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated from Shuʿbah, from Manṣūr, from Abū ʿUthmān, the freed slave of al-Mughīrah, who heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Mercy is not removed except from a wretched person.\"" (He said it three times.) [Ḥasan]"""
"16650","(16644) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥawshab narrated from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab, from Abū Umāmah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I enjoin the khalīfah after me to fear Allah"
"16651","(16645) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Mubārak al-Naysābūrī informed me; al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ informed us; Saʿīd —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibn al-Sarḥ narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb, from Abī Maḥrūm, from Sahl ibn Muʿādh, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever suppresses his anger while he is capable of executing it"
"16652","(16646) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Qurqub al-Tammār in Hamadhān informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Khālid narrated to us; Bishr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from al-Zuhrī. ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās said: \ʿUyaynah ibn Ḥiṣn ibn Ḥudhayfah ibn Badr arrived and stayed with his nephew al-Ḥur ibn Qays ibn Ḥiṣn"
"16653","(16647) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā both said: Yaḥyā, meaning Ibn Saʿīd, narrated from ʿUbaydullāh; Khubayb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿĀṣim, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Seven shall be shaded by Allah under His Throne on the Day when there shall be no shade except His shade: a just leader (imām ʿadl); a man who grew up in the worship of Allah; a man whose heart is attached to the mosques; two men who love each other for the sake of Allah"
"16654","(16648) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Abū Khaythamah narrated to us; Saʿd al-Ṭāʾī narrated to me; Abū Mudillah narrated to me that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Three supplications are not rejected: the supplication of a just leader"
"16655","(16649) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; ʿAffān ibn Jubayr al-Ṭāʾī narrated from a man he named to me, from ʿIkrimah —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū Umayyah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus informed us; Saʿd, Abū Ghaylān, narrated to us; ʿAffān ibn Jubayr al-Ṭāʾī narrated from Abū Jarīr or Ḥarīz al-Azdī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \One day of a just leader is better than sixty years of worship"
"16656","(16650) Abū Muḥammad al-Sukkariyy informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Tarqafī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Dimashqī narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Ṣubayḥ narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \When you pass through a land in which there is no ruler (sulṭān)"
"16657","(16651) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said at the time of his death: \Know that people will continue to be in goodness so long as their rulers (wulāt) and guides (hudāt) remain upright.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16658","(16652) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Suwayd narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī narrated from his maternal uncle al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥur, from al-Qāsim ibn Mukhaymirah, who said: \Your era is your ruler (sulṭān). When your ruler is righteous"
"16659","(16653) Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Abū Ḍamrah Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated. He said: I heard Abū Ḥāzim say: \People will continue to be in goodness so long as these desires do not enter into the ruler — those [desires] from which they protect the people. But when they enter into them"
"16660","(16654) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī. ʿĀmir ibn Wāthilah al-Laythī narrated to me, saying: \A man from the people of Taymāʾ came to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān. He was a man of the People of the Book. He said: 'O Commander of the Faithful"
"16661","(16655) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah al-San'ani narrated to us — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari informed us — 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \What do you think — if I appoint over you the best person I know and then command him to uphold justice"
"16662","(16656) Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmish al-Faqih informed us — Hajib ibn Ahmad al-Tusi narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Munib narrated to us — Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us — Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"
"16663","(16657) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yusuf said: Sufyan mentioned from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"
"16664","(16658) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Asbahani informed us — Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Humran narrated to us — Awf ibn Abi Jamilah narrated to us — Ziyad ibn Mikhraq narrated to us — Abu Kinanah narrated to us — from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"
"16665","(16659) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us — Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Hamyd ibn Mihran al-Kindi narrated to us — Sa'd ibn Aws narrated to us — from Ziyad ibn Kasib al-'Adawi, who said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amir used to address the people while wearing fine garments and having his hair combed. One day he prayed and then entered [his home], while Abu Bakrah was sitting beside the pulpit. Mirdas Abu Bilal said: \Do you not see the commander of the people and their master wearing fine garments and resembling the wicked (fussaq)?\"" Abu Bakrah heard him and said to his son al-Asyal': \""Call Abu Bilal for me.\"" So he called him. Abu Bakrah said: \""Did I not hear what you said just now about the commander? And I have heard the Messenger of Allah"
"16666","(16660) Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hurfi in Baghdad narrated to us — Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-A'la narrated to us — (and in another chain) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Baghdadi narrated to us — 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-A'la ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us — his father narrated to us — 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us — from 'Abd Allah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi (and in the narration of al-Hurfi, 'Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated to me — Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn 'Amir, who is al-Zubaydi, narrated to us) — al-Fudayl ibn Fadalah, tracing it back to Ibn A'idh, and Ibn A'idh tracing it back to Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that 'Iyad ibn Ghanm al-Ash'ari came upon the owner of Darayya when it was conquered. Hisham ibn Hakim came to him and spoke harshly to him. Hisham stayed for several nights, then came to him offering an apology and said: \O 'Iyad"
"16667","(16661) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us — 'Asim ibn Muhammad narrated from his father, who said: A man said to Ibn 'Umar: \We enter upon our ruler and speak to him with words other than those we speak when we are away from them.\"" He said: \""We used to consider this as hypocrisy (nifaq).\"" Al-Bukhari recorded it in his Sahih from Abu Nu'aym"
"16668","(16662) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Ibn Milhan narrated to us — Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth narrated — from Ibn Abi Habib, from 'Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \Indeed"
"16669","(16663) Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar narrated — from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"
"16670","(16664) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to me — Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhawayh narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to me — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Hazim and 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us — Yazid ibn al-Had narrated — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated — from 'Isa ibn Talhah al-Taymi, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \A servant may utter a word without giving it due consideration"
"16671","(16665) Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥurfī informed us in Baghdad: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me: Abū al-Ḍar narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning Ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from his father, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Indeed"
"16672","(16666) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qāḍī in Marw and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Makhlad al-Jawharī in Baghdad both narrated to us, saying: Al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir al-Ḍubaʿī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAlqamah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather ʿAlqamah ibn Waqqāṣ, who said: There was a frivolous man who would enter upon the commanders and make them laugh. My grandfather said to him: \Woe to you"
"16673","(16667) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ibn ʿUthmān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn al-Mubārak, informed us: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us, from ʿAlqamah ibn Waqqāṣ al-Laythī, that Bilāl ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muzanī said to him: \I see you entering upon these commanders and frequenting them. Be mindful of what you say in their presence"
"16674","(16668) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Mahrūyah al-Rāzī narrated to us: Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī and ʿAmr ibn Tamīm both narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Dīnawarī and al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī both narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from Abū Ḥuṣayn, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿĀṣim al-ʿAdawī, from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were seven or nine in number, and among us was a cushion of red leather. He said: \There will be after me commanders. Whoever believes them in their lies and assists them in their oppression"
"16675","(16669) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Mahdī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me: Al-Layth narrated to me, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who narrated to me: Khālid ibn Abī ʿImrān narrated to me: Abū ʿAyāsh narrated to me, from Ibn ʿUjrah al-Anṣārī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were in the mosque, I being the ninth of nine, and he said to us: \Do you hear? Do you hear?\"" three times. Then he said: \""There will be over you imāms. Whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lies and assists them in their oppression"
"16676","(16670) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir narrated to me: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yūnus informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khārijah ibn Zayd, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: I came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him: \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"
"16677","(16671) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Sarrāj informed us by dictation: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī narrated to me: ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to me, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws and what is between his legs"
"16678","(16672) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal al-Māsarjasī informed us: Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām, who said: I was sitting with Ḥudhayfah when a man passed by and they said: \This one carries reports to the ruler.\"" Ḥudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""The qattāt shall not enter Paradise.\"" Al-Aʿmash said: \""And the qattāt is the nammām (the talebearer).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from al-Aʿmash"
"16679","(16673) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah informed me: ʿAmr ibn Murrah narrated to me — he heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salamah narrating from Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl al-Murādī — that two men from the People of the Book said, one to his companion: \Come"
"16680","(16674) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Tājir al-Zāhid narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us in Baghdad: Surayj ibn Yūnus narrated to us: ʿAbīdah, meaning Ibn Ḥumayd, narrated to us: Al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, who said: Kaʿb said: \The greatest of people in sin on the Day of Resurrection is the one who carries tales about his brother to his imām (ruler).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16681","(16675) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, among others, who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī narrated to us, Isrāʾīl narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, al-Kudaymī narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Isrāʾīl narrated from al-Suddī, from al-Walīd ibn Abī Hāshim, from Zayd ibn Zāʾid, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to us and said: \Let none of you convey to me anything about any of my Companions"
"16682","(16676) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Qabīṣah narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Juḥādah, who said: I heard al-Ḥasan saying: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not recognize slander"
"16683","(16677) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām, from his father, who said: I heard a bishop from the people of Najrān speaking to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), saying: \O Commander of the Faithful"
"16684","(16678) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated in Baghdad, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū al-Nuʿmān narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Mujāhid, from al-Shaʿbī, that al-ʿAbbās said to his son ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both): \I see that this man has honored you\""—meaning ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)—\""and has drawn you close in his assembly and placed you among a people who are not your equal. So remember from me three things: let no falsehood be tested against you"
"16685","(16679) Al-Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī narrated to us, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us by dictation from the original of his book and from his memory, Abū Usāmah narrated from Burayd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Burdah, from his grandfather Abī Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, who said: When a beggar came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), he would say: \Intercede"
"16686","(16680) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd al-Bayrūtī narrated to us, my father narrated to me, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Hishām ibn al-Ghāz narrated to me from his father Hishām, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever acts as a means of connection for his Muslim brother to one in authority for the benefit of some righteous purpose or the easing of a difficulty"
"16687","(16681) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Kathīr ibn Zayd, from al-Walīd ibn Rabāḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The believer is the mirror of the believer"
"16688","(16682) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated in Baghdad, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to me, al-Layth narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym ibn Zayd, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), that he heard Ismāʿīl ibn Bashīr, the freedman of Banī Maghālah, say: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Ṭalḥah ibn Sahl al-Anṣārī both say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no one who forsakes a Muslim in a place where his honor is diminished and his sanctity is violated"
"16689","(16683) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī narrated to us, Abū al-Muwajjah narrated to us, ʿAbdān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh—that is Ibn al-Mubārak—narrated to us, Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it with its chain, similarly. [Weak]"
"16690","(16684) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Ibn Abī Laylā narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Ibn Abī al-Dardāʾ, from his father, who said: A man spoke ill of another man in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and a man came to his defense. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever defends the honor of his brother"
"16691","(16685) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī and Abū Yaḥyā al-Nāqid narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū Yaḥyā, meaning al-Nāqid, narrated to us. They both said: Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Ḥumayd, from al-Ḥasan, from Anas, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever supports his brother in his absence"
"16692","(16686) Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj narrated to us: Muṭayyin narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Maslamah narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the noble one of a people comes to you"
"16693","(16687) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Umayyah al-Ṭarsūsī narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muqātil al-Marwazī narrated to us: Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿUmar al-Aḥmasī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, from Jarīr ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) was sent, I came to him and he said: \O Jarīr"
"16694","(16688) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abū ʿImrān al-Jawnī ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Ḥabīb, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with them both): \There have always been among the people notables who bring forward the needs of the people. So honour the notables of the people. And it suffices a weak Muslim in terms of justice that he be treated fairly in justice and distribution.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"16695","(16689) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah and Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Ziyād ibn ʿIlaqah. ʿArfajah heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \There shall come to be calamities and calamities. So whoever seeks to divide the affair of this Ummah while they are united"
"16696","(16690) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mukhtār and a man he named narrated to us, from Ziyād ibn ʿIlaqah, from ʿArfajah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There shall come to be calamities and calamities. So whoever you see walking toward the Ummah of Muḥammad seeking to divide their jamāʿah"
"16697","(16691) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Abī Yaʿfūr narrated from his father, from ʿArfajah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever comes to you while your affair is united upon a single man"
"16698","(16692) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ḍarīr narrated to us in al-Rayy: Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: my father narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Zayd ibn Wahb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Rabb al-Kaʿbah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: I was sitting with him in the shade of the Kaʿbah while he was narrating to the people, saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey and we stopped at a place. Some of us were pitching their tents, some were tending to their livestock, and some were practising archery, when the caller of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called out: \Prayer in congregation!\"" I went to him while he was addressing the people"
"16699","(16693) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥīrī narrated to us: Musaddad ibn Quṭn narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Jarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, and he mentioned it with its chain and its meaning. In it he said: \And whoever gives bayʿah to an Imam"
"16700","(16694) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. They both said: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from his father, from Ibn Abī Nuʿm, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) sent to the Prophet (ﷺ) a quantity of gold still in its clay, and he distributed it among four: between al-Aqraʿ ibn Ḥābis al-Ḥanẓalī then al-Mujāshiʿī, and between ʿUyaynah ibn Badr al-Fazārī, and between Zayd al-Khayl al-Ṭāʾī then one of the Banī Nabhān, and between ʿAlqamah ibn ʿUlāthah al-ʿĀmirī then one of the Banī Kilāb. The Quraysh and the Anṣār became angry and said: \He gives to the chieftains of the people of Najd and leaves us out!\"" He said: \""I am only seeking to reconcile their hearts.\"" A man came with sunken eyes"
"16701","(16695) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak — informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī — informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb — narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl — narrated to us; Abū Naḍrah — narrated to us, from Abū Saʿīd that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There will be a split between two groups of my Ummah"
"16702","(16696) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Aḥmad al-Khusrawajirdī — informed us; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Khusrawajirdī — narrated to us; Naṣr ibn ʿAlī al-Jahḍamī — narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad — narrated to us; Sufyān — narrated to us, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk al-Mishraqī, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), in a narration in which he mentioned a people who will emerge upon a division among the people, and the one of the two factions that is closer to the truth will kill them.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qawārīrī, from Abū Aḥmad."
"16703","(16697) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah — narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Khaythamah, from Suwayd ibn Ghaflah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When I narrate to you a ḥadīth from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"16704","(16698) And Abū Muḥammad — informed us; Abū Saʿīd — narrated to us; al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī — narrated to us; al-Aʿmash — narrated to us, with its chain and its meaning, and added: \They will pass through the religion as an arrow passes through its game.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb and others"
"16705","(16699) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr — narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd and Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from ʿUbaydah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said — Ismāʿīl said: \He mentioned the Khawārij"
"16706","(16700) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī — in Baghdad, both said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq — informed us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān — narrated to us; Salamah ibn Kuhayl — narrated to us; Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhnī — informed me that he was among the army that was with ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), those who marched against the Khawārij. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \O people"
"16707","(16701) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Mihrān — narrated to us; Abū al-Ṭāhir — narrated to us; Ibn Wahb — narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Saʿīd, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Rāfīʿ, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), that when the Ḥarūriyyah emerged while he was with ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), they said: \There is no judgment except for Allah.\"" He said: \""A word of truth by which falsehood is intended. Indeed"
"16708","(16702) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Muzanī — narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā — narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān — informed me; Shuʿayb — narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī; Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — informed me that Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī said: \While we were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he was distributing a share"
"16709","(16703) Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd — narrated to us; my father — informed me, he said: I heard al-Awzāʿī say — and Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf — narrated to us; Abū al-Mughīrah — narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī — narrated to us, and the ḥadīth is from al-ʿAbbās; Qatādah — narrated to me, from Anas ibn Mālik and from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There will be in my Ummah disagreement and division — a people who will excel in speech and fail in action. They will recite the Qurʾān"
"16710","(16704) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl — in Baghdad, informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Sharīk — narrated to us; Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād — narrated to us; Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān — narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: It was said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16711","(16705) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, from his father, that it reached him from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: It was said to the Prophet ﷺ, \Would you go to ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy?\"" So the Prophet ﷺ set out riding a donkey"
"16712","(16706) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation; Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Zāhid narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Mahdī ibn Rustam narrated to us; Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah al-Qurashī narrated to us; my father narrated to me. And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated us; al-Ḥajjāj ibn Abī Manīʿ narrated to us; my grandfather narrated to us, and Yaʿqūb narrated to me; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Yūnus — all from al-Zuhrī. And this is the wording of the ḥadīth of Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah from al-Zuhrī: Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar informed me that while he was sitting with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, a man from the people of Iraq came to him and said: \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"
"16713","(16707) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from his father, from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: \I have not seen anything from which this nation has turned away more than this verse: {And if two groups of the believers fight"
"16714","(16708) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated to us, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Hour will not be established until two great factions fight one another"
"16715","(16709) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī and Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; they said: Sufyān narrated to us; Isrāʾīl Abū Mūsā narrated to us; he said: I heard al-Ḥasan say: I heard Abū Bakrah say: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon the minbar"
"16716","(16710) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd and Ādam narrated to us; they said: al-Mubārak narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan, from Abī Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and he mentioned something similar to the ḥadīth of Sufyān. Ādam added: al-Ḥasan said: \When al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī"
"16717","(16711) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Salamah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Ibn Sīrīn, that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: \Were you to look between Jābars and Jābilq"
"16718","(16712) And Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us; ʿAbdullāh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Mujālid narrated to us, from al-Shaʿbī.\n\n(Ḥ) And Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Mujālid narrated to us, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: When al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī made peace — and Hushaym said: When al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī surrendered the affair to Muʿāwiyah — Muʿāwiyah said to him at al-Nakhlah: \Stand and speak.\"" So he praised Allah and extolled Him"
"16719","(16713) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, from Sharīk, from Abī al-ʿAnbas, from Abī al-Bakhtarī, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about the people of the Camel: \Are they polytheists?\"" He said: \""They fled from polytheism.\"" It was said: \""Are they hypocrites?\"" He said: \""Indeed"
"16720","(16714) And Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us, from Abān ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī, from Nuʿaym ibn Abī Hind, from Ribʿī ibn Ḥirāsh, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I hope that I"
"16721","(16715) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us: Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Saʿdī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī narrated to us: Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī narrated from Abū Ḥabībah, the freedman of Ṭalḥah, who said: I entered upon ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) along with ʿImrān ibn Ṭalḥah after he had finished with the companions of the Camel. He welcomed him and drew him close, and said: \I hope that Allah will place me and your father among those about whom Allah"
"16722","(16716) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Hāshim al-Baghawī and Abū al-Qāsim al-Manīʿī both said: ʿAlī, i.e. ibn al-Jaʿd, informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Abū Wāʾil, who said: I heard ʿAmmār (may Allah be pleased with him) say when ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) sent him to al-Kūfah to mobilize the people: \We know that she is the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in this world and the Hereafter"
"16723","(16717) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Bundār narrated to us: Muḥammad narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, who said: I heard Abū Wāʾil say: When ʿAlī sent ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir and al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with them) to al-Kūfah to mobilize them, ʿAmmār delivered a speech and said: \I know that she is his wife in this world and the Hereafter"
"16724","(16718) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to us: ʿAwf narrated from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: Khālid ibn al-Wāshimah said: When the affair of the companions of the Camel was concluded and ʿĀʾishah had settled in her dwelling, I entered upon her and said: \Peace be upon you"
"16725","(16719) Abū Muḥammad informed us: Abū Saʿīd informed us: Saʿdān narrated to us: Isḥāq narrated to us: Ibn ʿAwn narrated from Ibn Sīrīn from Khālid ibn al-Wāshimah, similarly. And it was also narrated by Ayyūb from Ibn Sīrīn."
"16726","(16720) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥawshab narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Abū Wāʾil, who said: ʿAmr ibn Sharḥbīl, who was among the most eminent of the companions of ʿAbdullāh, said: \I saw as though I had entered Paradise"
"16727","(16721) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Miṣʿar narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabāḥ that ʿAmmār (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Do not say that the people of Shām have disbelieved"
"16728","(16722) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Sadīrī in Khusrawjird informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Khusrawjirdī narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us: Ḥumayd ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Miṣʿar narrated from ʿĀmir ibn Shaqīq, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, who said: A man said: \Who can recognize the mule on the day the polytheists were killed — meaning the people of al-Nahrawān?\"" ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib said: \""They fled from polytheism.\"" He said: \""Then were they hypocrites?\"" He said: \""The hypocrites do not remember Allah except a little.\"" He said: \""Then what were they?\"" He said: \""A people who rebelled against us"
"16729","(16723) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \The first fitnah erupted and caught — meaning the fitnah caught — a number of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) who had witnessed Badr with him. And it has reached us that they held the view that the matter of the fitnah should be disregarded"
"16730","(16724) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, who said: \Sulaymān ibn Hishām wrote to him asking about a woman who separated from her husband"
"16731","(16725) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar; Sayf ibn Fulān ibn Muʿāwiyah al-ʿAnazī narrated to me; my maternal uncle narrated from my grandfather, who said: On the day of the Battle of the Camel, when the rope became tangled and the people launched their assault, the people came to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) making various claims, and they overwhelmed him with so much that he could not understand. He said: \Is there no one who can summarise their speech for me in five or six words?\"" I braced myself on one of my feet and said: \""If he understood my words before"
"16732","(16726) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: \This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us"
"16733","(16727) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār, who said: \The first apostasy that occurred among the Arabs was that of Musaylimah in al-Yamāmah among Banī Ḥanīfah"
"16734","(16728) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdad; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; al-Ḥajjaj ibn Abī Manīʿ narrated to us; my grandfather narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: \When Allah made Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) the Caliph"
"16735","(16729) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī and ʿĪsā ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī both said: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Wahb narrated from al-Nuʿmān ibn Buzurj, who said: \al-Aswad the Liar emerged. He was a man from Banī ʿAns. He had two devils with him — one was called Saḥīq and the other Shuqayq — and they used to inform him of everything that happened among the people's affairs. al-Aswad travelled until he secured his protection. He narrated a lengthy account concerning his situation and his marriage to al-Marzbānah"
"16736","(16730) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd narrated to me from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away and Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was appointed Caliph after him"
"16737","(16731) al-Shāfiʿī and others narrated from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from Ibn Shihāb that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him): \Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: \""There is no god but Allah.\"" When they say it"
"16738","(16732) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʢĀṣim al-Kilābī narrated to us; ʿImrān ibn Dāwar al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Maʿmar ibn Rāshid narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away"
"16739","(16733) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah al-Shaybānī narrated to us in Kūfah; al-Haytham ibn Khālid narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAnbas Saʿīd ibn Kathīr narrated to me; my father narrated from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah"
"16740","(16734) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Abū al-Naḍr Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no god but Allah"
"16741","(16735) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Musnadī narrated to us: Ḥarmī ibn ʿUmarah narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Wāqid ibn Muḥammad, who said: I heard my father narrating from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah"
"16742","(16736) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd — who is Ibn Abī ʿArūbah — narrated from Qatādah regarding the statement of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {O you who believe! Whoever among you turns back from his religion, Allah will bring a people whom He loves and who love Him} [Sūrah al-Māʾidah: 54] — the entire verse. He said: \This verse was revealed when Allah already knew that people would become apostates. When Allah took His Messenger (ﷺ)"
"16743","(16737) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān al-Ḥakam ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us: Ṣafwān ibn ʿAmr narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) had dispatched armies after the Prophet (ﷺ), appointing over some of them Sharḥabīl ibn Ḥasanah, Yazīd ibn Abī Sufyān, and ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ. They proceeded until they descended upon Shām, where the Romans gathered for them a tremendous force. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was informed of that, so he sent word to Khālid ibn al-Walīd — who was in al-ʿIrāq — or wrote to him: \Turn back with three thousand horsemen and reinforce your brothers in Shām"
"16744","(16738) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq: Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr al-Ṣiddīq narrated to me, saying: \Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to command his commanders when he sent them during the Riddah: 'When you approach a settlement"
"16745","(16739) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Aḥmad al-Faqīh in Ṭabarān informed us: Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ṣawwāf narrated to us: Abū Yaʿqūb Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Maymūn al-Ḥarbī narrated to us: Abū Ghassān narrated to us: Ziyād al-Bakkāʾī narrated to us: Muṭarrif ibn Ṭarīf narrated from Sulaymān ibn al-Jahm, Abū al-Jahm, the freedman of al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: \ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) sent me to the people of al-Nahrawān — the Khawārij — and I called them to Islam three times before we fought them.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16746","(16740) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us from the original of his book: Abū Umayyah Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ṭarsūsī narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Yūnus ibn al-Qāsim ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Yamāmī narrated to us: ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār al-ʿIjlī narrated to us: Abū Zumayl Simāk al-Ḥanafī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated, saying: \When the Ḥarūriyyah went out"
"16747","(16741) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Hishām ibn ʿAlī al-Sadūsī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym and ʿAbdullāh ibn Wāqid narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād, who said: \I came to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) while we were sitting with her upon her return from al-ʿIrāq during the nights when ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was fought. She said to me: 'O ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād"
"16748","(16742) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbdah al-Salīṭī narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Shāfiʿī said: It was presented to me from Muslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿIyāḍ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād, that he entered upon ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) while we were with her upon his return from al-ʿIrāq during the nights when ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was killed, and he mentioned the hadith similarly.\n\nThe Shaykh al-Imām (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The hadith of al-Thudayyah is a ṣaḥīh hadith, which we have mentioned previously. It is possible that Ibn Shaddād did not hear it, and someone else heard it. And Allah knows best."
"16749","(16743) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Juwayriyah ibn Asmāʾ said — I think he said — from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who said: My uncle, or an uncle of mine, narrated to me, saying: \When we stood arrayed on the day of the Camel"
"16750","(16744) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥurfī narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Qurashī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to me: Jaʿfar ibn Ibrāhīm — from the progeny of ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar Dhī al-Janāḥayn — narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) did not fight the people of the Camel until he called the people for three days. When the third day came, al-Ḥasan, al-Ḥusayn, and ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar (may Allah be pleased with them) came to him and said: \They have inflicted many wounds upon us.\"" He said: \""O son of my brother"
"16751","(16745) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: Abū Maymūnah narrated from Abī Bashīr al-Shaybānī, in the story of the Battle of the Camel, saying: They gathered in Baṣrah, so ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Who will take the Muṣḥaf and say to them: 'What do you find objectionable? You are shedding our blood and your own blood.'\"" A man said: \""I will"
"16752","(16746) In what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us — and I think it was from Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad — from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from his grandfather ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn, who said: \I entered upon Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam and he said: 'I have not seen anyone more honourable in victory than your father"
"16753","(16747) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, who said: \ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) commanded his crier"
"16754","(16748) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us: Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Shādhān narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from al-Suddī, from Yazīd ibn Ḍubiʿah al-ʿAbsī, who said: \The crier of ʿAmmār — or he said ʿAlī — called out on the Day of the Camel"
"16755","(16749) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān, from Abī Isḥāq, from Khumayr ibn Mālik, who said: \I heard ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir ask ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with them both) about the captives of the offspring. He said: 'There is no captivity upon them; we only fought those who fought us.' He said: 'Had you said other than that"
"16756","(16750) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Isfarāyīnī informed us with it: Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Usāmah narrated to us: al-Ṣalt ibn Bahrām narrated from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, who said: \ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) did not take captives on the Day of the Camel"
"16757","(16751) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us: Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Abū Usāmah Ḥammād ibn Usāmah narrated to me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated from his father, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said on the Day of the Camel: \We bestow upon them the testimony that there is no deity but Allah"
"16758","(16752) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Salʿ, from ʿAbd Khayr, who said: \ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the people of the Camel. He said: 'They are our brothers who transgressed against us"
"16759","(16753) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah informed us that Kathīr ibn Hishām narrated to them: Jaʿfar ibn Burqān narrated to us: Maymūn ibn Mihrān narrated from Abī Umāmah, who said: \I witnessed Ṣiffīn"
"16760","(16754) In what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him: from Abī al-ʿAbbās, al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abī Fākhitah, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a captive on the Day of Ṣiffīn, and the captive said: \Do not kill me in cold blood.\"" So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I will not kill you in cold blood; I fear Allah"
"16761","(16755) A mursal hadith has been narrated regarding this, but it is weak.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Yūsuf ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khwārizmī narrated to us, saying: Abū Naṣr al-Tammār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Kharrāz narrated to us, saying: Abū Naṣr al-Tammār narrated to us, saying: Kauthar ibn Ḥakīm narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd: \O Ibn Masʿūd"
"16762","(16756) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us, saying: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, saying: Sulaimān al-Taimī informed us, saying: A man in al-Baḥrayn informed me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaid al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā — that is, ibn Ḥammād — narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAlī ibn Yazīd from Abū Ḥurrah al-Raqāshī from his paternal uncle, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The property of a Muslim man is not lawful for his brother except what he gives willingly with a contented soul.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Taimī. In the narration of al-Raqāshī it reads: \""The property of a man — meaning a Muslim — is not lawful except with his willing consent.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"16763","(16757) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaid informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn al-Haytham al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, saying: Abū Shihāb narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī from ʿArfajah from his father, who said: When ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) killed the people of al-Nahrawān, he moved among their camp. Whatever a person recognized, he took it, until only a cooking pot remained. Then I saw it taken afterwards.\n\nSufyān narrated it from al-Shaybānī from ʿArfajah from his father, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought the remnants of the people of al-Nahrawān, and he had them identified. Whoever recognized something took it, until a cooking pot remained that was not recognized.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from a man of Banī Tamīm, who said: I asked Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) about the wealth of the Khawārij, and he said: \I do not see any ghanīmah (spoils of war) in their wealth.\"" [Weak]"""
"16764","(16758) Abū Saʿīd al-Ṣayrafī informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: Yaʿlā ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Jāmiʿ ibn Shaddād from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qatādah, a man of the tribe, who said: I was among the cavalry on the day of al-Nahrawān with ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him). When he finished with them and killed them, he did not sever a head nor expose a private part."
"16765","(16759) He also cited as evidence what Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaimān informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding Ibn Muljam after he struck him: \Feed him"
"16766","(16760) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, saying: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥajjāj ibn Abī Manīʿ narrated to us, saying: My grandfather narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: When Allah appointed Abū Bakr as khalīfah and those of the Arabs who apostatized turned away from Islam, he mentioned the story of the dispatch of Khālid ibn al-Walīd and his fighting. He said: Ṭulaiḥah was fierce in battle. Ṭulaiḥah killed that day ʿUkāshah ibn Miḥsan and Ibn Aqram. When the truth prevailed over Ṭulaiḥah, he departed, then he accepted Islam and performed an ʿumrah. He rode, travelling among the people in safety, until he passed by Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) in al-Madīnah. Then he proceeded to Makkah and performed his ʿumrah.\n\nIt is mentioned from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that he waived the qiṣāṣ from him. [Ḥasan]"
"16767","(16761) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, saying: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, saying: Qabīṣah narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated from Qays ibn Muslim from Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb, who said: A delegation from Buzākhah — from Asad and Ghaṭafān — came to Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) asking for a peace settlement. He gave them the choice between a war of expulsion or a humiliating peace. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16768","(16762) And Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh informed us, saying: Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaimān narrated from Zakariyyā from Abū Isḥāq from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, who said: ʿAlqamah ibn ʿUlāthah apostatized from his religion after the Prophet (ﷺ) and refused to submit to peace. So Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \We will not accept from you anything but a humiliating peace or a war of expulsion.\"" He said: \""What is a humiliating peace?\"" He said: \""You testify that our slain are in Paradise and that your slain are in the Fire"
"16769","(16763) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah, saying: Abū al-Walīd informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr — that is, Ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us, saying: Ibn Numair narrated from al-Ajlaj from Salamah ibn Kuhail from Kathīr ibn Namir, who said: While I was in the Jumuʿah and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was on the minbar, a man stood and said: \There is no rule except Allah's.\"" Then another stood and said: \""There is no rule except Allah's.\"" Then they stood from all sides of the mosque. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) gestured to them with his hand: \""Sit down. Yes"
"16770","(16764) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Bakr al-Marwazī narrated to us, saying: ʿAffān narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Isḥāq from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) heard a group of people saying: \There is no rule except Allah's.\"" He said: \""Yes"
"16771","(16765) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ḥarmalah informed me: Ibn Wahb informed me: al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed him: that al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd al-Malik sent a message to him asking, \What do you say about one who curses the Caliphs? Do you think he should be killed?\"" He (Ibn Shihāb) said: \""I remained silent.\"" He (al-Walīd) rebuked me and said"
"16772","(16766) Abū Saʿid ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Khālid ibn Ḥumayd al-Mahrī narrated from ʿUmar, the freedman of Ghufrah, that ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd ibn al-Khaṭṭāb was the governor of Kūfah during the era of ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. He wrote to ʿUmar: \I found a man in al-Kunāsah"
"16773","(16767) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī — informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Ibn Mubashshir narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbādah narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated from Abī Mijlaz that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) forbade his companions from attacking the Khawārij until they committed an act (of aggression). They passed by ʿAbdullāh ibn Khabbāb, so they seized him and set off with him. They passed by a fallen date from a palm tree, and one of them picked it up and put it in his mouth. One of them said to him, \It is the date of a dhimmī (non-Muslim under protection). How did you make it lawful for yourself?\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn Khabbāb said"
"16774","(16768) As evidence, from what Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abī ʿImrān, who heard ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ṣāmit narrate from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to listen and obey"
"16775","(16769) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Razīn al-ʿAṭṭār al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Zubaydī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us: Ḥumayd ibn Mālik al-Lakhmī narrated from Makhūl, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O Muʿādh"
"16776","(16770) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Ḥārith, from Makhūl, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Jihād is obligatory upon you with every amir"
"16777","(16771) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz — narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, who said: ʿAmmār (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Bury me in my garments"
"16778","(16772) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Abī Yaʿfūr al-ʿAbdī narrated from his father, from Abī Shaykh al-Muhājir, that Zayd ibn Ṣūḥān al-ʿAbdī was carrying the banner of ʿAbd al-Qays on the Day of the Camel. He fell as a wounded casualty and said: \Do not wash the blood from me"
"16779","(16773) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Qays ibn Muslim, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Saʿīd ibn ʿUbayd, that he stood as a khaṭīb and said: \We shall be martyred tomorrow"
"16780","(16774) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation: Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Jahm narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faraj narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Wāqidī narrated to me: Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, who said: Abū Ḥudhayfah was present at Badr, and his father ʿUtbah called him to single combat, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prevented him from it. Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr al-Ṣiddīq remained upon the religion of his people in polytheism until he was present at Badr with the polytheists and called for single combat. His father, Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him), stood up to duel him. He mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him): \Let us benefit from your life.\"" Then ʿAbd al-Raḥmān embraced Islam during the truce of al-Ḥudaybiyyah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16781","(16775) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us that Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, Ibn Jurayj, and al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us that al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā al-Muṭarriz narrated to us that al-Qāsim ibn Hāshim al-Simsār narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Wuḥāẓī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, Ibn Jurayj, and Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The killer inherits nothing from the estate.\"" And Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated it from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb with his chain of narration in a hadith he mentioned"
"16782","(16776) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed us that Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī informed us that Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwf, from Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is killed while defending his property is a martyr.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16783","(16777) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from his father, from Abū ʿUbaydah ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir, from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwf, from Saʿīd ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is killed while defending his property is a martyr"
"16784","(16778) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us by dictation that Abū Ḥāmad Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed us that Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan, from Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is sought for his property unjustly and fights and is killed"
"16785","(16779) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn al-Munādī, informed us that Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq informed us that ʿAwf al-Aʿrābī narrated from Abū Naḍrah, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \My ummah will split into two groups"
"16786","(16780) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn al-Munādī, informed us that Rūḥ informed us that ʿUthmān al-Shaḥḥām informed us that Muslim ibn Abī Bakrah narrated: A man asked him: \Did you hear anything regarding the Khawārij?\"" He said: \""I heard my father"
"16787","(16781) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī informed us in Baghdad that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān al-Naysābūrī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us that Sufyān informed us that al-Aʿmash narrated from Khaythamah, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \When I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"16788","(16782) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Abū Ghālib, who said: \I was with Abū Umāmah when the heads of the Khawārij were brought and placed upon the steps of Damascus. He said: 'Dogs of the Fire.' He said it three times. 'The worst of those killed under the shade of the sky"
"16789","(16783) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us that Ḥammād, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated from Abū Ghālib, who said: \I was in al-Shām when al-Muhallab sent sixty heads of the Khawārij"
"16790","(16784) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Hishām narrated from Muḥammad, from ʿUbaydah, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, regarding the people of al-Nahrawān: \Among them is a man with a deformed hand"
"16791","(16785) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, who said: \I do not know of anyone who disliked fighting thieves and the Khawārij out of scrupulous avoidance of sin"
"16792","(16786) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Subʿiyy both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Saʿīd ibn Abī al-Ḥasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ, said to ʿAmmār: \You will be killed by the rebellious faction.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16793","(16787) He said: And Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ḥasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, and he mentioned a similar narration."
"16794","(16788) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us, and he mentioned something similar to it, except that he said: \from Saʿīd ibn Abī al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥasan"
"16795","(16789) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, from al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl, Shuʿbah narrated from Abī Maslamah, from Abī Naḍrah, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: \One who is better than me — Abū Qatādah — narrated to me that the Prophet"
"16796","(16790) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from his father, who said: \I do not know whether he was with his father or whether his father informed him.\"" He said: \""When ʿAmmār"
"16797","(16791) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khālid narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah, from his father, that the Prophet, ﷺ, said: \Do not return after me to misguidance"
"16798","(16792) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Naḍr al-Jārūdī narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah al-Ḍabbī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyūb, Yūnus, and al-Muʿallā narrated from al-Ḥasan, from al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays, from Abī Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ, said: \When two Muslims meet with their swords"
"16799","(16793) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Mūsā al-Ḥunaynī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyūb and Yūnus narrated from al-Ḥasan, from al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays, who said: \I set out to support this man"
"16800","(16794) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Karābīsī narrated to us in Bukhārā, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Abū Kāmil al-Jaḥdarī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, and he mentioned it with the same meaning, except that he said: \I said: 'I intend to support the cousin of the Messenger of Allah"
"16801","(16795) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed me that Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir narrated to us that Busr ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us that he heard Abū Idrīs al-Khawlānī say: I heard Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān say: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about good, but I used to ask him about evil, fearing that it might overtake me. So I said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16802","(16796) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us from his father from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There will be a tribulation (fitnah) or tribulations in which the sleeper will be better than the one who is awake"
"16803","(16797) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, that is Ibn al-Munādī, narrated to us that Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʔUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us that Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us that ʿUthmān al-Shaḥḥām narrated to us that Muslim ibn Abī Bakrah narrated to us from his father, Abū Bakrah, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \There will be tribulations"
"16804","(16798) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us by dictation that Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Dūlabī narrated to us that Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us from Abī ʿImrān al-Jawnī from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ṣāmit from Abū Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O Abū Dharr"
"16805","(16799) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us from Abī ʿImrān from al-Mushaʿith ibn Ṭarīf from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ṣāmit from Abū Dharr, and he mentioned the hadith with the same meaning, except that he said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16806","(16800) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Juḥādah from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Tharwān from Huzayl from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of a dark night. A man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever by evening"
"16807","(16801) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Muḥammad al-Zuhrī narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us that Sālim ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated to us from his father from Maḥmūd ibn Labīd from Muḥammad ibn Maslamah, who said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16808","(16802) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us that ʿUbayd ibn ʿUbaydah narrated to us that Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated to us from his father from Sulaymān al-Aʿmash from Shaqīq ibn Salamah from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl from ʿAbd Allāh from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \A man will come holding another man by the hand and say: 'O Lord"
"16809","(16803) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad al-ʿAmmī narrated to us that Abī ʿImrān al-Jawnī said: I said to Jundub: \Ibn al-Zubayr has taken my pledge of allegiance that I will fight whoever fights and wage war against whoever wages war"
"16810","(16804) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated to us from Abī Ẓabyān who narrated to us that Usāmah ibn Zayd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition to al-Ḥurqāt. They were warned and fled, and we caught up with a man. When we overtook him, he said: \Lā ilāha illā Allāh (There is no god but Allah).\"" We struck him until we killed him. Something of that troubled my mind"
"16811","(16805) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-ʿAdl informed me; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: that two men came to him during the tribulation (fitnah) of Ibn al-Zubayr and said, \The people have done what you see"
"16812","(16806) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb al-Razjāhī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Nājiyah narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Jarwī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā al-Maʿāfirī narrated to us; Ḥaywah ibn Shurayḥ narrated from Bakr ibn ʿAmr from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ashajj from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him: that a man came to him and said, \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"
"16813","(16807) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Sarī ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated from Bayān that Wahb narrated to him; he said: Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrated to me, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar came out to us while we were hoping that he would narrate to us a fine hadith. We passed by a man called Ḥakīm, who said, \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"
"16814","(16808) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Ibn ʿUthmān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh — that is, Ibn al-Mubārak — informed us; Kahmas ibn al-Ḥasan narrated from Abī al-Azhar al-Ḍubaʿī from Abī al-ʿĀliyah al-Barrāʾ: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣafwān were one day sitting in the Ḥijr when Ibn ʿUmar passed by them performing ṭawāf around the House. One of them said to his companion, \Do you think there remains anyone better than this man?\"" Then he said to a man"
"16815","(16809) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Ibn ʿUthmān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh informed us; al-Mundhir ibn Thaʿlabah narrated to me; Saʿīd ibn Ḥarb al-ʿAbdī narrated, saying: I was sitting with ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar in the Masjid al-Ḥarām during the time of Ibn al-Zubayr, and the leaders of the Khawārij — Nāfiʿ ibn al-Azraq, ʿAṭiyyah ibn al-Aswad, and Najdah — were in obedience to Ibn al-Zubayr. They — or some of them — sent a young man to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar [to ask], \What prevents you from pledging allegiance to ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr"
"16816","(16810) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Ibn ʿUthmān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh informed us; ʿAwf narrated from Abī al-Minhāl, saying: When the time came in which Ibn Ziyād was expelled, Marwān rose in Shām, Ibn al-Zubayr rose in Makkah, and those who were called the Qurraʾ rose in Baṣrah, my father was overcome with intense grief. He said, \Go — may you have no father — to this man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"
"16817","(16811) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnns ibn al-Musayyab al-Ḍabbī narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim and ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī, who both said: Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam said to Ayman ibn Khuraym, \Will you not come out and fight with us?\"" He said"
"16818","(16812) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd al-Taymī from his father from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \The covenant of the Muslims is one; the lowest among them may act on its behalf. Whoever betrays a Muslim"
"16819","(16813) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah and ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Khaffāf both said: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us.\n\n(Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī also informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to me; Yaḥyā narrated from Saʿīd from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan from Qays ibn ʿUbād, who said): I and al-Ashtar came to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, on the Day of the Camel. I said, \Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoin upon you a special covenant beyond the general one?\"" He said"
"16820","(16814) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash; he said: I heard Ibrāhīm narrating from al-Aswad from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \A woman would grant protection (tujīr) on behalf of the Muslims.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16821","(16815) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAnbasah ibn ʿAmr al-Yashkurī narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Makkī, from the progeny of ʿAbd al-Dār, narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbāy (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A slave shall not be given anything from the war booty"
"16822","(16816) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Sulaymān, from Fuḍayl ibn Zayd — and he had fought seven military expeditions during the era of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) — who said, and he mentioned the hadith, saying: \When we returned"
"16823","(16817) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Ṭabbāʿ informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who narrated to me: Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah both said: \We were with ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) in the house while he was under siege. When we entered"
"16824","(16818) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Yazīd informed us: Abū Badr Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd informed us: Sulaymān ibn Mihrān narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Murrah, from Masrūq, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except in one of three cases: a life for a life"
"16825","(16819) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān, from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Murrah, from Masrūq, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood among us and said: \By the One besides whom there is no god"
"16826","(16820) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah, from ʿIkrimah, who said: When Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) learned that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) had burned the apostates — or the heretics — he said: \Had it been me"
"16827","(16821) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Mālik, Dāwūd ibn Qays, and Hishām ibn Saʿ narrated — (ḥ) and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever changes his religion"
"16828","(16822) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥārithī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān informed us — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and Musaddad both said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated — Musaddad said: Qurrah ibn Khālid narrated to us: Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl narrated to us: Abū Burdah narrated, who said: Abū Mūsā said: \I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and with me were two men from the Ashʿarīs"
"16829","(16823) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Naṣr al-Dārabardī and al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥalīm in Marw both said: Abū al-Muwajjah informed us: ʿAbdān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh — that is, Ibn al-Mubārak — narrated from Yūnus, from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī, then al-Jundaʿī, narrated to me that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAdī ibn al-Khiyār informed him that Miqdād ibn ʿAmr al-Kindī — who was an ally of Banū Zuhrah and was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — informed him that he said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16830","(16824) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd informed us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Abī Ẓabyān, who said: Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us on a military expedition to al-Ḥuruqāt. They were warned and fled. We caught up with a man"
"16831","(16825) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan — and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAdī ibn al-Khayyār, that a man spoke privately to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he (ʿUbayd Allāh) did not know what he was saying to him, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke openly, and it turned out that he was asking his permission to kill a man from among the hypocrites. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Does he not bear witness that there is no deity but Allah?\"" He said: \""Yes"
"16832","(16826) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī narrated to us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAdī ibn al-Khayyār, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAdī narrated to him: that the Prophet ﷺ was sitting with his Companions when a man came and asked permission to speak to him privately. He granted him permission, and he spoke to him privately about killing a man from among the hypocrites. The Prophet ﷺ then spoke openly and said: \Does he not bear witness that there is no deity but Allah?\"" He said: \""Yes"
"16833","(16827) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity but Allah.' When they say it"
"16834","(16828) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: al-Firyābī narrated to us. Both said: Sufyān narrated from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity but Allah.' When they say 'There is no deity but Allah"
"16835","(16829) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation: Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us in Marw: Ibrāhīm ibn Hilāl narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated from Yazīd al-Naḥwī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Sarḥ used to write for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but Satan caused him to slip, so he joined the disbelievers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he be killed, but ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, sought protection for him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him protection. [Weak]"
"16836","(16830) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī narrated to us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A man from the Anṣār apostatized and joined the polytheists. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their faith and bore witness that the Messenger is true} [Āl ʿImrān 3:86] up to His words: {except those who repent} [Āl ʿImrān 3:89]. He said: His people wrote it to him, and when it was read to him, he said: \By Allah"
"16837","(16831) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Baṣrī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim al-Muʿaddal narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Abū Hammām Muḥammad ibn Muḥabbab narrated to us: Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from Ḥārithah ibn Muḍarrib, from Furāt ibn Ḥayyān, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered his killing, and he had been a spy for Abū Sufyān. He passed by a gathering of the Anṣār and said: \I am a Muslim.\"" This reached the Prophet ﷺ"
"16838","(16832) Al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh narrated it from Abī Isḥāq, from Ḥārithah ibn Muḍarrib, that Furāt ibn Ḥayyān apostatized during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who intended to kill him, but he bore witness to the testimony of truth, so he let him go, and his Islam became good. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj narrated it.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said: And it makes no difference how often that occurs from him, even if it be time after time, with regard to the preservation of blood."
"16839","(16833) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from a man, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted the repentance of Nabhān four times, and Nabhān had apostatized.\n\nSufyān said: And ʿAmr ibn Qays said from a man, from Ibrāhīm, that he said: \The apostate is asked to repent every time he returns.\""\n\nIbn Wahb said: And Mālik told me that: \""He is asked to repent every time he returns.\"" This is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ)"
"16840","(16834) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us. He said: I read to Abū al-Yamān that Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated to him from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that Abū Hurayrah said: \We witnessed Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about a man who claimed Islam: 'This one is among the people of the Fire.' When the fighting commenced"
"16841","(16835) The Shaykh, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: And in a similar vein, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Abdullah ibn Ya'qub informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad informed us, Abbas ibn Abdul-Azim al-Anbari informed us, al-Nadr ibn Muhammad informed us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar informed me — and he is Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa' — my father informed me, saying: We visited a man suffering from fever along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I placed my hand upon him and said, \By Allah"
"16842","(16836) And Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri informed us, al-Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan informed us, Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj informed us from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Qays ibn Ubad, who said: I said to Ammar, \What do you think of this action of yours regarding the matter of Ali — is it an opinion you have formed"
"16843","(16837) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us, al-Shafi'i informed us, Sufyan informed us from al-Zuhri, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I witnessed three gatherings in which the hypocrisy of Abdullah ibn Ubayy was evident. [Da'if]"
"16844","(16838) Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan informed us, Ahmad ibn Ubayd al-Saffar informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Milhan informed us, Amr ibn Khalid informed us, Zuhayr informed us, Abu Ishaq informed us from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey in which the people experienced great hardship. Abdullah ibn Ubayy said to his companions: \Do not spend upon those who are with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they disperse from around him.\"" And he said"
"16845","(16839) And Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar informed us, Yunus ibn Bukayr informed us from Ibn Ishaq, regarding the story of Tabuk and what occurred at al-Thaniyyah of the plot of the hypocrites to crowd the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there, and what was said among their statements, and Allah, glorified be He, informing His Prophet ﷺ of their secrets. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from al-Thaniyyah and said to his two companions — meaning Hudhayfah and Ammar: \Do you know what the people intended?\"" They said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""They intended to crowd me at al-Thaniyyah and throw me from it.\"" They said: \""Will you not command us"
"16846","(16840) Abu Amr al-Bistami informed us, Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us, al-Qasim — he is ibn Zakariyya — informed us, Abbas informed us, Musa ibn Dawud informed us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath informed us from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, who said: Hudhayfah stood over us while we were with Abdullah, and he said: \Hypocrisy has descended upon those who were better than you.\"" He said: We said"
"16847","(16841) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Hamid al-Qari' both said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Burlusi informed us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih informed us, Abu Shahab informed us from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, who both said: We were with Abdullah when Hudhayfah passed by us and said: \Hypocrisy has descended upon those who were better than you.\"" We said: \""Glory be to Allah!\"" Abdullah laughed and went on. Then Hudhayfah passed by us again and threw pebbles at me. I went to him and he said: \""Your companion knew something and laughed. Hypocrisy descended upon them"
"16848","(16842) As for the statement of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to His Prophet ﷺ regarding the hypocrites: {And never pray over any of them who dies, nor stand at his grave} — the cause of the revelation of this verse is what Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Ja'far ibn Salih ibn Hani' informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar both said: Yahya informed us from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The son of Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when his father died and said: \Give me your shirt so that I may shroud him in it"
"16849","(16843) Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan informed us, Ahmad ibn Ubayd al-Saffar informed us, Ubayd ibn Sharik al-Bazzar informed us, Yahya — meaning ibn Bukayr — informed us, al-Layth informed us from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was called to pray over him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, I leapt toward him and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16850","(16844) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad, Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri, in the story of Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman. He said: Hudhayfah said: While the Prophet ﷺ was traveling toward Tabuk, he dismounted from his mount to receive revelation, and the Prophet ﷺ halted his mount. The she-camel bolted, dragging her reins, and Hudhayfah intercepted her, took hold of her reins, and led her until he halted her. He sat beside her. Then the Prophet ﷺ arose and came toward his she-camel and said: \Who is this?\"" Hudhayfah said: \""Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""I am confiding to you a secret that you must never relate to anyone: I have been forbidden to pray over so-and-so and so-and-so\"" — a group of numbered men from among the hypocrites. He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away and Umar"
"16851","(16845) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk and Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān both said: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, saying: It reached us that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on the expedition to Tabūk, he dismounted from his mount and revelation came to him, while his mount was kneeling. It began dragging its reins until Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān encountered it. He took hold of its reins and led it until he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting. He made it kneel and then sat beside it until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arose. He went to him and said: \Who is this?\"" Ḥudhayfah said: \""Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""I am entrusting you with a matter"
"16852","(16846) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk in Baghdād narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl — (ḥ) and Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: Ḥudhayfah said: \There remain of the people of this verse only three\"" — I think he was referring to His statement {Fight the leaders of disbelief} [al-Tawbah: 12]. He said: \""And there remain of the hypocrites only four.\"" He said: \""There was a Bedouin sitting behind us.\"" He said: \""O company of the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ"
"16853","(16847) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Wāṣil al-Aḥdab, from Abū Wāʾil, from Ḥudhayfah, who said: \Indeed"
"16854","(16848) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Salamah narrated from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Abī ʿAwn, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken [in death]"
"16855","(16849) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Ibn Lahīʿah informed me from Abī al-Aswad, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) commanded Khālid ibn al-Walīd, when he sent him against those among the Arabs who had apostatized, to call them with the call of Islam, to inform them of what was for them and what was upon them, and to strive for their guidance. Whoever responded to him among all the people—their red and their black—he would accept that from him, for he only fought those who disbelieved in Allah after faith in Allah. When those called to Islam responded and their faith was confirmed, there was no way against them, and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, was their reckoner. And whoever did not respond to what he was called to from Islam, among those who turned away from it, he was to be killed. [Weak]"
"16856","(16850) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from al-Zuhrī. Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Indeed"
"16857","(16851) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ narrated, and al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said to a man who had manifested Islam and was known for it: \I think you are one seeking refuge.\"" He said: \""Islam has not granted me refuge.\"" He said: \""Indeed"
"16858","(16852) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us; Yūnus informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd arrested in Kūfah men who were spreading the ḥadīth of Musaylimah the Liar, calling people to them. He wrote to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) about them, and ʿUthmān wrote: \Present to them the religion of truth and the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah. Whoever accepts these and dissociates himself from Musaylimah"
"16859","(16853) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Saʿd ibn Yazīd al-Farrāʾ narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Simāk, from Qābūs ibn al-Mukhāriq, from his father, that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr wrote to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) asking him about Muslim heretics (zanādiqah). ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \As for the heretics"
"16860","(16854) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated from al-Layth ibn Saʿd, from ʿAbd Rabbih ibn Saʿīd, who said: I heard Ibn Shihāb say: \The heretic (zindīq)—if he denies and proof is established against him"
"16861","(16855) He said: And Ibn Wahb narrated to us from al-Layth from Rabi'ah that he said regarding the heretic (al-zindiq): \He is to be killed and no repentance is to be sought from him.\"" [Sahih. From Rabi'ah]"""
"16862","(16856) He said: And Ibn Wahb informed us, and he said: Malik said: \No repentance is to be sought from him.\"" The Shaykh"
"16863","(16857) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Zakariyya — Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Anbari and Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hafiz both said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Bushanjiyy narrated to us; Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us; Ruh ibn al-Qasim narrated from al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and believe in me and in that which I have brought. When they do that"
"16864","(16858) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar informed us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zaid narrated from Ayyub from 'Ikrimah that 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a group of heretics (al-zanadiqah), so he burned them with fire. That reached Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: \As for me"
"16865","(16859) And Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Ya'qub narrated to us.\n\n(And) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid informed us; Isma'il al-Qadi said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated from Ayyub from 'Ikrimah, similar to this, and he added in it: \That reached 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)"
"16866","(16860) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' al-Isfara'ini narrated to us there; Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated from Hisham al-Dastawa'i from Qatadah from Anas that 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought some people from the Zutt who were worshipping an idol, so he burned them with fire. Ibn 'Abbas said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) only said: 'Whoever changes his religion"
"16867","(16861) Abu Muhammad — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal al-Masrajisiyy informed us; Abu 'Uthman — 'Amr ibn 'Abd Allah al-Basri informed us; Abu Ahmad — Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Ya'la ibn 'Ubaid informed us; al-A'mash narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Murrah from Masruq from 'Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The blood of a man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful to shed except in one of three cases: a life for a life"
"16868","(16862) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr al-Qattan informed us; Abu al-Azhar informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddl informed us; Asbat ibn Nasa narrated; al-Suddiyy claimed from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from his father who said: \On the day of the Conquest of Makkah"
"16869","(16863) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid informed us; Muhammad ibn Yunus informed us; Abu 'Asim narrated from 'Uthman al-Shahham from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas that a slave woman (umm walad) of a man reviled the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so he killed her. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) proclaimed: \Her blood is lawful to shed (hadar).\""\n\nIsrael also narrated it from 'Uthman al-Shahham in full"
"16870","(16864) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak from Ma'mar from Simak ibn al-Fadl from 'Urwah ibn Muhammad from a man from Balqin that a woman reviled the Prophet (ﷺ), so Khalid ibn al-Walid (may Allah be pleased with him) killed her. [Da'if]"
"16871","(16865) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Silm al-Bazzāz narrated to us; al-Khalīl ibn Maymūn narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Udhaynah narrated from Hishām ibn al-Ghāzī from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir, who said: A woman apostatized from Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded that Islam be presented to her, and if she did not accept, she would be killed. They presented it to her, but she refused except to be killed, so she was killed.\n\nIn this chain of narration there are some who are unknown, and it has been narrated from another route from Ibn al-Munkadir. [Weak]"
"16872","(16866) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Baṭḥā narrated to us; Najīḥ ibn Ibrāhīm al-Zuhrī narrated to us; Maʿmarr ibn Bakkār al-Saʿdī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from al-Zuhrī from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir: that a woman called Umm Marwān apostatized from Islam, so the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded that Islam be presented to her; if she returned [to Islam], [well], otherwise she would be killed. [Weak]"
"16873","(16867) He said: and ʿAlī informed us; Ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUtbah narrated to us; Maʿmarr ibn Bakkār narrated with his chain of narration the same.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from the nephew of al-Zuhrī from his uncle with the same meaning.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from another weak route from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). And this is the verified position of al-Zuhrī from him."
"16874","(16868) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us of it; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmarr from al-Zuhrī regarding the woman who disbelieves after her Islam, he said: She shall be asked to repent; if she repents, [well], otherwise she shall be killed.\n\nAnd from Maʿmarr from Saʿīd from Abū Maʿshir from Ibrāhīm regarding the woman who apostatizes, he said: She shall be asked to repent; if she repents, [well], otherwise she shall be killed.\n\n[Sound. From al-Zuhrī]"
"16875","(16869) As for the hadith which Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Abū Yaḥyā al-Ḥimyānī narrated from Abū Ḥanīfah from ʿĀṣim ibn Abī al-Najūd from Abī Rāzin from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Women shall not be killed when they apostatize from Islam. [Weak]"
"16876","(16870) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn al-Muʾammal narrated to us; al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated, he said: I asked Sufyān about the hadith of ʿĀṣim regarding the female apostate, and he said: It is not from a trustworthy narrator. [Sound. From Sufyān]"
"16877","(16871) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī said: Some people differed with us regarding the female apostate, and their argument was something narrated from ʿĀṣim from Abī Rāzin from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the woman who apostatizes from Islam: she shall be imprisoned and not killed. Some of those who follow this position spoke to me, and in our presence were a group of scholars of hadith, so I asked them about this hadith, and I did not know a single one among them who refrained from saying: \This is an error"
"16878","(16872) Perhaps he intended what Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Khālid ibn Yazīd ibn Abī Mālik al-Dimashqī narrated to me; my father narrated to me: that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) killed a woman called Umm Qirfah for apostasy.\n\nAnd that has been narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Mālik from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab from Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). [Weak]"
"16879","(16873) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to me; al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Tanūkhī: that a woman called Umm Qirfah disbelieved after her Islam, so Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) asked her to repent, but she did not repent, so he killed her. [Weak]\n\nAl-Layth said: \And that which we heard is my opinion.\"" Ibn Wahb said: \""And Mālik said the same to me.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""It is not for us to use it as evidence"
"16880","(16874) Abū Saʿīd narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Baḥr narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to me; ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to him: that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: \Whoever disbelieves after his Islam willingly"
"16881","(16875) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me that my father narrated to me that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Shaybah narrated — and ʿAbdullāh said, \I heard it myself from ʿAbdullāh\"" — that Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from Dāwūd"
"16882","(16876) Its explanation is in what Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, that Abū Dāwūd informed us, that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us, that Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from his father, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Shaʿbī, from Jarīr, who said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \When a slave flees to the domain of shirk"
"16883","(16877) By way of evidence, through the apparent meaning of what Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, that Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn informed us, that ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated from Hishām, from Qatādah, from Anas, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever changes his religion"
"16884","(16878) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us. He said: I said to Mālik: Did Ibn Shihāb narrate to you from Anas ibn Mālik that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Makkah on the Year of the Conquest and upon his head was a helmet (mighfar)? When he removed it, a man came and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16885","(16879) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original manuscript that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us that Abū al-Azhar informed us that Aḥmad ibn al-Mufaḍḍal informed us that Asbāṭ ibn Naṣr narrated — al-Suddī claimed, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from his father, who said: On the day of the Conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted safety to the people except for four men and two women, and he said: \Kill them even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Kaʿbah: ʿIkrimah ibn Abī Jahl"
"16886","(16880) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us that Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: The order regarding Ibn Abī Sarḥ was issued because he had embraced Islam and used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), but then he apostatized and joined the polytheists and went to Makkah. The order to kill ʿAbdullāh ibn Khaṭal was issued because he had been a Muslim. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had sent him as a collector of ṣadaqah (alms), and sent with him a man from the Anṣār, along with a freed servant who served him and was a Muslim. They halted at a place, and he ordered the freed servant to slaughter a goat and prepare food for him. The servant fell asleep. When he awoke, he had not prepared anything for him, so he attacked him and killed him. He then apostatized and became a polytheist. He had two singing slave-girls who used to sing satirical verses abusing the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so he ordered that they be killed along with him. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16887","(16881) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us that Qurrah ibn Khālid informed us that Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl informed us that Abū Burdah narrated from Abū Mūsā, who said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) accompanied by two men from the Ashʿarīs. He mentioned the hadith until he said: He (Abū Mūsā) sent him to Yemen, then sent Muʿādh ibn Jabal after him. When Muʿādh arrived, he threw a cushion for him and said: \Dismount.\"" He found a man bound there. He said: \""What is this?\"" He replied: \""This one was a Jew who embraced Islam"
"16888","(16882) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī informed us that al-Ḥimmānī — meaning ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — narrated from Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā and Burayd ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Burdah, from Abī Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, who said: Muʿādh (may Allah be pleased with him) came to me while I was in Yemen, and there was a man who had been a Jew, then embraced Islam, then apostatized from Islam. When Muʿādh arrived, he said: \I shall not dismount from my mount until he is killed.\"" So he was killed. One of the two narrators said: He had been given the opportunity to repent before that. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16889","(16883) Abū ʿAlī informed us that Abū Bakr informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ informed us that Ḥafṣ informed us that al-Shaybānī narrated from Abī Burdah, with this same story, and said: Abū Mūsā was brought a man who had apostatized from Islam. He called him to repent for twenty nights, or nearly that. Then Muʿādh came and called him, but he refused, so he struck his neck (and killed him).\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr narrated it from Abī Burdah and did not mention the opportunity to repent (istitābah).\n\nIbn Fuḍayl narrated it from al-Shaybānī, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah, from his father, from Abū Mūsā, and did not mention the opportunity to repent in it.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And it has been narrated to us from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) that he ordered Khālid ibn al-Walīd, when he was sent to those Arabs who had apostatized, to call them with the call of Islam. Whoever responded, that would be accepted from him; and whoever did not respond to what he was called to from Islam — meaning whoever persisted in his apostasy — he was to be killed. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16890","(16884) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, who said: ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) used to call the apostate to repent three times, then kill him. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16891","(16885) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us — Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Badayl narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Hadrami narrated to us — Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr said: I was present with Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) when his brother from Banu 'Ijil, al-Mustawrid ibn Qabisah, was brought before him. He had apostatized after his Islam. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \What has been reported about you?\"" He replied: \""What has been reported about me?\"" He said: \""It has been reported to me that you have become a Christian.\"" He said: \""I am upon the religion of the Messiah.\"" Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) then said: \""I am upon the religion of the Messiah.\"" Then Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""What do you say about him?\"" He then uttered something unintelligible to me. Ali said: \""Tread upon him!\"" So he was trampled until he died. I said to the one beside me: \""What did he say?\"" He said: \""He said: 'The Messiah is his Lord.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"16892","(16886) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-'Anbari informed us — my grandfather, Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi, narrated to us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Yahya ibn Durust ibn Ziyad narrated to us — Abu 'Awanah narrated from Abu Ishaq — from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, who said: I prayed the morning prayer with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him). When he gave the salam, a man stood up and informed him that he had gone to the mosque of Bani Hanifah — the mosque of Abdullah ibn al-Nawwah — and heard their mu'adhdhin testify that there is no god but Allah and that Musaylimah the Liar is the Messenger of Allah, and that he had heard the people of the mosque [saying] that. Abdullah said: \Who is here?\"" A group leapt up and said: \""Bring Ibn al-Nawwah and his companions.\"" They were brought while I was sitting there. Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said to Abdullah ibn al-Nawwah: \""Where did you used to recite from the Qur'an?\"" He said: \""I used to frighten you with it.\"" He said: \""Then repent.\"" He refused. He then ordered Qarazah ibn Ka'b al-Ansari to take him out to the market and strike his head. I heard Abdullah say: \""Whoever would like to see Ibn al-Nawwah slain in the market"
"16893","(16887) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Malik narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Qari —\n\n(And) Abu al-Mihrajani informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakka narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanji narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Malik narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Qari — from his father, who said: A man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) from the direction of Abu Musa. He asked him about the people, and he informed him. Then he said: \Has there come to you any extraordinary news?\"" He said: \""Yes"
"16894","(16888) The Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Another hadith has been narrated regarding being leisurely with him from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) with a connected isnad. Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan in Baghdad informed us — Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us — Malik ibn Yahya narrated to us — Ali ibn 'Asim narrated — from Dawud ibn Abi Hind — from 'Amir — from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When we descended upon Tustar — and he mentioned the hadith regarding the conquest and his arrival before Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) — Umar said: \O Anas"
"16895","(16889) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us — Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us — Waki' narrated — from Sufyan — from Jabir — from 'Amir — from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The apostate is granted repentance three times. Then he recited: {Indeed, those who believed, then disbelieved, then believed, then disbelieved, and then increased in disbelief} [al-Nisa' 137]. [Da'if]"
"16896","(16890) And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Hafiz al-Isbahani informed us — Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us — Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated — from al-Ash'ath — from al-Sha'bi, who said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \The apostate is granted repentance three times; if he returns"
"16897","(16891) He said, and Abu Bakr narrated to us — Waki' narrated — from Sufyan — from Abd al-Karim — from one who heard Ibn Umar saying: \The apostate is granted repentance three times.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16898","(16892) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Ibn Lahi'ah narrated — from Yazid ibn Abi Habib — that Abu Ali al-Hamdani narrated to them: They were with Fadalah ibn 'Ubayd, the companion of the Prophet (peace be upon him), at sea, when a Muslim who had fled to the enemy was brought. Islam was offered to him, and he accepted Islam. Then he fled a second time and was brought. Islam was offered to him, and he accepted Islam. Then he fled a third time and was brought. He [Fadalah] cited this verse: {Indeed, those who believed, then disbelieved, then believed, then disbelieved, and then increased in disbelief — Allah will never forgive them, nor will He guide them to a way} [al-Nisa' 137]. So he struck his neck. The isnad of these narrations contains weakness. The verse is applicable to one who persists upon disbelief.\n\n(T) And it has been narrated with a mursal isnad that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) granted repentance to Nabhan four times, each time he would join the polytheists.\n\nAnd the apparent meaning of the sound ahadith regarding that which justifies the shedding of blood bears witness to this mursal narration and is in agreement with it. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"
"16899","(16893) Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Jabir narrated to us — 'Ubayd, that is Ibn Janad, narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Amr narrated — from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah — from Adiyy ibn Thabit — from Yazid ibn al-Bara' — from his father, who said: My uncle met me while he had fastened a banner. I said: \Where are you going?\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon me) has sent me to a man who married his father's wife"
"16900","(16894) Abu Sa'id al-Khalil ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Busti, the Qadi, informed us — he came to us as a pilgrim in the year four hundred — Abu al-'Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Muzaffar al-Bakri informed us — Ibn Abi Kaythamah narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Manazil narrated to us — Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us — Khalid ibn Abi Karimah narrated — from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah — from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) sent his father, Mu'awiyah's grandfather, to a man who had consummated a marriage with his father's wife. He ordered him, so he struck his neck and divided his wealth into fifths.\n\nOur companions said: Striking the neck and dividing the wealth into fifths is not done except upon an apostate, as though he deemed it permissible despite his knowledge of its prohibition. And Allah knows best.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And it has been narrated that Mu'awiyah wrote to Ibn 'Abbas and Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with them both), asking them about the inheritance of the apostate. They said: \To the Bayt al-Mal.\"" Al-Shafi'i said: Meaning that it is fay' (spoils of war for the Muslim community)."""
"16901","(16895) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān — narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān — from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd ibn Ḥayyān — from ʿAmmār al-Duhnī — who said: Abū al-Ṭufayl narrated to me, saying: I was among the army that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālli — may Allah be pleased with him — sent to Banū Nājiyah. He said: We reached them and found them divided into three groups. He said: Our commander said to one group: \Who are you?\"" They said: \""We are a people who were Christians"
"16902","(16896) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān al-Jallāb in Hamadhān — informed us; Hilāl ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Raqqī — narrated to us; my father — narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr — from ʿAbd al-Karīm — from Abū ʿUbaydah ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir — from his father, who said: The polytheists seized ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir and did not release him until he reviled the Prophet ﷺ and spoke well of their idols. Then they released him. When he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \What is behind you?\"" He said: \""Evil"
"16903","(16897) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us orally; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Abū al-Bakhtarī ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir — narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī — narrated to us; Zāʾidah — from ʢĀṣim — from Zirr — from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The first to manifest his Islam were seven: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr, ʿAmmār, his mother Sumayyah, Ṣuhayb, Bilāl, and al-Miqdād — may Allah be pleased with them all. As for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah protected him through his uncle Abū Ṭālib. As for Abū Bakr, Allah protected him through his people. As for the rest of them, the polytheists seized them, clad them in coats of mail, and bound them in the sun. There was not one of them but that they complied with what they demanded — except Bilāl, for his self was insignificant in the sight of Allah, and he was insignificant in the sight of his people. So they gave him to the children, who made him wander through the valleys of Makkah, and he kept saying: \Aḥad"
"16904","(16898) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār — narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr — from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: Ḥakīm ibn Jubayr narrated to me — from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: I said to Ibn ʿAbbās: \O Abū al-ʿAbbās"
"16905","(16899) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī — informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī — narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī — narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ — from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ — from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah — from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding His statement: {Except one who is compelled while his heart is at rest with faith} — he said: Allah, glorified is He, informed that whoever disbelieves after his faith, upon him is wrath from Allah, and for him is a great punishment. As for the one who is compelled and speaks with his tongue while his heart contradicts him with faith, in order to save himself from his enemy, there is no blame upon him. Indeed, Allah, glorified is He, only takes the servants to account for what their hearts have resolved upon."
"16906","(16900) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī — informed us; my father — narrated to us; Abū Hammām — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bishr al-ʿAbdī — who said: I heard Sufyān ibn Saʿīd mention — from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʿAṭāʾ narrated to me — from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding {Except that you fear from them a fear (tuqāt)} — he said: \The tuqāt is speaking with the tongue while the heart is at rest with faith"
"16907","(16901) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Mihrān al-Aṣbahānī — narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Saʿīd al-Dimashqī — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Bashīr — from Qatādah — from al-Ḥasan — from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When you see the fornicator"
"16908","(16902) It is only known from the hadith of al-Nuʿmān ibn Murrah as a mursal narration. Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah — informed us; Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najayd al-Sulamī — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī — narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr — narrated to us; Mālik —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us among others; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — informed us; al-Shāfiʿī — informed us; Mālik — from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd — from al-Nuʿmān ibn Murrah — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \What do you say about the drinker"
"16909","(16903) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah — narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Thābit al-Marwazī — narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn — from his father — from Yazīd al-Naḥwī — from ʿIkrimah — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: {And those who commit fāḥishah from among your women} — the verse. He said: Then He mentioned the man after the woman and combined them, and said: {And the two who commit it among you, then punish them both} — the verse. Then He abrogated that with the verse of flogging, and said: {The fornicatress and the fornicator, flog each of them with a hundred lashes.}"
"16910","(16904) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Kāmil al-Qāḍī — informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Saʿd ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAṭiyyah — narrated to us; my father — narrated to us; my paternal uncle — narrated to us; my father — from his father — from Ibn ʿAbbās, with the same meaning."
"16911","(16905) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us: Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding His — exalted is He — words {And those who commit unlawful sexual intercourse among your women} [al-Nisāʾ 4:15], meaning fornication (zinā). And regarding His words {so punish them both} [al-Nisāʾ 4:15], meaning by verbal abuse. Then this was abrogated by {The fornicatress and the fornicator, flog each of them with a hundred lashes} [al-Nūr 24:2]. And regarding His words {or Allah makes a way for them} [al-Nisāʾ 4:15], he said: \The way\"" (al-sabīl) refers to the prescribed punishment (al-ḥadd). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16912","(16906) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from ʿĪsā, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding His words {And those who commit unlawful sexual intercourse among your women} [al-Nisāʾ 4:15], he said: \It refers to fornication (zinā).\"" He said: \""They were commanded to be confined — that is"
"16913","(16907) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd — Ibn Abī ʿArūbah — narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Ḥiṭṭān ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Raqāshī, from ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who was an ʿAqabī, a Badrī, and one of the chiefs of the Anṣār: that when revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would become distressed by it and his face would change. One day revelation descended upon him and he experienced that. When it was completed, he said: \Take from me"
"16914","(16908) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl informed us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us: Yūnus narrated from al-Ḥasan regarding this verse {And those who commit unlawful sexual intercourse among your women} [al-Nisāʾ 4:15] up to His words {or Allah makes a way for them} [al-Nisāʾ 4:15]. He said: \The first of the prescribed punishments for women was that they would be confined in their houses until the verse in al-Nūr was revealed: {The fornicatress and the fornicator"
"16915","(16909) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān informed us: Abū al-Ṭāhir — (ḥ) and Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad informed us, and the wording is his: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Ḥarmalah informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah informed me that he heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās say: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābl — may Allah be pleased with him — said while seated on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \Indeed"
"16916","(16910) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \I fear that time will lengthen for people until someone says: 'We do not find stoning in the Book of Allah"
"16917","(16911) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, who said: Ubayy ibn Kaʿb — may Allah be pleased with him — said to me: \How many verses do you count"
"16918","(16912) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, who said: I heard Yūnus ibn Jubayr narrating from Kathīr ibn al-Ṣalt, who said: They were writing the maṣāḥif in the presence of Zayd ibn Thābit. When they reached this verse, Zayd said: \I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'The married man and the married woman"
"16919","(16913) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā informed us: Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated from Ibn ʿAwn, from Muḥammad, who said: \I was informed from the brother of Kathīr ibn al-Ṣalt"
"16920","(16914) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding His words {And those who commit unlawful sexual intercourse among your women} [al-Nisāʾ 4:15], the verse. He said: \When a woman committed fornication"
"16921","(16915) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq al-Baṣrī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿĀmir and ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Jābir ibn Samurah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought Māʿiz ibn Mālik, a hairy man, short in stature, with muscular build. He confessed to adultery, so the Prophet ﷺ turned away from him. Then he came from another direction and confessed again, and the Prophet ﷺ turned away from him. He said: \I do not know whether it was two or three times.\"" Then he ordered that he be stoned. And he said: \""Whenever we send out a raiding party"
"16922","(16916) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī narrated to us, saying: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat narrated to us, saying: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād narrated to us, saying: Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated from Jābir ibn Samurah that the Prophet ﷺ stoned Māʿiz and did not mention flogging. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16923","(16917) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated from al-Zuhrī —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: al-Qaʿnabī narrated, in what he read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah from Abū Hurayrah and from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, that both of them informed him: Two men came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disputing. One of them said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16924","(16918) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, saying: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, saying: Ibn Qaʿnab and Ibn Bukayr narrated from Mālik, and he mentioned it with its chain, similarly. He said: \And al-ʿasīf is the hired servant (al-ajīr).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Yūsuf and Ibn Abī Uways from Mālik"
"16925","(16919) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ibn ʿAbbās that he said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Stoning is in the Book of Allah"
"16926","(16920) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd that he heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib say: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Beware lest you perish regarding the verse of stoning"
"16927","(16921) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated, mentioning it similarly.\n\nHe added: Mālik said: \ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb meant by 'the shaykh and the shaykhah' the married man (al-thayyib) among men and the married woman (al-thayyibah) among women.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16928","(16922) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān narrated to us, saying: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us, saying: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, saying: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned"
"16929","(16923) Abū Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, saying: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: al-Aʿmash narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth, Abū Muʿāwiyah, and Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Murrah from Masrūq from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The blood of a Muslim who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful to shed except in one of three cases: the married person who commits adultery"
"16930","(16924) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd from Abū Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khālid that they both said: A man from the Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16931","(16925) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ibn Milḥān informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Layth, from Ibn Shihāb — without the mention of ʿUqayl.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us, Abū al-Walīd informed us, Layth narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū Bakr informed me, Ibrāhīm ibn Sharīk informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus informed us, Layth narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū Bakr informed us, al-Firyābī informed us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us, al-Layth narrated from Ibn Shihāb. Ḥ And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us, Ibn Ṣāliḥ, Ibn Bukayr, Ibn Rumḥ, and Muḥammad ibn Khallād narrated to us that al-Layth narrated to them, he said: Ibn Shihāb narrated to me, from ʿUbaydullāh, from Abū Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khālid, that both of them said: A man from the Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and they mentioned it.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and Abū al-Walīd, and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ, thus."
"16932","(16926) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn Milḥān informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us, al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, that he said: A man from among the Muslims came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was in the mosque, and he called out to him, saying: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16933","(16927) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed me, Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAqīl informed us, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth informed us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, he said: ʿUqayl narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith with its like.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr, and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16934","(16928) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣāʾigh informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿlā ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muḥāribī informed us, my father narrated to us, from Ghaylān ibn Jāmiʿ, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: Māʿiz ibn Mālik came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16935","(16929) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated — in what he read to Mālik — from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he said: The Jews came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned to him that a man and a woman from among them had committed zinā. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to them: \What do you find in the Torah regarding the matter of zinā?\"" They said: \""We disgrace them and they are flogged.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām said: \""You have lied! Indeed"
"16936","(16930) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd informed me, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — and the wording is his — Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr informed us. Both said: Wakīʿ informed us, al-Aʿmash narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Murrah, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: They passed by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a Jew who had been flogged and whose face had been blackened. He asked the Jews: \Who is your scholar?\"" They said: \""So-and-so.\"" He sent for him"
"16937","(16931) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAmr al-Ḥīrī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq informed us, Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us, Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad informed us. He said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say: The Prophet (ﷺ) stoned a man from Aslam and a Jewish man and his wife.\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah have mercy on him — said: Meaning, a Jewish woman. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16938","(16932) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated it to us in Baghdad, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us, Ibn Lahīʿah informed us, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Mulyal, that his father informed him, that he heard ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ al-Zubaydī mention: The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had both committed zinā, and both had been married (muḥṣan). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered regarding them, and they were both stoned. ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith said: I was among those who stoned them.\n\nThis wording is also narrated in the hadith of Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah, from Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Shaybānī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had both been married, and they asked him to judge between them. He judged between them with rajm (stoning). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16939","(16933) And among what Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to me by way of ijāzah: Abū al-Walīd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Mūsā informed us, Jarīr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd in the hadith of al-Zuhrī: A man from Muzaynah narrated to Ibn al-Musayyab that Abū Hurayrah narrated to them: The Jewish rabbis gathered in the Bayt al-Midrās when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in al-Madīnah, and a man from among them had committed zinā after being married, with a Jewish woman who had been married. He mentioned the hadith, and it is recorded in the chapter on the ḥadd of the dhimmīs. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"16940","(16934) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed me, al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd, that Abū Wāqid al-Laythī — who was among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) — informed him: While he was with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) at al-Jābiyah, a man came to him and said: \O Commander of the Faithful"
"16941","(16935) ʿAlī ibn Bashrān informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Muʿammar ibn Sulaymān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Hārūn Abū Ḥāmid narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Mujālid narrated to us that Muʿammar ibn Sulaymān al-Raqqī narrated from al-Ḥajjāj from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil from his father, who said: A woman was forced [into unlawful intercourse] during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, so the ḥadd punishment was waived from her, and it was carried out upon the one who had assaulted her. [Weak]"
"16942","(16936) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Hāshim al-Baghawī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to me that Juwayriyyah narrated from Nāʿif that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: Whoever associates partners with Allah is not a muḥṣin [one in a state of iḥṣān].\n\nThis is how the companions of Nāʿif narrated it from Nāʿif. [Authentic]"
"16943","(16937) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḍārib ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that my father narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī informed us that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever associates partners with Allah is not a muḥṣin.\"" [Denounced (Munkar)]"""
"16944","(16938) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, both saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: No one raised it [to the Prophet] other than Isḥāq, and it is said that he retracted from it. The correct view is that it is mawqūf [a statement of the Companion]."
"16945","(16939) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Munīr al-Maṭīrī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Baldī wrote to me that Abū Salamah Aḥmad ibn Abī Nāʿif narrated to us that ʿAfīf ibn Sālim narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The people of shirk with Allah do not confer iḥṣān upon anything.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: It was also narrated from Aḥmad ibn Abī Nāʿif from Muʿāfā ibn ʿImrān from al-Thawrī"
"16946","(16940) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, both saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: ʿAfīf erred in raising it [to the Prophet]. The correct view is that it is mawqūf, from the statement of Ibn ʿUmar.\n\nʿAlī said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khushaysh narrated to us that Salm ibn Junādah narrated to us that Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \Whoever associates partners with Allah is not a muḥṣin.\"""""
"16947","(16941) ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Karābīsī informed us that Abū al-Faḍl Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Maryam al-Ghassānī narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Kaʿb ibn Mālik: that he intended to marry a Jewish or Christian woman, so he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he forbade him from it and said: \She will not make you a muḥṣin.\"" [Weak]"""
"16948","(16942) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, both saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Maryam is weak, and ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah did not meet Kaʿb.\n\nThe Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It was also narrated by Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd from Abū Sabāʾ ʿUtbah ibn Tamīm from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Kaʿb, and it is munqaṭiʿ [disconnected]. [Weak]"
"16949","(16943) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī informed us in it [i.e., in Isfarāyin] that Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that al-Ramādī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, who said: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān asked ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah about the slave woman: \Does she confer iḥṣān upon the free man?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""From whom do you narrate this?\"" He said: \""We heard the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying that.\"" [Authentic]"""
"16950","(16944) And Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād narrated to us that Yūnus, i.e. Ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb that he heard ʿAbd al-Malik asking ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd: \Does the slave woman confer iḥṣān upon the free man?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" ʿAbd al-Malik said: \""From whom do you narrate this?\"" He said: \""We heard the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying that.\""\n\nImām Aḥmad said: It reached me from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā that he said: I found al-Awzāʿī had followed Yūnus"
"16951","(16945) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, he said: I read to Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth: \Your father informed you"
"16952","(16946) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār in Baghdād informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Abū al-Ashʿath narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from a man of Banī ʿIjl, who said: \I was with ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) at Ṣiffīn when suddenly a man in a field was shouting: 'I have committed an immoral act; carry out the ḥadd on me!' So I brought him to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"
"16953","(16947) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatāda informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar and Abū al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj informed us, they said: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān al-Marwazī narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Shuʿba narrated to us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, who said: \I heard Ḥanash ibn al-Muʿtamir say: 'A man from among us married a woman and committed adultery before consummating the marriage with her"
"16954","(16948) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ al-Baghdādī informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us, from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: \Whoever marries someone who had not previously been in a state of iḥṣān (marital chastity) and then commits adultery before consummating the marriage with his wife"
"16955","(16949) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) flogged a man one hundred lashes for adultery, and then it was reported that he was a muḥṣan (married person), so he ordered that he be stoned. [Denounced (Munkar)]"
"16956","(16950) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: Abū ʀāṣim narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm, Abū Yaḥyā al-Bazzāz, informed us: Abū ʀāṣim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, that a man committed adultery with a woman, and his state of iḥṣān was not known, so he was flogged. Then his iḥṣān was established, so he was stoned. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Bazzāz.\n\nAnd in the narration of Abū Muslim, he said, from Jābir, regarding a man who committed adultery, was then flogged, and then his iḥṣān was established, he said: \He is to be stoned.\"""""
"16957","(16951) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Hishām narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, that Abū Qilāba narrated to him, from Abī al-Muhallab, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that a woman from Juhayna came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while she was pregnant from adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded her guardian to treat her well, and when she delivered her child, he should bring her to him. He did so. Then he ordered that she be stoned. Her garments were wrapped around her, then he ordered that she be stoned. Then he prayed over her. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16958","(16952) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ informed me: Abū ʿAlī al-Qabbānī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us: My father narrated to me, mentioning it with its chain and its meaning, except that he said: \If it were divided among seventy of the people of Madīnah"
"16959","(16953) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Najda narrated to us: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Bashīr ibn al-Muhājir narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Burayda narrated to us, from his father, in the story of the Ghāmida woman and her stoning, and Khālid ibn al-Walīd's cursing of her. He said: \The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard his cursing of her and said: 'Gently"
"16960","(16954) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Ḥaramī ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUlātha narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us that Khālid ibn al-Lajlāj narrated to him that his father al-Lajlāj informed him: \He was sitting working in the market when a woman passed by carrying a child. The people rose up"
"16961","(16955) As for Ma'iz ibn Malik, Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukari informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar narrated from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah that a man from the tribe of Aslam came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and confessed to adultery. The Prophet turned away from him. He confessed again, and the Prophet turned away from him, until he testified against himself four times. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Are you insane?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Are you married (muhsan)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered that he be stoned at the place of prayer (al-musalla). When the stones began to pain him"
"16962","(16956) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabari narrated to us: 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: Ma'iz ibn Malik came and confessed to adultery before the Prophet (peace be upon him) three times. The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired about him, then ordered that he be stoned. We stoned him with pottery shards, stones, and bones. We neither dug a pit for him nor bound him. He went off running hard toward the Harrah, and we followed him. He stood before us, and we stoned him until he was still. The Prophet (peace be upon him) neither sought forgiveness for him nor cursed him.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. Thus it is in this narration.\n\nWe have narrated in the hadith of Sulayman ibn Buraydah from his father that which indicates that if the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not seek forgiveness for Ma'iz ibn Malik at that time, he ordered them to seek forgiveness for him after two or three days.\n\nWe have narrated in the hadith of 'Abdullah ibn Buraydah from his father from the Prophet (peace be upon him) regarding the story of the Ghamidiyyah woman that he ordered that she be prayed over and buried. The story of the Ghamidiyyah occurred after the story of Ma'iz. In the story of the Ghamidiyyah, she said: \O Prophet of Allah"
"16963","(16957) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us. Abu 'Abdullah said: \He informed me"
"16964","(16958) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan narrated to us: Abu Hufayfah —\n\n(Chain continues) He said: And Sulayman informed us: 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us. Both chains said: Sufyan narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from Yazid ibn Nu'aym — meaning ibn Hazzal — al-Aslami from his father, who said: Ma'iz came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16965","(16959) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr said: This hadith was recited to Sufyan while I was present —\n\n(Chain continues) And Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: al-Zuhri informed me: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah informed me from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, Abu Hurayrah, and Shibl, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace be upon him) when a man stood up and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"16966","(16960) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Malik narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abu Waqid al-Laythi that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was approached by a man while he was in Syria. The man mentioned to him that he had found a man with his wife. 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) sent Abu Waqid al-Laythi to his wife to ask her about that. He came to her while women were around her. He mentioned to her what her husband had said to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed her that she would not be taken at his word. He kept suggesting similar things to her so that she might retract. But she refused to retract and persisted in her confession. So 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered that she be stoned, and she was stoned.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said in his book: He did not say, \Inform me that I was present.\"" And indeed 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered the stoning of a woman"
"16967","(16961) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajanii informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik informed him — that it reached him — that 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a woman. He mentioned the hadith regarding his ordering her stoning and that he ordered her return, but she was found to have already been stoned. [Da'if]"
"16968","(16962) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us: 'Ammar — that is ibn Ruzayq — narrated from Abu Hasin from al-Sha'bi who said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought Shurahah al-Hamadaniyyah, who had committed adultery. He sent her back until she gave birth. When she gave birth, he said: \Bring me the closest of women to her in kinship.\"" She was brought"
"16969","(16963) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkhi informed us: Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us: Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us: al-Ajlah narrated from al-Sha'bi who said: Shurahah al-Hamadaniyyah was brought to 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). He said to you: \Woe to you! Perhaps a man lay upon you while you were asleep.\"" She said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Perhaps he coerced you?\"" She said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Perhaps your husband is from among our enemies who came to you"
"16970","(16964) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us: 'Ammar — that is ibn Ruzayq — narrated from Abu Hasin from al-Sha'bi who said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought Shurahah al-Hamadaniyyah, who had committed adultery. He sent her back until she gave birth. When she gave birth, he said: \Bring me the closest of women to her in kinship.\"" She was brought"
"16971","(16965) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed me; Mu'adh ibn Najdah narrated to us.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us; Abu Muhammad Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Shaybagh al-Baghdadi in Harah informed us; Mu'adh ibn Najdah informed us; Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Bashir ibn Muhajir narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah narrated to me from his father, who said:\n\nI was sitting with the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) when Ma'iz ibn Malik al-Aslami came and said: \O Prophet of Allah"
"16972","(16966) And from his father, who said:\n\nI was sitting with the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) when a woman from Ghamid came and said: \O Prophet of Allah"
"16973","(16967) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us from Zakariyya Abu 'Imran, who said: I heard an old man narrating from Ibn Abi Bakrah from his father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) stoned a woman, and a pit was dug for her up to the chest.\n\nAbu Dawud said: I was informed from 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith, who narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Sulayman narrated to us with his chain, similar to it, and he added: \Then he stoned her with a pea-sized stone and said: 'Stone"
"16974","(16968) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; Ibn Abi Qummash narrated to us; 'Awn ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us from Hushaym.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed me; Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Imam narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; Hushaym informed us from Mansur from al-Hasan from Hittan ibn 'Abd Allah from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Take from me; Allah has made for them a way: the virgin with the virgin — one hundred lashes and banishment for one year; and the non-virgin with the non-virgin — one hundred lashes and stoning.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Yahya. And in the narration of 'Amr: \""and exile for a year.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya."""
"16975","(16969) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Shayban narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us from al-Zuhri from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and Shibl, who said:\n\nWe were with the Prophet (ﷺ) when a man stood up and said: \I adjure you by Allah"
"16976","(16970) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus informed me. I heard 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi say: I heard 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah al-Madini say regarding this hadith: I said to Sufyan, \Some of them attribute it to one (narrator only).\"" He said: \""But I narrate to you from al-Zuhri"
"16977","(16971) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi informed us by dictation; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Sharqi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us from al-Zuhri from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said:\n\nI heard the Prophet (ﷺ) command regarding one who committed zina but was not married (muhsan): one hundred lashes and exile for one year. This is the wording of the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman. And in the narration of al-Tayalisi: \I witnessed him judge regarding one who committed zina.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Malik ibn Isma'il from 'Abd al-'Aziz"
"16978","(16972) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; Ibn Milhan narrated to us; Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us from 'Uqayl from Ibn Shihab from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said regarding one who committed zina but was not married (muhsan): \He is to be banished for one year from Madinah"
"16979","(16973) Abu al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Ma'ruf al-Faqih informed us; Abu Sahl al-Isfarayini informed us; Abu Ja'far Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadda' narrated to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah al-Madini narrated to us; Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, who said:\n\nWhile Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was in the mosque, a man came to him and spoke to him with confused speech, bewildered. So Abu Bakr said to 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): \Go to him and look into his affair"
"16980","(16974) 'Ali said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us; 'Ubayd Allah narrated to me; Nafi' informed me from Safiyyah — and 'Ali said: She is Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd — that a man hosted another man, and he assaulted his sister. Her brother came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him. So he sent for him, and he confessed it. He said: \Are you a virgin or previously married?\"" He said: \""A virgin.\"" So he gave him one hundred lashes and banished him to Fadak. Then the man married the woman afterward. Then the man was killed on the Day of Yamamah.\n\nAhmad said: \""And with its meaning"
"16981","(16975) Abu al-Mihrajan informed us: Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī — informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-'Abdī — informed us: Ibn Bukayr — informed us: Mālik — from Nāfi' — from Safiyyah bint Abī 'Ubayd, who informed him that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a man who had intercourse with a virgin slave-girl and impregnated her, and then confessed upon himself that he had committed zinā, though he had never been married (muḥṣan). So Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered regarding him, and he was flogged the ḥadd punishment, and then he was banished to Fadak. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16982","(16976) And Shu'ayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated it from Nāfi', who said: Ṣafiyyah bint 'Ubayd informed me regarding Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) that he flogged him and banished him for a year.\n\nAbū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burhān informed us: Ismā'īl al-Ṣaffār informed us: 'Abd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham informed us: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Shu'ayb said — Nāfi' said, and he mentioned it."
"16983","(16977) And 'Abd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated it from 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Umar, as Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Abū Kurayb informed us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ja'far — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ja'far al-Qirmisīnī — informed us there: Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Shādhān al-Baghdādī — informed us: Abū Ja'far — Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn al-Buhlūl al-Qāḍī — informed us by dictation, he said: It was recited to Abū Kurayb while I was listening: \You have 'Abd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrate to you from 'Ubayd Allāh"
"16984","(16978) And Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Abū Sa'īd al-Ashajj informed us: 'Abd Allāh ibn Idrīs said: I heard 'Ubayd Allāh from Nāfi' from Ibn 'Umar, that Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) struck and banished, and that 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) struck and banished."
"16985","(16979) Abū Ḥāzim al-'Abdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl al-Karābīsī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Sa'īd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Hushaym informed us: al-Shaybānī informed us — from al-Sha'bī, that 'Alī (may Allah be pleased with him) flogged and banished from al-Baṣrah to al-Kūfah, or he said, from al-Kūfah to al-Baṣrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16986","(16980) Abū 'Alī — al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrām ibn Shādhān al-Baghdādī — informed us: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-'Abbās informed us: al-'Abbās ibn Muḥammad informed us: Abū Salamah informed us: Abū 'Awanah informed us: Firās informed us — from 'Āmir — from Masrūq — from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The two unmarried persons (al-bikrān) are flogged and banished, and the two previously married persons (al-thayyibān) are stoned. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"16987","(16981) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-'Abbās — Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb — informed us: Aḥmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār informed us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr informed us — from Hishām ibn 'Urwah — from his father — from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah — from Umm Salamah, who said: There was a mukhannath (effeminate man) in my presence, and he said to 'Abd Allāh, my brother: \If Allah conquers al-Ṭā'if for you tomorrow"
"16988","(16982) And Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsá informed us: al-Ḥumaydī informed us: Sufyān informed us — from Hishām ibn 'Urwah — from his father — from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah — from her mother, Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) entered upon me while there was a mukhannath in my presence, and he heard him saying to 'Abd Allāh ibn Abī Umayyah: \O 'Abd Allāh"
"16989","(16983) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burhān informed us in Baghdād: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān informed us: 'Abd Allāh ibn Abī al-Dunyā informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥammād al-Ḍabbī informed us: 'Abadah informed us — from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — from Yazīd — from Mūsá ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn 'Āyash ibn Abī Rabī'ah, who said: During the era of the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam), there were three mukhannathūn (effeminate men): Māti', Hidl, and Hīt. And Māti' belonged to Fākhitah bint 'Amr ibn 'Ā'idh, the maternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam), and he used to enter the houses of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) and go in among the women. When the siege of al-Ṭā'if took place, the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) heard him saying to Khālid ibn al-Walīd: \If al-Ṭā'if is conquered tomorrow"
"16990","(16984) Abū al-Ḥasan — 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān — informed us: Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Hishām al-Dastawā'ī informed us: Yaḥyá ibn Abī Kathīr informed us — from 'Ikrimah — from Ibn 'Abbās, that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) cursed the mukhannathūn (effeminate men) among the men and the mutarajjalāt (women who assume the mannerisms of men) among the women, and he said: \Expel them from your homes"
"16991","(16985) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār related to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī related to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar related to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Expute the effeminate men (al-mukhannathīn) from your homes.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ expelled an effeminate man"
"16992","(16986) And Maʿmar informed us, from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that a man from among the effeminate men be expelled"
"16993","(16987) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Raffāʾ informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz related to us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ related to us: Abū Usāmah related to us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah related to us: Abū Dāwūd related to us: Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh and Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ related to us, that Abū Usāmah informed them, from Mufaḍḍal ibn Yūnus, from al-Awzāʿī, from Abī Yasār al-Qurashī, from Abī Hāshim, from Abī Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet ﷺ was brought an effeminate man whose hands and feet had been dyed with henna. The Prophet ﷺ said: \What is the matter with this one?\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"
"16994","(16988) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed me: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā related to us: Abū al-Yamān informed me: Shuʿayb informed me, from al-Zuhrī, that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed him, that Abī Hurayrah said: \While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"
"16995","(16989) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār related to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh related to us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm related to us: Hishām related to us: Yaḥyā related to us, from Abī Qilābah, from Abī al-Muhallab, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \She has committed zinā"
"16996","(16990) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baghdādī related to us: Hāshim ibn Yūnus related to us: Abū Ṣāliḥ related to me: al-Layth related to me: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Khālid related to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ibn al-Musayyib and Abī Salamah, that Abī Hurayrah said: \A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the mosque"
"16997","(16991) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī informed us: Abū al-Muwajjih informed us: ʿAbdān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Yūnus informed us, from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī, that Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed him, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī, that a man from among the Banū Aslam came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him that he had committed zinā, and he testified against himself four times. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered, and he was stoned, and he had been married (aḥṣana).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil, from ʿAbd Allāh."
"16998","(16992) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm related to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah related to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: al-Zuhrī informed me, from Abī Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that a man from among the Banū Aslam testified before him against himself for zinā four times, so he ordered, and he was stoned, and he had been married (aḥṣana). He said: \They claimed that he was Māʿiz.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""That was only in the early period of Islam"
"16999","(16993) And in what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb related to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī related to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿlā ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muḥāribī related to me: my father related to us, from Ghaylān ibn Jāmiʿ, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: \Māʿiz ibn Mālik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"17000","(16994) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār related to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq related to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb related to us: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim related to us, from Yaʿlā ibn Ḥakīm, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that when Māʿiz came to the Prophet ﷺ, he ﷺ said to him: \Woe to you! Perhaps you kissed"
"17001","(16995) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to me, Ibrāhīm ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us, my father narrated to us with this, except that he said: \Did you have intercourse with her?\"" He said: Yes.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from Wahb ibn Jarīr."""
"17002","(16996) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh in Ṭabarān informed us that Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām informed me that Abū Kāmil al-Jaḥdarī narrated to us that Abū ʿĀwānah narrated from Simāk from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: I saw Māʿiz ibn Mālik when he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ — a short, muscular man wearing no cloak — and he testified against himself four times that he had committed zinā (unlawful sexual intercourse). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Perhaps…\"" He said: \""No"
"17003","(16997) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū ʿAmr al-Ḥīrī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Isḥāq and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, Dāwūd narrated from Abī Naḍrah from Abī Saʿīd: that a man from the tribe of Aslam, called Māʿiz ibn Mālik, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \I have committed an obscene act; so carry out the punishment on me.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him repeatedly. Then he asked his people about him and they said: \""We know nothing bad about him except that he has done something from which he believes there is no escape except that the ḥadd be carried out upon him.\"" He said: So he returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he commanded us to stone him. He said: So we went to Baqīʿ al-Gharqad. He said: We neither tied him nor dug a trench for him. He said: We pelted him with bones"
"17004","(16998) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh — informed us that Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, who is Abū al-Shaykh — narrated to us that Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿĀṣim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me that Abū al-Zubayr narrated from a paternal uncle of Abī Hurayrah, from Abī Hurayrah: that Māʿiz came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"17005","(16999) Abū Aḥmad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī — informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, who said: A man from the tribe of Aslam came to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: \The other one has committed zinā.\"" Abū Bakr said to him: \""Have you mentioned this to anyone other than me?\"" He said: No. Abū Bakr said: \""Then repent to Allah and conceal yourself with the veil of Allah"
"17006","(17000) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Khashram narrated to us, ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr from Abī Salamah from Abī Hurayrah, who said: Māʿiz al-Aslamī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \I have committed zinā.\"" He turned away from him"
"17007","(17001) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Tamtām — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib — narrated to us, Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from Yazīd ibn Nuʿaym ibn Hazzāl al-Aslamī from his father: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding Māʿiz when he had gone: \Why did you not leave him? Perhaps he would have repented and Allah would have accepted his repentance.\"" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Hazzāl"
"17008","(17002) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ṭalq ibn Ghannām narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us, Abū Ḥāzim narrated from Sahl ibn Saʿd from the Prophet ﷺ: that a man came to him and confessed to him that he had committed zinā with a woman. He named her for him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to the woman and asked her about that, and she denied having committed zinā. So he had the ḥadd carried out upon him (by flogging) and left her. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"17009","(17003) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, Hishām ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, al-Qāsim — the brother of Khallād's paternal uncle — narrated from Khallād ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, who said: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was addressing the people on Friday, a man from Banī Layth ibn Bakr ibn ʿAbd Manāt came, pushing through the people until he approached him and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"17010","(17004) Abū al-Qāsim — ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Mu'adhdhin — informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb al-Baghdādī in Bukhārā narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Salām al-Sawwāq narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us, Isrāʾīl narrated from al-Suddī from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah from Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, who said: I heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) delivering a sermon from the minbar. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \O people"
"17011","(17005) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, from what we read to him from his original: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, al-Thawrī informed us from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Thaʿlabī, from Abū Jamīlah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) that a slave-girl of the Prophet (ﷺ) gave birth as a result of zinā (unlawful sexual intercourse). The Prophet (ﷺ) sent me to carry out the ḥadd (prescribed punishment) upon her. I found her still in the state of postpartum bleeding, which had not yet ceased. So I returned to the Prophet (ﷺ) and informed him. He said: \When the blood ceases from her"
"17012","(17006) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿlā ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muḥāribī informed us, my father informed us from Ghaylān ibn Jāmiʿ, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from his father, in the story of the Ghāmidī woman. She said: \Indeed I am pregnant from zinā.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Are you a thayyibah (previously married woman)?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then we shall not stone you until you deliver what is in your womb.\"" He said: \""So a man from the Anṣār took responsibility for her until she delivered. Then she came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'The Ghāmidī woman has delivered.' He said: 'We shall stone her and leave her small child"
"17013","(17007) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Naṣr informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, Bashīr ibn Muhājir informed us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: \I was sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) when a woman from Ghāmid came to him and said: 'Indeed I have committed zinā"
"17014","(17008) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd and Abū al-Zinād — both of them from Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf — that a man (one of the two said \aḥabbān\"" and the other said \""muqʿad"
"17015","(17009) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us, ibn Numayr informed us, ibn Isḥāq informed us from Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ashajj, from Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf, from Saʿīd ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, who said: \There was among our dwellings a deformed"
"17016","(17010) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Naṣr informed us, Abū Mūsā —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Qāḍī al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā informed us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us from Fulayḥ, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd: that a slave-girl in the time of the Prophet (ﷺ) became pregnant from zinā. She was asked: \Who impregnated you?\"" She said: \""The paralytic man (al-muqʿad).\"" He was asked about that and he confessed. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed he is too weak for flogging.\"" So he ordered that a hundred date-palm clusters (ʿuthkūl) be brought"
"17017","(17011) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān al-Faqīh informed us in Baghdad, al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad informed us, Isḥāq ibn ʿĪsā informed us from Mālik, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"17018","(17012) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that a man in Shām found a man with his wife and killed him or killed her. Muʿāwiyah wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī asking him to inquire about that from ʿAlī. So he asked him, and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \This is something that does not happen in the land of Iraq. I adjure you"
"17019","(17013) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Mūsā al-Balkhī informed us, Abū Usāmah informed us — Mujālid informed us from ʿĀmir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: \The Jews came with a man and a woman from among them who had committed zinā. He said: 'Bring me the two most learned men among you.' So they brought the two sons of Ṣūriyā. He adjured them: 'How do you find the matter of these two in the Torah?' They said: 'We find in the Torah that when four witnesses testify that they saw his penis in her vagina like the kohl-stick in the kohl-container"
"17020","(17014) And Abū ʿAlī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah informed us from Hushaym, from Mughīrah, from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, from the Prophet (ﷺ), a similar narration. He did not mention: \Then he called for witnesses and they testified.\"" [Weak]"""
"17021","(17015) He said: And Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Hushaym, from Ibn Shubrumah, from al-Sha'bi, with a similar narration."
"17022","(17016) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid al-Faqih informed us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abu Bakr — he is Ibn Abi Shaybah — narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Yahya ibn 'Atiq, from Ibn Sirin: that some people testified against a man regarding zina (unlawful sexual intercourse), so 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Is this how you testify against him?\"" And he inserted his index finger into his left finger"
"17023","(17017) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan — informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; Isma'il al-Qadi narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \May Allah curse the one who takes as a patron other than his rightful masters; may Allah curse the one who alters the boundaries of the land; may Allah curse the one who misleads a blind person from the path; may Allah curse the one who curses his parents; may Allah curse the one who slaughters for other than Allah; may Allah curse the one who has intercourse with an animal; and may Allah curse the one who commits the act of the people of Lut\"" — and he repeated \""may Allah curse the one who commits the act of the people of Lut\"" three times. [Hasan]"""
"17024","(17018) And Abu al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; 'Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us; Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Ibn Abi al-Zinad and Ibn al-Darawardi both said: 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its chain, similar to it, except that he said: \the one who allies himself with other than his rightful masters"
"17025","(17019) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr al-Qadi both informed us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from 'Amr, the freed slave of al-Muttalib.\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan — informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; 'Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us; Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Amr, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever you find committing the act of the people of Lut"
"17026","(17020) Abu Sa'd — Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Malini — informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us; 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — Abu Hafs al-Sulami — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us; 'Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), regarding the one who commits the act of the people of Lut, and regarding the one who is approached in his own person, and regarding the one who has intercourse with a mahram (close female relative), and regarding the one who has intercourse with an animal: \He is to be killed.\"" [Da'if]"""
"17027","(17021) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan — informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us; Isma'il al-Qadi narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever has intercourse with a man"
"17028","(17022) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn Khalifah narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Tamim narrated to us; he said: I heard Hajjaj say: Ibn Jurayj said: Ibrahim informed me, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Kill the one who does it and the one to whom it is done\"" — meaning the one who commits the act of the people of Lut"
"17029","(17023) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Rahawayh narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj informed us; Ibn Khuthaym informed me; he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Mujahid narrating from Ibn 'Abbas regarding a bachelor (unmarried youth) who is found committing the act of Lut: \He is to be stoned.\"" [Hasan]"""
"17030","(17024) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us; he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in say: Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Yazid narrated to us; he said: Abu Nadrah said: Ibn 'Abbas was asked about the punishment of the one who commits the act of Lut. He said: \Look for the tallest building in the village"
"17031","(17025) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān informed us, Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us, Sharīk narrated from al-Qāsim ibn al-Walīd, from some of his people, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) stoned a practitioner of the act of the people of Lūṭ. [Weak]"
"17032","(17026) And Abū Ḥāziṃ the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl al-Karābīsī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najda narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Qāsim ibn al-Walīd al-Hamdānī, from a man among his people, that he witnessed ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) stoning a practitioner of the act of the people of Lūṭ."
"17033","(17027) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said, from a man, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from al-Qāsim ibn al-Walīd, from Yazīd — whom he thought was Ibn Madhkūr — that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) stoned a practitioner of the act of the people of Lūṭ.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \And this is what we act upon — the practitioner of the act of Lūṭ is to be stoned"
"17034","(17028) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatāda and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī both said: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāziṃ informed us, Dāwūd ibn Bakr narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar and Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym, that Khālid ibn al-Walīd wrote to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with both of them) during his caliphate, mentioning to him that he had found a man among certain Bedouin Arabs who was being approached sexually as women are approached. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) gathered the people from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked them about that. The most emphatic of them in speech that day was ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \This is a sin by which no nation has ever transgressed except one nation"
"17035","(17029) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us with the hadith of al-Thawrī, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Sufyān mentioned it.\n\nAnd from Sufyān, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from ʿAṭāʾ, that he said regarding the practitioner of the act of Lūṭ: \His punishment is the punishment of the fornicator (zānī).\"" [Weak]"""
"17036","(17030) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī say: I heard Yazīd ibn Hārūn inform us, al-Yamān ibn al-Mughīra narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, who said: \I was present with Ibn al-Zubayr when seven men were brought who had been caught committing the act of Lūṭ. Four of them had been married to women"
"17037","(17031) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Mihrajānī informed us with it, Abū Saʿīd ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Rāzī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Hishām narrated to us, Qatāda narrated from al-Ḥasan, regarding a man who has intercourse with an animal or commits the act of the people of Lūṭ, that he said: \He is in the same category as the fornicator (zānī).\"" [Good]"""
"17038","(17032) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Shaybānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Saʿīd informed us, from Abī Maʿshar, from Ibrāhīm, who said: \The punishment of the practitioner of the act of Lūṭ is the punishment of the fornicator (zānī). If he is married (muḥṣin)"
"17039","(17033) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Mūsā, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When a man approaches a man"
"17040","(17034) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that he said regarding the one who has intercourse with an animal: \Kill the doer and the one done to.\"" [Weak]"""
"17041","(17035) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whosoever you find having committed bestiality with an animal"
"17042","(17036) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us — Ibn Manīʿ narrated to us — Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd, meaning Ibn Sulaymān, narrated to us — ʿAmr narrated with his chain of narration that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Cursed is the one who commits bestiality with an animal.\"" And he said: \""Kill him and kill the animal"
"17043","(17037) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Harawī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ashhalī narrated to us — Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whosoever commits zinā with a maḥram woman"
"17044","(17038) And Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Abū ʿAwānah and Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Bahdalah, from Abī Razīn, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he was asked about the one who commits bestiality with an animal. He said: \There is no ḥadd upon him.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"17045","(17039) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — he said: Abū Dāwūd said: \The ḥadīth of ʿĀṣim weakens the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr.\"" The Shaykh"
"17046","(17040) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated from Saʿīd, from Budayl, from Jābir ibn Zayd, who said: \Whoever commits bestiality with an animal"
"17047","(17041) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — al-Ḥasan narrated to us — Abū Bakr narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated from Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn, from Abī ʿAlī al-Raḥabī, from ʿIkrimah, who said: Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with them both, was asked about a man who commits bestiality with an animal. He said: \If he is muḥṣin (married)"
"17048","(17042) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me through ijāzah — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū Bakr narrated to us — Abū Usāmah narrated from ʿAwf, from Qasāmah ibn Zuhayr, who said: \When the matter of Abī Bakrah and al-Mughīrah arose —\"" and he mentioned the ḥadīth — \""He called for witnesses"
"17049","(17043) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us — Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, that Abā Bakrah, Nāfiʿ ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Kaladah, and Shibl ibn Maʿbad testified against al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah that they saw him inserting and withdrawing. Ziyād was the fourth of them, and he was the one who spoiled their testimony. The three testified to that. Abū Bakrah said: \By Allah"
"17050","(17044) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me through ijāzah — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — the daughter of Ibn Aḥmad ibn Manīʿ narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muṭīʿ narrated from Hushaym, from ʿUyaynah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abī Bakrah, who mentioned the story of al-Mughīrah. He said: \We came to ʿUmar"
"17051","(17045) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Hārūn narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl, from Abū ʿAwānah, from Ismāʿīl ibn Sālim, from Abū Idrīs, in the story of Sawsan, who said: Dāniyāl (peace be upon him) was the first to distinguish between the testimonies of witnesses. He said to one of them: \What did you see"
"17052","(17046) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; al-Asfaṭiyy narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Muʿammar ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, from Ḥajjāj, from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil, from his father, who said: A woman was raped during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ), and the ḥadd was waived from her.\n\nAnother narrator added in it: and the ḥadd was carried out upon the one who had assaulted her, and it was not mentioned that he assigned a dower for her.\n\nThis chain of narration has two weaknesses: one of them is that al-Ḥajjāj did not hear from ʿAbd al-Jabbār, and the other is that ʿAbd al-Jabbār did not hear from his father, as stated by al-Bukhārī and others. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"17053","(17047) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; they said: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah al-Karābīsī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a woman from the people of Yemen. They said: \She has committed zinā.\"" She said: \""I was asleep"
"17054","(17048) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Mayṣarah, from al-Nazzāl ibn Sabrah, who said: We were in Makkah when we found a woman around whom the people had gathered, nearly killing her, and they were saying: \She has committed zinā! She has committed zinā!\"" She was brought to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) while she was pregnant"
"17055","(17049) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, that a slave who was in charge of the slaves of the khums coerced a slave-girl from among those slaves and had intercourse with her. So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) flogged him and exiled him, and he did not flog the slave-girl because he had coerced her.\n\nAnd al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it from Nāfiʿ, from Ṣafiyyah bint Abī ʿUbayd. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"17056","(17050) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAlawī in Kūfah and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī in Naysābūr informed us; they said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī informed us; Wakīʿ narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a woman whom thirst had overcome. She passed by a shepherd and asked him for water, but he refused to give her water unless she gave herself to him. So she did that. He consulted the people regarding stoning her, and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \She was compelled; I think she should be released.\"" So he did so. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"17057","(17051) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān ruled regarding a woman who had been assaulted by coercion that her ṣadāq (dower) was due upon the one who had done that to her.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: Upon him is the ḥadd and the ṣadāq. And from al-Ḥasan, who said: Upon him is the ḥadd and the ʿuqr (compensation). And from al-Zuhrī: Upon him is the ṣadāq and the ḥadd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — from al-Zuhrī]"
"17058","(17052) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Abū Bakr al-Narsī Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to us; Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Mājishūn narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say regarding one who commits zinā and is not muḥṣin (married): \One hundred lashes and exile for one year.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"17059","(17053) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Birtī narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Stoning is in the Book of Allah"
"17060","(17054) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Khālid narrated to us, from—\n\nAnd Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Muṭarrif narrated to us, from Abū al-Jahm, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: While I was searching for a camel of mine that had gone missing, a group of riders or horsemen approached with a banner. The Bedouins gathered around me due to my standing with the Prophet (ﷺ). They came to a tent and brought out a man from it and struck his neck (executed him). I asked about him, and they mentioned that he had married his father's wife. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"17061","(17055) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us: Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar narrated from Ashʿath ibn Sawwār from ʿAdīy ibn Thābit from Yazīd ibn al-Barāʾ from al-Barāʾ from his maternal uncle that a man married his father's wife or his son's wife—thus said Abū Khālid—so the Prophet (ﷺ) sent for him and he was killed. [Weak]"
"17062","(17056) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlīy ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrīy narrated to us: Hāshim ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Ḥabībah narrated from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever commits sexual intercourse with a woman within the prohibited degrees of kinship (dhāt maḥram)"
"17063","(17057) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamīy and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith both informed us: ʿAlīy ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rabīʿah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn al-Najjār informed us in Kūfah: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlīy ibn Shuqayr ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Hārūn al-ʿIjlīy narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rizmah informed us: al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā—both of them—from Yazīd ibn Ziyād from al-Zuhrīy from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Avert the prescribed punishments (ḥudūd) from the Muslims as much as you are able. If you find a way out for a Muslim"
"17064","(17058) Wakīʿ narrated it from Yazīd ibn Ziyād, stopped (mawqūf) at ʿĀʾishah. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from Yazīd, and he mentioned it as mawqūf. Yazīd ibn Ziyād al-Shāmīy is alone in narrating it from al-Zuhrīy, and he is weak.\n\nThe narration of Wakīʿ is closer to correctness, and Allah knows best.\n\nRishdīn ibn Saʿd narrated it from ʿUqayl from al-Zuhrīy, raised [to the Prophet], and Rishdīn is weak."
"17065","(17059) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānīy informed us: ʿAlīy ibn ʿUmar informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn Zakarīyā informed us: Abū Kurayb informed us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated from Mukhtār al-Tammār from Abū Maṭar from ʿAlīy (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Avert the prescribed punishments.\"" In this chain of narration there is weakness. [Weak]"""
"17066","(17060) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us: It was recited to Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlīy narrated to us: Sahl ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: al-Mukhtār ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us: Abū Ḥayyān al-Taymīy narrated from his father from ʿAlīy (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Avert the prescribed punishments"
"17067","(17061) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from his father, who said: It reached me—or it reached us—that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When you come to us"
"17068","(17062) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Hushaym informed us: ʿUbaydah informed us: Ibrāhīm said that Ibn Masʿūd said: \Avert the prescribed punishments as much as you are able"
"17069","(17063) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Salām—that is, ibn Ḥarb—narrated from Isḥāq ibn Abī Farwah from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father that Muʿādh, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, and ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir (may Allah be pleased with them) said: \When the prescribed punishment is doubtful"
"17070","(17064) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān from ʿĀṣim from Abū Wāʾil from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \Avert flogging and execution from the Muslims as much as you are able.\"" This chain is connected (mawṣūl). [Authentic]"""
"17071","(17065) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muslim ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, that Yaḥyā ibn Ḥāṭib narrated to him, saying: Ḥāṭib passed away, and those of his slaves who prayed and fasted were manumitted. He had a Nubian slave-girl who had prayed and fasted, but she was a non-Arab who did not understand (the rulings). Nothing alarmed her except her pregnancy, and she was a previously married woman (thayyib). He went to ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, and informed him. ʿUmar said: \You are a man from whom no good comes!\"" This statement alarmed him. So ʿUmar"
"17072","(17066) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said: Abū ʿUbayd said: Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah and Yazīd narrated to us from Ḥumayd, from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, that it was written to him regarding a man who was asked: \When was your last intimacy with women?\"" He said: \""Last night.\"" He was asked: \""With whom?\"" He said: \""Umm Mathwāyā.\"" It was said to him: \""You are doomed.\"" He said: \""I did not know that Allah had forbidden zinā.\"" So ʿUmar"
"17073","(17067) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Hushaym narrated from Abū Bishr, from Ḥabīb ibn Sālim, that a woman came to al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \My husband has had intercourse with my slave-girl without my permission.\"" Al-Nuʿmān said: \""I have in this matter a decisive ruling that I took from the Messenger of Allah"
"17074","(17068) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: My father narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Bishr, from Khālid ibn ʿUrfaṭah, from Ḥabīb ibn Sālim, from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said regarding a man who has intercourse with his wife's slave-girl: \If she had made her lawful for him"
"17075","(17069) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Abān narrated to us: Qatādah narrated from Khālid ibn ʿUrfaṭah, from Ḥabīb ibn Sālim, that a man called ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥunayn had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl, and the matter was raised to al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who was the governor of Kūfah. He said: \I shall judge with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah"
"17076","(17070) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: al-Asfaṭī narrated to us: al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us: Hammām said: Qatādah was asked about a man who had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl, and he narrated to us from Khubayb ibn Yasāf, from Ḥabīb ibn Sālim, that the matter was raised to al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, and he said: \I shall judge in this matter with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah"
"17077","(17071) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khālid narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us: Qatādah narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Sālim, from Khubayb ibn Yasāf, that a man had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl, and the matter was raised to al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, and he mentioned it — \Thus I found them both in the book.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: \""I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī about this hadith"
"17078","(17072) Another hadith, weaker than this, has been narrated regarding this matter. Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated from al-Ḥasan, from Salamah ibn al-Muḥabbiq, that a man had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl, and the matter was raised to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and he said: \If she consented to him"
"17079","(17073) It was narrated from Shuʿbah, from Qatādah, as Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us orally: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Saʿīd al-Nasawī and Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī both said: Bakr ibn Bakkār narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan, from Jawn ibn Qatādah, from Salamah ibn al-Muḥabbiq, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl: \If he coerced her"
"17080","(17074) Maʿmar narrated it from Qatādah, as Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā al-Sukkārī informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Qabīṣah ibn Ḥurayth, from Salamah ibn al-Muḥabbiq, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, judged regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl — and in the narration of al-Ramādī: \He judged regarding a man who has intercourse with his wife's slave-girl\"" — \""If he coerced her"
"17081","(17075) It was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ, who narrated to us al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who narrated to us Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb, who narrated to us al-Qāsim ibn Sallābn ibn Miskīn, who narrated to me my father, who said: I asked al-Ḥasan about a man who has intercourse with his wife's slave-girl. He said: Qabīṣah ibn Ḥurayth al-Anṣārī narrated to me from Salamah ibn Muḥabbiq that a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ used to constantly travel and participate in military expeditions, and his wife sent a slave-girl with him, saying: \She shall wash your head"
"17082","(17076) It was narrated to us by Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī, who narrated to us Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī, who said: I heard Ibn Ḥammād mention it from al-Bukhārī.\n\nThe Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: The occurrence of consensus (ijmāʿ) among the jurists of the major cities after the Successions upon abandoning this ruling is evidence that, if it is established, it has been abrogated by what has come in the narrations regarding the ḥadd punishments. [Authentic, as per al-Bukhārī]"
"17083","(17077) It was narrated to us by Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī, who narrated to us Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, who narrated to us ʿAlī ibn Baḥr, who narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabīb ibn ʿArabī, who narrated to us Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith, who narrated to us al-Ashʿath, who said: It has reached me that this was before the ḥadd punishments were prescribed.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And it has been narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, from his own statement, something similar to the ḥadīth of Salamah ibn al-Muḥabbiq, and it has been narrated from him that he said: \Seek forgiveness from Allah and do not repeat it.\"" [Good]"""
"17084","(17078) And it was narrated to us by Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī, who narrated to us Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī, who narrated to us Sufyān al-Jawharī, who narrated to us ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī, who narrated to us ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd, who narrated to us Sufyān, from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Ibn Sīrīn, that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Ibn Umm ʿAbd does not know what occurred after him; if he were brought to me"
"17085","(17079) And from Sufyān, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \If he were brought to me"
"17086","(17080) And it was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who narrated to me ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī, who narrated to us Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn, who narrated to us Ādam, who narrated to us Shuʿbah, who narrated to us Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Ḥujayyah ibn ʿAdī al-Kindī say: A woman came to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \My husband has come to my slave-girl.\"" ʿAlī"
"17087","(17081) It was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād, who narrated to us Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār, who narrated to us al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān, who narrated to us Ibn Numayr, from ʿUbaydullāh — meaning Ibn ʿUmar — from Nāfiʿ, who said: A woman gifted a slave-girl to her husband. He took her on a journey and had intercourse with her, and she became pregnant. When her wife learned of her pregnancy, she went to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \I sent a slave-girl with my husband to serve him and attend to him"
"17088","(17082) It was narrated to us by Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī, who narrated to us Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī, who narrated to us Sufyān al-Jawharī, who narrated to us ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan, who narrated to us ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd, who narrated to us Sufyān, from al-Mughīrah, from al-Haytham ibn Badr, from ʿIrqūṣ al-Ḍabbī, that a woman came to ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \My husband has come to my slave-girl.\"" Her husband said: \""She speaks the truth"
"17089","(17083) And it was narrated to us by Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī, who narrated to us Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, who narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād, who narrated to us my father, who narrated to us ʿAbd al-Razzāq, who narrated to us Maʿmar, from Simāk ibn al-Faḍl, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, was presented with a man who had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl. He flogged him one hundred lashes and did not stone him. This is a disconnected (munqaṭiʿ) narration. (Qāla:) And it is as though, if it is authentic, he claimed ignorance, so he subjected him to taʿzīr and did not stone him. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"17090","(17084) It was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād, who narrated to us Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār, who narrated to us Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī, who narrated to us Musaddad, who narrated to us Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ, who narrated to us Sulaymān al-Taymī, from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, from Ibn Masʿʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man kissed a woman, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the verse was revealed: \And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the approaches of the night. Indeed"
"17091","(17085) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr informed me; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) He said: And Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us; both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ informed us from Simāk, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said:\n\nA man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allāh"
"17092","(17086) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Ḥusayn ibn Ḥasan and Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; both said: ʿĪsā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that he heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ say:\n\n\When the slave-girl of one of you commits zinā and her zinā becomes evident"
"17093","(17087) ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, and Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated it from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-ʿAnbas narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us; al-Ḥumaydī informed us; Sufyān narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Mūsā narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāʾ informed us; Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with the meaning of the ḥadīth of al-Layth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the various routes we have mentioned.\n\nIsmāʿīl ibn Umayyah likewise narrated it from Saʿīd, from Abū Hurayrah."
"17094","(17088) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik ibn Anas informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; Ibn Qaʿnab and Ibn Bukayr narrated to us from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Abū Hurayrah, and from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, that:\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh ﷺ was asked about the slave-girl who commits zinā while not being in a state of iḥṣān (marital chastity). He said: \If she commits zinā"
"17095","(17089) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānī al-ʿAdl informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, that Sulaymān ibn Yasār informed him that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah al-Makhzūmī said:\n\nʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) commanded me regarding a group of young Qurayshī men, so we flogged slave-girls from among the slave-girls of the governorship, fifty lashes each, for zinā. [Ḥasan]"
"17096","(17090) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharzah narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Qādim narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Salām informed us from al-Suddī, from ʿAbd Khayr, from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said:\n\n\When your slave-girls commit zinā"
"17097","(17091) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated to us from al-Suddī, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, who said:\n\nʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) delivered a sermon and said: \O people"
"17098","(17092) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī informed us from Abī Ḥabībah, who said:\n\nI came to ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) and said to him: \I have committed a grave sin—establish the prescribed punishment upon me.\"" He turned me away four times"
"17099","(17093) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām ibn al-Ḥārith, from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥīl, that Maʿqil ibn Muqarrin came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd and said:\n\n\My slave stole a cloak from my other slave.\"" He said: \""Some of your property stole from some of your property.\"" He said: \""I believe he mentioned that my slave-girl committed zinā.\"" He said: \""Flog her.\"" He said: \""She has not been married (iḥṣān).\"" He said: \""Her Islam is her iḥṣān.\""\n\nḤammād ibn Zayd also narrated it from Manṣūr"
"17100","(17094) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Harawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; Dāwūd—who is Ibn Abī Hind—informed us; Thumāmah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Anas narrated to us, who said:\n\nI witnessed Anas ibn Mālik flogging his slave-girls the prescribed punishment when they committed zinā, whether they had been married or had not been married. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"17101","(17095) Abū Naṣr informed us, Abū Manṣūr informed us, Aḥmad informed us, Saʿīd informed us, Abū ʿĀwānah narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Sālim from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \The iḥṣān (condition triggering the hadd) of a slave woman is her entry into Islam and her affirmation thereof. If she enters Islam and affirms it"
"17102","(17096) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik narrated from Nāʿif that a slave who was in charge of the slaves of the khums (one-fifth share) coerced a slave girl from among those slaves and had intercourse with her. ʿUmar flogged him and banished him, but he did not flog the slave girl because he had coerced her. [Ḍaʿīf]\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Mundhir, the author of the al-Khilāfiyyāt, narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar that he imposed the hadd upon his slave woman for zinā and banished her to Fadak. It has also been narrated to us from Ḥammād from Ibrāhīm that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding an umm walad who committed zinā: \She is to be flogged"
"17103","(17097) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us, Ibn Abī Uways informed us, Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: \If a male slave or a female slave commits zinā"
"17104","(17098) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī, and Mūsā ibn Muḥammad said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us. He said: I read to Mālik from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about the slave woman who commits zinā but has not been muḥṣanat (i.e., married). He said: \If she commits zinā"
"17105","(17099) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated from Mālik, and he mentioned it with its chain, similar to it, except that he said: from Abū Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī. He added, and said: \Then if she commits zinā"
"17106","(17100) And Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it, as Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us orally; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb informed us; Sufyān narrated.\n\n(H) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us.\n\n(H) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; al-Ḥumaydī informed us; Sufyān informed us; al-Zuhrī informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah informed me from Abū Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī and Shibl, who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he was asked about the slave woman who commits zinā.\"" And he mentioned something similar"
"17107","(17101) The ḥadīth of Shibl is only as Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Ṣāliḥ and Ibn Bukayr said: al-Layth informed us; ʿUqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihāb; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah informed me from Shibl ibn Khulayd al-Muzanī from Mālik ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Awsī from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said regarding the slave woman: \If she commits zinā"
"17108","(17102) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Sufyān informed us from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \If the slave woman of one of you commits zinā and her zinā becomes evident"
"17109","(17103) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqrīʾ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If the slave woman of one of you commits zinā"
"17110","(17104) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us; Isrāʾīl narrated from al-Suddī from Saʿīd ibn ʿUbaydah from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) addressed us and said: \O people"
"17111","(17105) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf — informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī — informed us; al-Ḥasan al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us; ʿAffān — narrated to us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʀĀmir — from Abū Jamīlah — from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) was informed of a slave woman who had committed fornication, so he said: \Carry out the ḥadd on her.\"" So I went and found that her blood had not yet dried"
"17112","(17106) He said: And al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAlī narrated to us; Sharīk narrated to us — from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā and ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Jamīlah — from Abū Jamīlah — from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A slave woman belonging to one of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave birth, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Carry out the ḥadd on her.\"" And he mentioned something similar to it.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us previously from al-Thawrī"
"17113","(17107) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī — informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — informed us; al-Shāfiʿī — informed us; Sufyān — from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār — from al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī, that Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), carried out the ḥadd on a slave woman of hers who had committed fornication. [Weak]"
"17114","(17108) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib — informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ — informed us; Saʿīd — from Thumāmah ibn Anas, that Anas ibn Mālik, when his slave committed fornication, would command some of his sons to carry out the ḥadd on him. [Weak]"
"17115","(17109) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh — informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān — narrated to us; Abū al-Azhar — narrated to us; Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah — narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj — informed me; Ibn Abī Mulaykah — from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar — from his father, that he carried out the ḥadd on a slave woman of his who had committed fornication, and he said to the one who was to flog her: \Below her feet"
"17116","(17110) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad — narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh — narrated to us; my father — narrated to us; Shuʿbah — from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Saʿīd ibn Jubayr say: \If a slave woman commits fornication"
"17117","(17111) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah; Abū al-Walīd — narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān — narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām — from Ashʿath — from his father, who said: I witnessed Abū Barzah flogging a slave woman of his who had committed fornication. [Sound]"
"17118","(17112) He said: And Abū Bakr narrated to us — from Sufyān — from Abū al-Zinād — from Khārijah ibn Zayd — from Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), that he carried out the ḥadd on a slave woman of his."
"17119","(17113) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ — informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī — narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways — narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād — from his father — from the fuqahāʾ whose opinion is referred to among the people of Madīnah, who used to say: \It is not permissible for anyone to carry out any of the ḥadd punishments without the authority of the sulṭān"
"17120","(17114) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah — informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us; Abū ʿAānah — from Mughīrah — from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, who both said: \When the People of the Book bring a case before the Muslim judges"
"17121","(17115) Abū Naṣr informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Hushaym informed us, al-ʿAwwām from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, regarding the statement of Allah, the Exalted: \So judge between them with justice\"" [al-Māʾidah: 42]"
"17122","(17116) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Abī Usāmah from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan, who said: \Leave the People of the Book and their judges to themselves. If they refer a matter to you"
"17123","(17117) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū ʿAwf ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Marzūq informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus informed us, Zuhayr informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed us, ʿAmr ibn Khālid informed us, Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ with a man and a woman from among them who had committed zinā (unlawful sexual intercourse). He said: \What do you do with the one among you who commits zinā?\"" They said: \""We strike them and blacken their faces with our hands.\"" He said: \""What do you find in the Torah?\"" They said: \""We find nothing in it.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām said: \""You have lied! The Torah contains the ruling of stoning. Bring the Torah and recite it"
"17124","(17118) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah from al-Aʿmash from ʿAbdullāh ibn Murrah from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: A blackened and flogged Jew was brought past the Prophet ﷺ. He called them and said: \Is this how you find the punishment for the adulterer in your Book?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He then called one of their scholars and said: \""I adjure you by Allah"
"17125","(17119) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: al-Zuhrī informed me, who said: I heard a man from Muzaynah narrating to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib that Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, informed them that the Jewish rabbis gathered in the Bayt al-Madras when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madīnah, and a married man from among them had committed zinā with a Jewish woman who was also married. They said: \Take this man and this woman to Muḥammad and ask him what the ruling concerning them is"
"17126","(17120) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Yaḥyā Abū al-Aṣbaʿ al-Ḥarrānī informed me, Muḥammad ibn Salamah from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from al-Zuhrī, who said: I heard a man from Muzaynah narrating to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from Abī Hurayrah, who said: A man and a woman from the Jews committed zinā, both having been married, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madīnah. Stoning had been prescribed for them in the Torah, but they had abandoned it and adopted the practice of blackening—being struck one hundred times with a rope smeared with pitch, then carried on a donkey with the face turned toward the rear of the donkey. A group of their rabbis gathered and sent another group to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \Ask him about the punishment for the adulterer.\""\n\nHe said: And he narrated the hadith. In it he said: \""They were not of his religion that he should judge between them"
"17127","(17121) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Wakīʿ narrated to us from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Simāk from Qābūs ibn Mukhāriq that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr wrote to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, asking him about a Muslim who committed zinā with a Christian woman. He wrote back to him: \Carry out the ḥadd on the Muslim and return the Christian woman to the people of her religion.\""\n\n[Ḥasan]\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""If this is established with you"
"17128","(17122) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Sufyān from ʿAmr, who heard Bajālah say: I was a scribe for Jazī ibn Muʿāwiyah, the paternal uncle of al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays. A letter from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, reached us one year before his death: \Kill every male and female sorcerer"
"17129","(17123) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: I said to him: \Bajālah is an unknown man"
"17130","(17124) And what I intend is what Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Isḥāq al-Azraq informed us, from al-Aʿrābī, who said: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz wrote to ʿAdī ibn Arṭāʾah: \To proceed: ask al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ḥasan what prevented those Imāms who came before us from intervening between the Magians and the women they marry whom no one among the People of the Book other than them marries.\"" So ʿAdī asked al-Ḥasan"
"17131","(17125) Imam Abū al-Ṭayyib: Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Ṣaʿlūkī informed us orally, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and others said: Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn from al-Ḥakam from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Two verses were abrogated from this Sūrah"
"17132","(17126) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated from Sufyān from al-Suddī from ʿIkrimah regarding {So judge between them or turn away from them} [al-Māʾidah 42]. He said: \This verse abrogated it: {And judge between them by what Allah has revealed and do not follow their desires} [al-Māʾidah 49].\"""""
"17133","(17127) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \How do you ask the People of the Book about anything"
"17134","(17128) Abū Bakr: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in Baghdād; Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Uwaysī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Thawr ibn Zayd from Abī al-Ghayth from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Avoid the seven destructive sins.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"
"17135","(17129) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us orally; Abū al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Sakan and Hishām ibn ʿAlī said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated from Abī Saʿīd, the freed slave of ʿĀmir ibn Kurayz, from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not envy one another"
"17136","(17130) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Fuḍayl ibn Ghazwān informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Yaʿlā informed us; Abū Khaythamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf narrated from Fuḍayl ibn Ghazwān from Ibn Abī Nuʿm from Abū Hurayrah: \I heard the Prophet of Repentance"
"17137","(17131) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm narrated to me from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Asʿad ibn Zurārah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the story by which my innocence was revealed to the people"
"17138","(17132) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Nufaylī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq with this ḥadīth, but he did not mention ʿĀʾishah. He said: \He ordered that two men and a woman from those who had spoken of the slander be given their ḥadd punishment"
"17139","(17133) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān narrated, and I heard him say: \I heard some people of knowledge say: 'The companions of al-Ifk were flogged with the ḥadd punishment"
"17140","(17134) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us; Hishām ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; al-Qāsim, the brother of Khallād's paternal uncle, narrated from Khallād ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab that he heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: \While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was addressing the people"
"17141","(17135) Abū Sa'd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn 'Adiyy informed us; Ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Hishām ibn 'Ammār narrated to us; Muslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī narrated to us; 'Abbād ibn Isḥāq narrated from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \So-and-so woman has committed adultery with me\"" — and he named her. The Prophet ﷺ sent for her"
"17142","(17136) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; 'Abdullāh ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Ya'qūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Nu'aym narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Salamah ibn al-Muḥabbq al-Ḥanafī, who said: I said to a man, \O you who does such-and-such to his mother!\"" He brought me before Abū Hurayrah"
"17143","(17137) And Shu'bah narrated from Abū Maymūnah, who said: I arrived in Madīnah. Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb say: I heard al-'Abbās ibn Muḥammad say: 'Uthmān ibn 'Umar ibn Fāris narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Abū Maymūnah, who said: I arrived in Madīnah, so I dismounted from my mount and hobbled it. I entered the mosque, and a man came and began to untie its hobble. I said to him, \O you who does such-and-such to your mother!\"" He said: So he brought me before Abū Hurayrah. He said: He flogged me eighty lashes. He said: Then I began to recite:\n\n\""If only you could see me the day I am flogged standing"
"17144","(17138) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffā' informed us; 'Uthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: Whoever says to a man, \O Lūṭī"
"17145","(17139) Abū Aḥmad 'Abdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī al-'Adl informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-'Abdī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Abī al-Zinād that he said: 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz — may Allah have mercy on him — flogged a slave eighty lashes for a false accusation of fornication (qadhf).\n\nAbū al-Zinād said: I asked 'Abdullāh ibn 'Āmir ibn Rabī'ah about that, and he said: I lived during the time of 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and 'Uthmān ibn 'Affān — may Allah be pleased with them both — and the Caliphs after them, one after another. I never saw any of them flog a slave for a false accusation of fornication more than forty lashes. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"17146","(17140) Al-Thawrī narrated it from 'Abdullāh ibn Dhakwān, Abī al-Zinād: 'Abdullāh ibn 'Āmir ibn Rabī'ah narrated to me, saying: I lived during the time of Abū Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthmān — may Allah be pleased with them — and those Caliphs after them, and I never saw them strike a slave for qadhf except forty lashes. Abū Bakr al-Ardastānī informed us; Abū Naṣr al-'Irāqī narrated to us; Sufyān al-Jawharī narrated to us; 'Alī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; 'Abdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated it. And Sufyān narrated to us: Ja'far narrated from his father that 'Alī — may Allah be pleased with him — used not to strike a slave who accused a free man of fornication except forty lashes. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"17147","(17141) By way of evidence, Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Asfaṭī narrated to us; Ismā'īl — that is, Ibn Abī Uways — narrated from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sa'īd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayyah: that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \My wife has given birth to a black boy.\"" He said: \""Do you have camels?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""What are their colours?\"" He said: \""Red.\"" He said: \""Is there a grey one among them?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""How is that?\"" He said: \""Perhaps a vein has drawn it out.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Perhaps your son has had a vein draw it out.\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Asfaṭī's ḥadīth. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismā'īl ibn Abī Uways. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"17148","(17142) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — dictating — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; al-Zuhrī narrated to us; Sa'īd ibn al-Musayyab informed me, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin from Banī Fazārah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \O Messenger of Allah"
"17149","(17143) Abū 'Amr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismā'īlī informed us; Abū Ya'lā narrated to us; Hārūn ibn Ma'rūf narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Abī al-Zinād, from al-A'raj, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Are you not astonished at how Allah turns away from me the curses and insults of Quraysh? They insult 'Mudhammam' and they curse 'Mudhammam"
"17150","(17144) Abū Muḥammad 'Abdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — may Allah have mercy on him — informed us; Abū Sa'īd ibn al-A'rābī narrated to us; Sa'dān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Mas'ūdī, from al-Qāsim ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān, who said: 'Abdullāh ibn Mas'ūd said: There is no flogging (ḥadd) except in two cases: a man accuses a chaste woman of fornication, or a man denies his father's lineage. [Da'īf]"
"17151","(17145) 'Abdullāh informed us; Abū Sa'īd informed us; Sa'dān informed us; Sufyān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, who said: \We did not consider flogging to be warranted except in the case of explicit slander (qadhf) or explicit denial of paternity (nafy).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Qāsim]"""
"17152","(17146) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah and the jurist Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ma'rūf informed us, saying: Abū 'Amr ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī informed us; Abū Muslim informed us; Abū 'Āṣim narrated from Ibn Abī Dhi'b from Ibn Shihāb from Sālim from Ibn 'Umar, that 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to impose the prescribed punishment (ḥadd) even in cases of allusive speech (ta'rīḍ). [Ḥasan]"
"17153","(17147) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik narrated from Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān, Abū al-Rijāl, from his mother 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Raḥmān, that two men exchanged insults during the time of 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and one of them said to the other: \My father is not an adulterer"
"17154","(17148) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us; Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abdullāh al-Harawī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ismā'īl ibn Abī Fudayk informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ismā'īl al-Ashhalī informed us; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn narrated from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If a man says to another man"
"17155","(17149) Abū Ḥāziṃ al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Sa'īd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Abū 'Awānah narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr from his companions from 'Alī (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding a man who says to another man: \O wicked one! O transgressor!\"" He said: \""There is no fixed prescribed punishment (ḥadd) upon him; rather the authority (wālī) may punish him (yu'azziruhu) at his discretion.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""
"17156","(17150) Abū 'Amr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn al-Ghiṭrīf informed us; Abū Ya'lā informed us; 'Ubaydullāh al-Qawārīrī informed us; Abū 'Awānah narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr from a shaykh from the people of Kūfah, who said: I heard 'Alī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \You asked me about a man who says to another man"
"17157","(17151) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-'Adl in Baghdād informed us; Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Sa'dān ibn Naṣr informed us; Mu'ādh ibn Mu'ādh narrated from Awf al-A'rābī from Abū Rajā' al-'Uṭāridī, who said: \'Umar and 'Uthmān (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to punish for satirical verse (hijā').\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"17158","(17152) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Shāfi'ī informed us; Abū Ismā'īl — Muḥammad ibn Ismā'īl — informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Qutaylah informed us; 'Abd al-'Azīz ibn Muḥammad informed me; 'Abd al-Wāḥid ibn Abī 'Awn narrated from Ibn Shihāb from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad and from 'Ubaydullāh ibn 'Abdullāh, who both narrated to him that 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to flog those who fabricated lies against the women of the people of the faith (ahl al-millah). This hadith is munqaṭi' (disconnected). If it is established, it is understood to refer to discretionary punishment (ta'zīr). And Allah knows best. [Ḍa'īf]"
"17159","(17153) Abū al-Ḥasan — Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Ma'rūf — informed us; Abū Sahl — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Jumān al-Rāzī — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Musaddad informed us; Ḥafṣ narrated from Ash'ath from al-Ḥasan, that a man said to another man: \You do not approach your wife except through adultery or what is unlawful.\"" This was brought to 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"
"17160","(17154) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Bazzāz informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Za'farānī informed us; Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdullāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Ja'far Muḥammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzāz informed us; Aḥmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār informed us; Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated from al-A'mash from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \May Allah curse the thief who steals an egg and has his hand cut off"
"17161","(17155) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Faqīh in Bukhārā informed me: Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Quraysh were greatly troubled by the matter of a woman of Banū Makhzūm who had stolen. They said: \Who will speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning her?\"" They said: \""Who would dare to do so except Usāmah ibn Zayd"
"17162","(17156) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī informed us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The hand is cut off for a quarter of a dīnār and above.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"17163","(17157) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us: it was recited to Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram al-Baṣrī in Baghdād: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sulaymān ibn Kathīr and Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us: al-Zuhrī narrated to us, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The cutting off is for a quarter of a dīnār and above.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"17164","(17158) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its like.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Yazīd ibn Hārūn.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: Maʿmar followed it up from al-Zuhrī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"
"17165","(17159) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us by dictation: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The hand of the thief is cut off for a quarter of a dīnār and above.\"""""
"17166","(17160) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Shaybān al-Ramlī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The cutting off is for a quarter of a dīnār and above.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Shāfiʿī. And in the narration of al-Ramlī: \""He used to cut off for a quarter of a dīnār and above.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"17167","(17161) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Ḥarmalah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ibn al-Sarḥ narrated to us. They both said: Ibn Wahb informed us: Yūnus informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah and ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The hand of the thief is cut off for a quarter of a dīnār and above.\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn al-Sarḥ. And in the narration of Ḥarmalah"
"17168","(17162) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Muqrī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Hād, from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad, from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \The hand of a thief is not cut off except for a quarter of a dīnār and above.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"17169","(17163) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Zurʿah al-Dimashqī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Khālid narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, who said: A Nabataean who had stolen was brought to me, so ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān sent word to me: \O my son"
"17170","(17164) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā al-Ghassānī, who said: I came to Madīnah and met Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, who was the governor over Madīnah. He said: \A thief from among your people"
"17171","(17165) Abū ʿAmr al-Bisṭāmī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; Abū Yaʿlā informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; ʿAbdah and Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Ibn Numayr informed us; Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \A thief's hand was not cut off during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ) for less than the price of a shield — a ḥajafah or a turs — and both of those had value.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Numayr.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī and Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah"
"17172","(17166) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; Yūsuf ibn Mūsā informed us; Jarīr, Wakīʿ, and Ibn Idrīs informed us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father: \The hand of a thief was not cut off during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for less than the price of a ḥajafah or a turs"
"17173","(17167) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; al-Ḥasan — he is Ibn Sufyān — and al-Qāsim — he is Ibn Zakariyyā — both said: Hārūn ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAbdah informed us, from Hishām: \A man stole a bowl and it was brought to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. Hishām said: My father said: 'The hand is not cut off for something trivial.' Then he said: ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated to me that a hand was not cut off during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for less than the price of a shield — a ḥajafah or a turs.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"17174","(17168) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad, Mūsā ibn Muḥammad, and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cut off the hand of a thief for a shield valued at three dirhams.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways"
"17175","(17169) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr and Abū al-Azhar both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah informed me that Nāfiʿ informed him that Ibn ʿUmar informed them: \The Prophet (ﷺ) cut off the hand of a man who stole a shield from the women's terrace"
"17176","(17170) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Bukayr ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥaddād in Makkah informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us. Both said: Abū Nuʿaym informed us; Sufyān informed us, from Ayyūb, Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah, ʿUbayd Allāh, and Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: \The Prophet (ﷺ) cut off the hand for a shield valued at three dirhams.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dārimī"
"17177","(17171) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿd informed us; my uncle informed us; my father informed us; Ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb informed me that Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ashajj informed him that Sulaymān ibn Yasār informed him that ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed him that she heard ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The thief's hand is not cut off for less than the price of a shield.\"" It was said to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): \""What is the price of a shield?\"" She said: \""A quarter of a dīnār.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"17178","(17172) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr informed us; ʿAbd al-Ghaffār ibn Dāwūd informed us; Ibn Lahīʿah informed us; Abū al-Naḍr informed us, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The hand of the thief is not cut off except for the price of a shield or more.\"" ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I said to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): \""And what was the price of a shield at that time?\"" She said: \""A quarter of a dīnār.\"" And the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah from the Prophet (ﷺ) — the cutting off for a quarter of a dīnār — and the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (ﷺ) — that he cut off the hand for a shield valued at three dirhams.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: These two are in agreement"
"17179","(17173) As for the ḥadīth: Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The price of a shield during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was valued at ten dirhams.\""\n\nThus narrated Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār"
"17180","(17174) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed it to us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ibn Rustah informed us; Abū Kāmil informed us; Abū ʿAwānah informed us, from Manṣūr, from al-Ḥakam, from ʿAṭāʾ and Mujāhid, from Ayman, who said: \It was said: 'The thief's hand is not cut off except for the price of a shield or more.'\"" He said: \""And the price of a shield at that time was a dīnār.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: Shaybān followed him"
"17181","(17175) And al-Shāfiʿī responded regarding it, as Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, he said: al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I said to some people, \This is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — that the hand be cut for a quarter dīnār and above. So how do you say that the hand is not cut except for ten dirhams and above? What is your evidence for that?\"" He said"
"17182","(17176) It is as Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Malik, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ayman, the freed slave of Ibn al-Zubayr, from Tubyiʿ, from Kaʿb, who said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ and perfects the wuḍūʾ"
"17183","(17177) As for the hadith which Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us, Abū Yaʿlā informed us, Ibn Numayr informed us, my father narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: \The price of the shield (mijann) in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ten dirhams.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"17184","(17178) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, he said: al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \This is an opinion of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr in the narration of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb. The shields (majān)"
"17185","(17179) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq and Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān said: Sahl informed us, Wuhib narrated to us, from Abū Wāqid, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd, from his father: \That the Prophet ﷺ cut the hand for a shield (mijann) whose price was five dirhams.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"17186","(17180) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ʿAbdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us, Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us, al-Anṣārī informed us, Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated to me, he said: \Qatādah asked Anas ibn Mālik"
"17187","(17181) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah be pleased with him, informed us, Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us, from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, who said: \I heard Qatādah asking Anas ibn Mālik about cutting (the hand)"
"17188","(17182) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed me, ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad informed us, Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī informed us, from Sufyān, from Shuʿbah, from Qatādah, from Anas, who said: \Abū Bakr"
"17189","(17183) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr informed us, Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Anas: \That a man stole a shield (mijann) in the time of the Prophet ﷺ"
"17190","(17184) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar Mushkadānah informed us, ʿUbaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from Anas: \That the Prophet ﷺ cut the hand for a shield (mijann) of the price of five dirhams"
"17191","(17185) And the preserved narration from the ḥadīth of Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, as Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — he narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us — Saʿīd, who is Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, that Abū Bakr (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) amputated the hand in a shield (mijann) whose value was five dirhams or four dirhams. Saʿīd was uncertain. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"17192","(17186) And Abū al-Khayr Jāmiʿ ibn Aḥmad al-Wakīl informed us — Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Abū Hilāl informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us — Abū Yaʿlā and Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad said — Shaybān narrated to us — Abū Hilāl, from Qatādah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) amputated the hand in a shield (mijann). I asked: \What was its worth?\"" He replied: \""Five dirhams.\""\n\nThis is the wording of Shaybān's ḥadīth. In the narration of Mūsā"
"17193","(17187) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Abū Muslim narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us — Abū Hilāl, from Qatādah, from Anas, that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) amputated the hand in a shield worth five dirhams or four dirhams. I met Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, and he said: \It is from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu).\"" I met Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbdillāh"
"17194","(17188) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed him — al-Shāfiʿī informed him — Mālik, from ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Ḥazm, from his father, from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that a thief stole a citron (utrujjah) during the caliphate of ʿUthmān (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu). ʿUthmān ordered that it be appraised, and it was valued at three dirhams at the exchange rate of twelve dirhams to one dīnār. So he amputated his hand. Mālik said: \It is the citron that people eat.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"17195","(17189) And Abū Zakariyyā informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed me — more than one narrator, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), who said: \Amputation is in a quarter dīnār and above.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"17196","(17190) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us — Abū Khalīfah narrated to us — al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) amputated the hand of a thief in an iron egg (bayḍah) worth a quarter dīnār. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"17197","(17191) As for the athār which Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us — Sufyān, from ʿAṭiyyah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Thaqafī, who said: \Al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me"
"17198","(17192) The Shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ al-Sharīf informed us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Sharīḥ narrated to us — Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us — al-Masʿūdī, from al-Qāsim, who said: \ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said: 'The hand is not amputated except for a dīnār or ten dirhams.' Both of these are equivalent.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"17199","(17193) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: \Al-Shāfiʿī said: 'Some of the people have narrated our statement from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu).'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""I said: 'Al-Zāfirī narrated it from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu).' And the companions of Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad have informed us from their father that ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) said: 'Amputation is in a quarter dīnār and above.' And the ḥadīth of Jaʿfar from ʿAlī is more deserving of being established than the ḥadīth of al-Zāfirī.\""\n\nHe said: \""We have narrated from Ibn Masʿūd (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) that he said: 'The hand is not amputated except for ten dirhams.'\""\n\nWe said: \""Al-Thawrī narrated from ʿĪsā ibn Abī ʿAzza from al-Shaʿbī from Ibn Masʿūd that the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) amputated a thief's hand for five dirhams. This is more likely to be correct from ʿAbdullāh than the ḥadīth of al-Masʿūdī from al-Qāsim from ʿAbdullāh.\""\n\nHe said: \""How did you not adopt this?\"" We said: \""This ḥadīth does not contradict our ḥadīth. If he amputated for three dirhams"
"17200","(17194) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed him — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — ʿUmar ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Marwān narrated to us — my father narrated to me — ʿĀṣim, I think he was Ibn ʿUmar, narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn al-Yasaʿ narrated to us — Juwaybir, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk, from al-Nazzāl, from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), who said: \The hand is not amputated except for ten dirhams"
"17201","(17195) And that which has been narrated in opposition to it is not weaker than it. It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani, who was informed by Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan, who was informed by Abu Ya'la, who narrated to us Abu Khaythamah, who narrated to us Ibn Mahdi, from Sufyan, from 'Isa ibn Abi 'Azzah, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Abd Allah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) cut off the hand for a shield valued at five dirhams.\n\nAs for the hadith of 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), we have previously mentioned its discontinuity, in that it was narrated from him only by al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, and he did not meet any of the Companions. And we have narrated previously from Abu Bakr and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding cutting off the hand for five dirhams. [Da'if]"
"17202","(17196) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr al-Isbahani, who both said: It was informed to us by 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Makhlad, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Harun al-Fallas, who was a hafiz, who narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, who narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Idris, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Five are not cut off except for five.\"" And it was narrated by Mansur ibn Zadhan"
"17203","(17197) It was informed to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, and Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Hamid al-Muqri', and Abu Sadiq al-'Attar, who all said: It was narrated to us by Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Mukram, who narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, who informed us Shu'bah, from Dawud ibn Farahij, that he heard Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri both saying: \The cutting off (of the hand) is for four dirhams and above.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is possible that they said this at the time when the exchange rate of a quarter dinar became four dirhams.\n\nAnd likewise what has been narrated to us from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and from others regarding the five — it is possible that this was at the time of a change in the exchange rate. And the original basis for the nisab is a quarter dinar"
"17204","(17198) It was informed to us by Abu Ahmad al-Mihranjani, who was informed by Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki, who was informed by Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi, who narrated to us Ibn Bukayr, who narrated to us Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, that 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), said: \I have not forgotten"
"17205","(17199) It was informed to us by Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, who narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm, who informed us al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman, who informed us al-Shafi'i, who informed us Malik.\n\n(And it was also informed to us by Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, who was informed by Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, who narrated to us Ibn Bukayr, who narrated to us Malik, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman) that a thief stole during the time of 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) a citron (utrujjah), and 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered that it be appraised. It was appraised at three dirhams at the exchange rate of twelve dirhams to a dinar, and so 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) cut off his hand.\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Bukayr. Al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) added in his narration that he said: Malik said: \It is the citron (utrujjah) that people eat.\"""""
"17206","(17200) It was informed to us by Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri', who informed us al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who narrated to us Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi, who narrated to us Musaddad, who narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, that a slave boy of his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban stole a young palm tree (wadiyy) from a neighbor's land and planted it in his own land. The matter was raised to Marwan ibn al-Hakam, who ordered that his hand be cut off. His patron came to Rafi' ibn Khadij and mentioned that to him, and he said: \There is no cutting off (of the hand) for him.\"" He said to him: \""Come with me to Marwan.\"" So he brought him and he narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""There is no cutting off (of the hand) for fruit or kathar (unripe dates on the palm).\"" [Sahih]"""
"17207","(17201) And it was informed to us by Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari, who informed us Abu Bakr ibn Dasah, who narrated to us Abu Dawud, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd, who narrated to us Hammad, who narrated to us Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, with this hadith, and he said: \So Marwan flogged him several times and then released him.\"" [Sahih]"""
"17208","(17202) It was informed to us by Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri', who informed us al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who narrated to us Yusuf ibn Ya'qub, who narrated to us Abu al-Rabi', who narrated to us Abu Shihab, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no cutting off (of the hand) for fruit or kathar.\"" Yahya said: \""Al-thamr (fruit) is that which is atop the palm tree"
"17209","(17203) It was informed to us by Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr, who all said: It was narrated to us by Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who informed us al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman, who informed us al-Shafi'i (may Allah be pleased with him), who informed us Ibn 'Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There is no cutting off (of the hand) for fruit or kathar.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Abu Sa'id. Abu Sa'id added in his narration.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: \""And we say the same — there is no cutting off (of the hand) for hanging fruit"
"17210","(17204) That is, what was informed to us by Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, who narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who informed us al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman, who informed us al-Shafi'i, who informed us Malik, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he said: \There is no cutting off (of the hand) for hanging fruit. But when it is stored in the jarin (harvest enclosure)"
"17211","(17205) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Abū ʿAwānah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Akḥnas from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \At what value is the hand cut off?\"" He said: \""The hand is not cut off for fruit hanging on the tree. But when it is gathered into the drying place"
"17212","(17206) Abū Ḥāzim and Abū Naṣr informed us, saying: Abū al-Faḍl informed us; Aḥmad informed us; Saʿīd narrated to us; Faraj ibn Faḍālah narrated from Luqmān ibn ʿĀmir from Abū al-Dardāʾ, who said: \There is no cutting off of the hand for one who steals a pigeon.\""\n\nAnd this refers specifically to birds and pigeons that are not kept in an enclosure. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"17213","(17207) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī and Yaʿqūb al-Dawraqī both said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uḥud while I was fourteen years of age"
"17214","(17208) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Ibn Idrīs narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar. Nāfiʿ said: \I narrated this hadith to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"
"17215","(17209) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Misʿar narrated from al-Qāsim, who said: \A slave girl who had stolen and had not yet menstruated was brought to ʿAbd Allāh"
"17216","(17210) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abū Ẓabyān from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \A mad woman who had committed fornication was brought to ʿUmar"
"17217","(17211) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mihrān from Abū Ẓabyān from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \ʿAlī"
"17218","(17212) ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated it from Abū Ẓabyān as a mursal, marfūʿ narration. Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Abū Ẓabyān, who said: \A woman who had committed fornication was brought to ʿUmar"
"17219","(17213) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Yūnus narrated from al-Ḥasan from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'The pen has been lifted from three: from the child until he attains discernment (ʿaql)"
"17220","(17214) He said: And Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated from Abū al-Ḍuḥā from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"17221","(17215) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Ṣafwān ibn ʿAbd Allāh that Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah was told: \Whoever does not emigrate is doomed.\"" So Ṣafwān came to Madīnah and slept in the mosque"
"17222","(17216) Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr from Ṭāwūs from the Prophet ﷺ, a hadith similar to that of Mālik. This mursal narration strengthens the first one, and it has been narrated through another chain. It was also narrated from Ibn Kāsib from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah with his chain, connected, mentioning Ibn ʿAbbās in it, but it is not authentic."
"17223","(17217) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī narrated to us: Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us: Bikkār ibn al-Khaṣīb narrated to us: Ḥabīb narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, who said: \While Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah was lying down in al-Baṭḥāʾ"
